The Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Singapore consider the short-lived relationship in the past as a nightmare (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On the occasion of his presence in Bangkok, Thailand to attend the 34th ASEAN Summit on On June 23, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Lee Hsien Loong, Prime Minister of Singapore, met at a luncheon at the end of the ASEAN Summit.
During the dialogue, the two leaders considered the resentment in relations caused by Li Xianlong's claim that Vietnam invaded Cambodia was a nightmare and that both sides were committed to maintaining ties and holding hands. Each moves forward. This is according to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, during the dialogue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke about the merits of Cambodia in recognizing Singapore's independence one day after the country declared independence in 1965 and claimed that Cambodia and Singapore Have a good relationship for a long time.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon stated that during the dialogue, both sides considered the past as a different point of view and one side could not change the other side's point of view. But both sides agreed to look forward and shake hands for the positive.
In late May 2019, Singapore Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong stated that Vietnam had invaded Cambodia in the 1980s. Such remarks provoked strong reactions from the top leaders of Cambodia and Vietnam, who considered them to be contrary to actual history and supported the Khmer Rouge regime.
Vivian stated that Singapore only wanted peace and prosperity for Cambodia, had no intention of supporting the Khmer Rouge and did not want to see the regime return to Cambodia. Let there be no doubt about this honesty.
