(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing Mr. Im Chhun Lim to continue as Chairman of the Constitutional Council for the eighth three-year term from 2019 to 2022. . This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News this morning, June 23, 2019.
Please be informed that on the morning of June 21, 2019, Mr. Im Chhun Lim was voted as the Chairman of the Constitutional Council by all 9 members of the Constitutional Council for the 8th mandate, which will last for 3 years from 2019 to 2022. .
The election was held in secret under the chairmanship of the oldest member of the Constitutional Council. After being elected as the new President of the Council, Mr. Im Chhun Lim committed to abide by the Constitution, the rules and regulations of the Constitutional Council and strive to fulfill the role of the Constitutional Council is to protect the constitutional monarchy. Build and protect the Kingdom of Cambodia to become the rule of law and development.
Mr. Im Chhun Lim is the former Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. Mr. Im Chhun was elected Chairman of the Constitutional Council for the seventh term in 2016.
