In addition, some funds were also provided to the families of the dead and injured due to the collapse of this building, including: the budget of the National Working Group and the Red Cross, the budget of the provincial hall, the budget of the prosecutor, the budget of the National Assembly and the budget of the National Assembly. Of the Ministry of Labor.
In total, the budget for the victims who died was 49 million Riels, of which the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to provide 40 million Riels by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 1 million Riels for the National Working Group, 1 million Red Cross. 2 million riels for the provincial hall, 500,000 riels for the prosecutor, 500,000 riels for the Sihanoukville MP and 4 million riels for the Ministry of Labor.
The injured received a total of 7,200,000 Riels per person, including the Royal Government of Cambodia 5 million Riels provided by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 1 million Riels for the National Working Group, 1 million Riels for the Red Cross. And the budget of the provincial hall 200,000 Riels.
