(Phnom Penh): Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, which has Chinese and Cambodian shareholders, has decided to standardize and is preparing for an IPO and listing on the Cambodia Securities Exchange. This is according to the press release of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, translated by officials of the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone will start preparing documents and procedures to become a listed company on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
According to the press release, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone intends to issue IPOs and list them on the Cambodia Securities Exchange to increase capital through the securities market, promote the development of high quality areas and contribute more to development. Economy of Cambodia.
In addition, through registration, all shareholders can achieve the success of the achievement and achieve a win-win strategy.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is located in Sihanoukville Province, located 12 km from Sihanoukville Deep Sea Port and only 3 km from Sihanoukville International Airport. The total area is 11.13 square kilometers.
