One day, the National Children's Hospital received more than 300 dengue patients, from the beginning of 2019 to June 20, there were more than 3,000 cases of dengue fever, 4 deaths
(Phnom Penh): Director of the National Children's Hospital, Dr. Nhep Angka Bos, said that one day, the National Children's Hospital received more than 300 dengue patients, and from the beginning of 2019 to June 20, children have dengue fever. More than 3,000 people were treated at the National Children's Hospital, four of whom died.
He added that most of the deaths were due to the parents leaving the child in a critical condition before being taken to the hospital, and that the child had other illnesses, such as blisters on the mouth, hands and feet, a disease that damages the lungs during dengue fever. It makes you very sick for a while.
Moreover, the doctor said that the Ministry of Health under the leadership of Minister Mam Bun Heng has taken great care and has already put in place measures to prevent cases and deaths from dengue fever, both equipment and medical training. Diagnose. In fact, today, the Minister visited the patient and sent an additional 80 beds to the National Children's Hospital.
At the same time, the Minister of Health also encouraged the medical team to make more efforts with high attention to save patients effectively and quickly from death.
