Samdech Tea Banh: Vietnam's support for Cambodia does not change at all
(Tbong Khmum): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said that from the past until now, Vietnam's support for Cambodia has not changed.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh's remarks were made on the occasion of Samdech leading the delegation of the Ministry of National Defense to celebrate the 42nd anniversary of the Day of Remembrance of the Journey to the Overthrow of the Genocidal Regime "Pol Pot" (June 20, 1977 - June 20, 2019) ) In Koh Thmor area, Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh stated: "The support of the Vietnamese friends to Cambodia from the past to the present has not changed at all, and there is nothing beyond the international obligations to save. "A country that has suffered so much."
Vietnam assisted Cambodia in cooperating with the Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation to liberate the Cambodian people from the 1979 Pol Pot genocidal regime. After that, on behalf of neighboring countries, Vietnam has continued to support Cambodia.
Despite repeated attacks on bilateral relations, Cambodia and Vietnam remain committed to strengthening and expanding closer cooperation.
On this occasion, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also reacted to the provocation that intended to cause divisions between Cambodia and Vietnam. "True history is not like what some people slander, causing divisions between Cambodia and Vietnam," he said. "Some unscrupulous people are following in the footsteps of those who slander true history," he said.
CDI Announces Outcome of Its Meeting on Establishment of International Center for Democrats International Research Institute
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of the Central Democrats International (CDI) from several continents and countries on June 20, 2019 held a meeting in Phnom Penh to establish the CDI Research Institute.
The second meeting of the CDI Research Institute Establishment Working Group was organized by the Cambodian People's Party to support the development of specific plans to strengthen the CDI Research Institute Initiative, which complements discussions on cooperation initiatives. And related issues.
The meeting unanimously decided to submit a proposal to the CDI Executive Committee to establish the CDI Research Institute for the benefit and needs of the CDI member parties. The main points of the meeting that led to the agreement to establish the CDI Research Institute can be clarified through:
* The great efforts and dedication of CDI member parties around the world to establish closer and deeper cooperation among members, researchers and policymakers through dialogue and exchange of experiences. And business skills, innovation and culture.
It should be noted that the meeting also reminded of the CDI Resolution, which requires the European Union to be fair to Cambodia, which was adopted on April 10, 2019 in Belgium.
