Minister of Agriculture Receives Research Team of the Project Management Unit to Support Agricultural Investment of the Supreme National Economic Council
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, on the afternoon of June 20, 2019, met with the research team of the Project Management Unit to support agricultural investment within the ASPIRE framework of the Supreme National Economic Council. Directed by Mr. Ros Silva.
The purpose of this consultation meeting is to learn more about the "Review of Agricultural Investment in Cambodia" and to evaluate the size of investment by the Royal Government, development partners and the private sector, investment policy models and strategies.
The Minister highly appreciated the time and goodwill of the National Economic Council, which intends to study and research more on agricultural investment in Cambodia at this time.
In response to the objectives of the Economic Council, the Minister informed the working group in detail about the progress from one stage to another in the field of agriculture, policies, environment, potential opportunities, challenges and mechanisms or procedures to solve both short and long term. : A long time that this sector has been experiencing.
In addition, the Minister also informed the guests about the current state of investment in the agricultural sector that the Ministry is trying to promote: processing and export by applying modern agricultural technology, implementation of contract farming, agribusiness refers to the production of products. Sanitary and phytosanitary quality meets the needs of the domestic and export markets.
He also added that in order for this policy to be more successful and sustainable, it requires full support and effective implementation cooperation with the private sector, development partners, agricultural communities and especially relevant institutions. Roles and responsibilities, all of which are important inputs to support investment in agriculture for development, both now and in the future.
