European Investment Bank provides $ 60 million in low-interest loans to Cambodia for Bak Kheng water plant project
(Belgium): Mr. Hem Vandy, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance, Representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia, signed a Concessional Loan Agreement (Low Interest Loan) amounting to US $ 60 million with a Legal Representative of the European Investment Bank. EIB) for the implementation of "Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Construction Project".
The ceremony took place at the EU headquarters in Brussels, Belgium.
A press release from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, obtained by Fresh News on June 20, 2019, states that the project will run for four years from 2019 to 2022 and aims to increase capacity. Production of additional clean water of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority in the amount of 195,000 cubic meters per day in 2022 in addition to the current production capacity of 560,000 cubic meters per day.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority is the implementing agent of the above project and a sub-borrower from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
