China and India have a combined population of 37 percent of the world's current population of 7.7 billion, of which China has more than 1.4 billion and India more than 1.3 billion. (Figures for 2018). But according to a report by the United Nations World Population Outlook 2019 released this week, by 2027, India will overtake China to become the world's most populous country.
In addition, between 2019 and 2050, the population in 55 countries or regions will decline by at least 1 percent due to lower living standards and increased migration. China's population will shrink by 2.2 percent, bringing the country's population to 1.1 billion, while India will grow to 1.5 billion, the report said. .
