(Phnom Penh): On June 20, 2019, it was the 42nd anniversary (June 20, 1977 - June 20, 2019) that 25-year-old Hun Sen, along with four other loyal fighters, decided in a dire situation. Tightly leave the land, leave your beloved wife and unborn child across the most dangerous border to Vietnam to seek support for the liberation of the nation and the Cambodian people from the cruel clutches of Pol Pot.
Please be informed that in 2017, the 40th anniversary of the national liberation struggle, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his surviving comrades traveled to all parts of the struggle to commemorate the bitter memories. That. Every point that Samdech passed through the place that reminded Samdech and the tears flowed was at the point of crossing the border under the tree.
At the beginning of this trip, before moving forward, Samdech Techo Hun Sen turned his face to the face of Cambodia and expressed his feelings to his wife and unborn child, not knowing whether the abduction will be reunited or not. . Especially miss the tragic fate of being separated from his parents at the age of 13 for education, until the age of 25 must be away from the land away from loved ones equal life because of the nation and people.
Starting from the great sacrifice of Hun Sen and his comrades 42 years ago, which is the greatest cause to bring the nation and the people of Cambodia to the light of progress and beauty as today.
Khmer historians see that without the beginning of the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and patriotic Khmer dignitaries to rise up to liberate the nation, the nation and the Cambodian people will have no chance of escaping the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. .
Even though I and the Cambodian people are now enjoying happiness, I will never forget the tens of thousands of tears when I stepped out of my homeland, leaving the suffering Cambodian people, especially my estranged wife. Sadly pregnant. I do not have a better choice because we can not ask for mercy from Pol Pot. It's dangerous choices and tears that bring happiness and prosperity to this day.
