Buhler International to bring advanced technology to develop Cambodian rice price chain and boost exports
(Phnom Penh): A representative of the world-class company Buhler, headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland, plans to invest in the construction of a state-of-the-art (silo) dryer in Cambodia to participate in the development of the rice price chain and to host Export finished products to the global market sustainably.
Mr. David Wang emphasized that Buhler's mission is to focus on using the latest technology to process products, build partnerships with consumers and strengthen production sustainability, and in Cambodia he plans to invest in 10 state-of-the-art drying facilities 10 that can store about 1 million tons of rice and can dry 13,000 tons of rice per day for processing into food products for export to international markets.
In response, Minister Pan Sosak expressed his satisfaction and appreciation for Buhler's investment projects that are in line with the Cambodia Integration Strategy (CTIS) and the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy (IDP) and the goals of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy. Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The minister expressed strong belief that when completed, the project will not only stabilize domestic agricultural prices, but also prevent the flow of rice to neighboring countries, improve farmers' livelihoods as well as economic development. Rural. In addition, all dryers will also provide significant benefits to the development of the national agribusiness sector, which will contribute to enhancing Cambodia's reputation on the international stage.
