Cambodian Customs and Japan Business Association vow to continue trade facilitation and improve business environment
Mr. Kun Nhim mentioned the sharp measures recently introduced by the Royal Government of Cambodia, including some measures related to customs.
In addition, he highlighted the reform and modernization program of the Cambodian Customs Administration, which has achieved remarkable achievements, including: the growing momentum of revenue collection, prevention and suppression of crime, governance in the customs unit and facilitation. Trade through automation and simplification of customs procedures as well.
He also mentioned the need to strengthen closer cooperation between the customs administration and the private sector to improve the business environment in Cambodia by adjusting procedures to meet the needs of the private sector.
On this occasion, the meeting monitored the progress of work related to the development process and preparation for the implementation of the second phase of the National Single System and the ASEAN Single System, which is scheduled to start in early July 2019, and the cooperation between the two countries. .C.R. and Camcontrol.
At the same time, the meeting also heard about the recent progress related to some important reform measures that the ECCC has introduced in line with the sharp reform program of the Royal Government of Cambodia, including the adjustment of customs procedures, reduction Scanner inspections, additional incentives for high-compliance companies, implementation of customs incentives for small and medium enterprises, and arrangements for customs clearance studies.
The dialogue then proceeded to discuss and resolve the nine issues and issues raised by JBAC related to the reduction of documents in paper form, the improvement of customs website functions, customs management, simplification of customs procedures and implementation. Special procedures for companies in special economic zones.
Of the nine proposals and issues, seven have been resolved, and one will be subject to further technical and legal review before being finalized, and another will be proposed at the inter-institutional level.
At the same time, the JICA representative also informed the meeting about its main assistance projects at present to the Royal Government of Cambodia: Master Project on Improving the Logistics System 2. Study to reduce congestion of goods and passengers on National Road No. 1, Bavet-Mok Bai border area and 3. Implementation of surveillance camera systems at major ports and border crossings.
The meeting appreciated the outcome of the third round of talks and noted that the dialogue mechanism was used as a model for dialogue between the JBAC and other government institutions.
