Kampong Chhnang Provincial Armed Forces Detain Two Journalists for Defamation and Extortion of Tea Vichet
(Kampong Chhnang): Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie arrested two journalists on charges of publishing defamatory articles and extorting about $ 2,800 from Tea Vichet.
The arrest took place on June 19, 2019 in a cafe located near the old Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police in Kandal Village, Sangkat Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang City.
The detained journalists include: Ngin Veasna, director of the Kraing Meas website, and Touch Din, 51, an associate of Ngin Veasna.
Lim Hak, a military police officer in Kampong Chhnang province, confirmed that the military police had arrested Ngin Veasna, the director of the Kraing Meas website, and a colleague, as the two suspects were charged with defamation and intimidation. Take the money according to the complaint of the lawyer of Tycoon Tea Vichet.
The Kampong Chhnang provincial military police official said that the arrest of Ngin Veasna and his associates after they wrote an article accusing Tycoon Tea Vichet of smuggling oil into Sihanoukville.
Regarding this publication, Tycoon Tea Vichet, through his lawyer, requested Mr. Ngin Veasna to re-interpret. However, the director of this broadcast did not publish, clarify or reinterpret. After there was no explanation, the police arrested him according to the complaint of the lawyer of Tycoon Tea Vichet.
Currently, the military police has built a case to send the two journalists to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court to take further action in accordance with the law.
