President of the Livestock Breeders Association: Despite the increase in local farm prices, farmers still do not have the confidence to raise!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Breeders' Association, said that despite the current increase in the price of live pigs in Cambodia, farmers who still raise pigs still do not trust the expansion of livestock due to farmers. Fear of the African plague that is currently plaguing pigs in Vietnam and spreading to one of Cambodia's provinces.
Before the outbreak of African plague, the price of live pigs was between 8,000 and 10,000 riel per kilogram, but after banning the import of pigs from Vietnam, the price of pigs increased, but not much, on average 11,000 riel. Kg.
"The African epidemic is so devastating that if it were to happen to one pig, all the pigs in one farm would have to die, and that's why farmers, companies and farm owners would not dare to raise and expand," he said. Raising.
He added that the above factors are causing the price of pigs to increase, but there are not many farmers or expand in raising, and this is why Cambodia does not have enough pork supply in the market and requires imports from Thailand. By importing 1,000 or 1.5 thousand per day.
He said that if the African epidemic continues to infiltrate the Cambodian border, Cambodia will face a shortage of pigs and continue to import more pigs from Thailand.
Please be informed that after the outbreak of African swine fever in Vietnam, the Royal Government of Cambodia has announced a ban on the import of pigs from Vietnam to Cambodia to prevent the disease from spreading to pigs in Cambodia.
