Khmer Rouge tribunal hears appeals against O'An
He said that the hearing on the appeal would be held in public on June 20 and 21, 2019, before the Pre-Trial Chamber ruled on whether the accused should be sent to trial. Or the charges shall be dropped before the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia.
He stated that national co-prosecutors, international co-prosecutors and national-international co-lawyers defending the accused would have the right to present their arguments. At the end of the hearing, the Pre-Trial Chamber will take some time to consider and issue a decision on this appeal.
It should be noted that the Pre-Trial Chamber of the ECCC consists of three national judges and two international judges. As the Appeals Chamber, the Pre-Trial Chamber may hear hearings and appeals against orders and decisions issued by the Co-Investigating Judges.
It should be noted that the Co-Investigating Judges of the Khmer Rouge Tribunal on 16 August 2018 issued two separate Closing Orders in the case against O'An, according to the differing record of whether O'An is within the jurisdiction of Is the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) a senior leader or one of the highest authorities?
The International Co-Investigating Judge considers O'An to be under the jurisdiction of the ECCC, which is one of the highest authorities and has sufficient evidence to charge him with Cham genocide and crimes. Against humanity as well as other crimes under Cambodian law.
The National Co-Investigating Judge considers that O'An is not under the individual jurisdiction of the ECCC in either category, is not a senior leader of the Democratic Kampuchea regime and is responsible for serious crimes committed. Must be brought to trial and decided to drop the charges against O'An for that reason.
The meeting was attended by seven ASEAN member countries and representatives of relevant institutions in Cambodia, including the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts. Cambodia, with the General Department of Camcontrol of the Ministry of Commerce as the national codec liaison point, is hosting a rotating host of the 19th ASEAN Codex Working Group.
