Mr. Mon Chhin, the victim's husband, said that his wife gave birth on June 7, 2019 at the Takeo Provincial Referral Hospital with a normal delivery by a midwife named Sothea.
Three days after the birth, he took his wife to stay at home in Samrong district for a day. Suddenly, his wife had a severe stomach ache. The family was rushed to Calmette Hospital for treatment.
The husband and wife of the victim claimed that at Calmette Hospital, doctors said his wife had an infection in her uterus and had received a large amount of blood transfusions and was in critical condition.
Nuth Sinath, director of the Takeo provincial health department, told Fresh News that the department was conducting a search today and could find out for sure if it was true. The Department has taken action against negligent doctors.
