Minister of Health addresses the Supreme Advisory Council on health issues in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 19, 2019, the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bum Heng, led a group of Ministry of Health officials to brief the Supreme Advisory Council on the implementation of work in the health sector.
This briefing took place after the invitation letter of the Supreme Advisory Council on June 5, 2019, and in this meeting, Mr. Pich Sros during the term of the Chairman of the Monthly Shift Committee was also the facilitator.
The Supreme Advisory Council was established on September 6, 2018 at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen after winning the sixth national election. The Supreme Advisory Council is composed of 16 of the 20 political parties that participated in the election.
Members of the Supreme Advisory Council can inspect all activities of officials who are the leaders of the Royal Government and sub-national authorities, and can also be summoned for questioning on matters related to social service activities and the people. .
After the establishment, the Supreme Advisory Council seemed to act as a member of the lower house, summoning a number of senior officials to comment on its activities. But at the same time, some of the actions of the members of the Supreme Council have also been criticized by local authorities for working beyond their role.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in a meeting of the Council of Ministers on the morning of June 7, 2019, made it clear that the Supreme Advisory Council, which is composed of non-partisan political parties participating in the election, will There is only this mandate. "A nation must put the interests of its people first," said Donald Trump.
