After listening to the discussions and suggestions from the Department of Expertise, companies, the private sector and development partners on the issue of planting, selling and buying of all agricultural communities, Mr. Thiv Vanthy said that business is a common problem that the agricultural community. Women producers and farmers are experiencing a lot in recent years.
He said those problems included farmers, lack of technology, lack of investment capital, lack of information for markets and lack of policies to support farmers or small production groups at the grassroots level. That is why the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Thom Province organized this program in collaboration with partner organizations that are supporting agricultural communities in many provinces.
