The Youth Party proposed 7 points to the Minister of Health to strengthen the health of Cambodians across the country (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In the meeting between the Ministry of Health and the Supreme Advisory Council on the morning of June 19 In 2019, the delegation of the Cambodian Youth Party proposed seven points to the Minister of Health to strengthen the health of Cambodians across the country.
The seven proposals include:
1: Let the Ministry of Health urge the law on alcohol control as soon as possible to protect the lives of our Cambodian citizens
2. The Ministry of Health should review the attitude of the staff of the Ministry of Health to non-medical hospitals, such as receptionists, IT professionals, accountants who receive patients for the first time when receiving services at some government departments.
3. Let the Ministry review the use of poor cards in a transparent and effective manner for the Cambodian people with the utmost care.
4: The Ministry of Health is requested to inform and indicate the number of standard medical staff who must go to provide health services at the local level, such as health posts, health centers, in order to determine the number of medical staff to provide health services and health reforms that are delegated. Young people observe in that base.
5. Let the Ministry take action against the behavior of doctors taking money from private clinics, which is corrupt and extorts money from doctors who work in rural and remote areas.
7: The Ministry of Health should check and arrange the sleeping area for the hospital staff, especially the students, to go to the hospital for rehabilitation in an appropriate and orderly manner.
