Health official: Dengue cases in Banteay Meanchey province increased up to 3 times compared to the same period in 2018
(Banteay Meanchey): Dr. Roeun Sothy, Director of the Technical Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department, said on June 17 that dengue fever in this province has increased up to three times compared to the same period. And in 2018.
He said that in the first five months of 2018, there were 214 cases of dengue fever, while in the first five months of 2019, there were 728 cases, of which 70% were treated at Kantha Bopha Komar Angkor Hospital in Siem Reap.
Dr. Roeun Sothy said this on the occasion that he and Dr. Chepichet, the head of the disease response team, led subordinates to educate people in homes, restaurants and schools to explain the prevention of dengue fever in the province. Banteay Meanchey.
Dr. Roeun Sothy said that dengue fever now affects people of all ages, but mostly children, so parents need to watch their children's clothing, play or sleep during the day to prevent mosquito bites because mosquitoes bite during the day. When a child has a fever, take him to a nearby health center or hospital.
He said that breeding tiger mosquitoes need clean water, such as water in cans, pots, plastic cups, plastic plates, foam, especially tires, which can lay eggs and hatch into water worms and evolve into mosquitoes, so be eliminated. Clean water stored for use in jars must be washed, covered, fed to 7-color fish, or abattoired to kill water worms.
He added that the intervention by spraying mosquito repellent is effective only for a short time and kills only mosquitoes can not kill water worms. The best option is to work together to eliminate mosquito and worm habitats.
