Krouch Chhmar district is located along the Mekong River in Tbong Khmum province, most of the people are engaged in fishing and farming. Every day, the people there bring fish, vegetables, fruits to sell at the market in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, traveling in small boats, boats, and for the last 3 years, there have been ferries to help copy instead.
Mr. Chhin Hor Chea described that the construction of the Cambodia-China Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar Friendship Bridge is not difficult compared to the other three bridges across the river that the company has already built. However, the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has to have a foundation pillar deeper than the previous three bridges, with a depth of up to 103 meters, because the riverbed in that area has a lot of sand.
Currently, the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has been built to the middle of the river, and one can also see the shape of the bridge standing firmly on the river gradually. The people of Stung Trang and Kroch Chhmar, who take the ferry across the Mekong River, always look at the bridges that have never been on their land.
The presence of the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has made the people who used to have difficulty in giving birth very excited, some even excited to the point of tears. The people of Stung Trang and Kroch Chhmar districts consider the bridge as an achievement, a great achievement that is priceless for his life. In particular, they expect the bridge to contribute to a better life.
