What is most special is that each of the peers expressed their deepest condolences and gratitude to the former military elders, who used to educate and teach them with sincerity. They consider all military teachers to be second parents. Dedicated to physical and mental strength and time for almost a lifetime to fulfill the priceless duty is to provide knowledge to all students.
The initiative of Major General Hing Sok Mony, as well as the guidance of friends, brought this group of former trainees and the 17th generation of map makers to keep in close contact until they came together. More than 100 people and have created many collective events together.
Intimate gatherings as well as mutual pain of peers, training courses, secretarial staff and 17th generation map staff, this group made them build solidarity, friendship, heartfeltness, sharing, helping each other all the time. Difficult and they even vowed to organize a solidarity dinner and express gratitude to the former military officer on June 17 every year.
