The arrest of the suspect was made on the orders of Mr. Koy Sao, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on charges of trafficking, illegal possession and use of drugs at the Club (Lux Sary) House No. 42, Street 214, Sangkat Boeung Reang, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, on June 4, 2019. According to Article 42 and Article 44 of the Law on Drug Control.
After further questioning later that afternoon, Investigating Judge Koy Sao ordered the detention of suspect Huon Tuch in prison pending further trial. Senior officials of the Ministry of Labor call on all parties concerned to oppose all forms of child labor in the brick industry
(Phnom Penh): In order to manage and develop the brick handicraft sector to have better work standards and ensure the sustainable elimination of child labor in the brick handicraft sector, on June 17, 2019, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized a workshop on Campaign to prevent the use of child labor in the field of brick-making handicrafts in the capitals and provinces with the first brick-making handicraft in 2019.
The workshop was chaired by Ms. Soeng Sor Socheata, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, representing Minister Ith Sam Heng, with the following objectives:
1. Provide guidance to labor inspectors and relevant authorities who have the right to be judicial police to intervene in the prevention, prevention and integration of vulnerable and vulnerable children in the field of brick production.
2: Raise awareness and promote the campaign against child labor through the definition of child labor, disclosure of the causes and effects of child labor, policies and legal norms and measures to combat child labor in the field of brick production. .
3. Cooperate and participate in the implementation of labor inspection measures, crime prevention and suppression mechanisms and monitoring systems for child labor in the workplace (brick production) in schools and in the communities where children and their families live for lower institutions. The nation continues to practice.
4. The contribution of labor inspectors and relevant authorities in advising, sharing experiences and reflecting on the recent progress of the brick-and-mortar industry in order to make this draft guideline comprehensive in terms of improving working conditions and benefits. Children in Cambodia.
In addition, on behalf of the States Parties, Cambodia has ratified international instruments to protect children from the exploitation of child labor and to promote their fundamental rights, including the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child, Convention 138, 182 and 29; Of the International Labor Organization, which deals with the prohibition and elimination of the most serious forms of child labor.
The Royal Government of Cambodia considers the elimination of child labor as one of the most important issues in Cambodia, especially the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the process of ending child labor by 2025 in line with the Global Development Goals. Sustainable (2015-2030).
The Secretary of State called on all stakeholders to work closely and strictly implement the policy objectives of the Royal Government, with a high level of commitment and commitment to take action against all forms of exploitation. Child labor in the field of successful brick-making, which is obligatory to prevent children from doing things that endanger children's educational opportunities, health, well-being and development.
She sincerely hopes and believes that the content of this workshop will be put to good use, including a strong commitment to the successful implementation of specific activities to contribute to the construction sector in Cambodia without child labor. A tourist boat sank in the sea, but no danger to people
(Sihanoukville): The Maritime Traffic Police of Sihanoukville Provincial Police said that a Daly Tour tourist boat sank in the sea in front of Mlup Chrey Beach in Sihanoukville at 9 pm. June 16, 2019.
Brigadier General Nop Panha, Deputy Police Commissioner of Preah Sihanouk Province, told the media on June 17 that the sinking of a tourist boat was caused by a technical problem and was not related to the weather.
Mr. Nop Panha stated that this incident caused damage to property and parts of the tourist boat, but did not cause danger or affect human life.
However, Mr. Nop Panha reminded people, especially tourists to be very careful when traveling by sea, because this season is the rainy season, there is a lot of rain, wind and big waves. Mr. Nop Panha called on seafarers, especially tourists traveling by sea and fishermen, to increase their safety precautions.
