Secretary of State Chan Chesta: More than 300 companies are exhibiting agricultural products in Koh Pich as an opening from the Royal Government to attract investors to participate in the development of the country
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has the 4th International Exhibition and Workshop on Agriculture, Livestock and Fisheries, which has been held for 2 days from 17 to 18 June 2019 at the Koh Pich Exhibition Center in Phnom Penh. More than 300 companies from different countries represent the latest products, innovations and tools of the agricultural, livestock, chemical and pesticide industries in Cambodia and the region.
During the opening ceremony this morning, Mr. Chan Chesta, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the private sector, which has more than 300 companies exhibiting agricultural products, is open to the government to attract private investors. Participate in the development of the nation together.
Mr. Chan Chesta stated: "This is the openness of the Royal Government as well as attracting private investors to participate in the development of the country. In fact, an important partner in the development of the country in the context that Cambodia is taking agriculture as the core of the economy and strive to promote industry instead of agriculture is private.
"Therefore, we can not miss the private sector. We are open and supportive of the private sector. In the past, the government has reduced bureaucracy, which means reducing the complexity of the investment process. In Cambodia. At the same time, the Royal Government is reducing the cost of transporting electricity so that private investors can develop in our country.
In recent years, the demand for meat and fisheries in Cambodia has increased rapidly, which has led to an increase in the processing and production of cattle feed and aquaculture feed. The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also estimates that the demand for meat will be around 300,000 tons and will increase by 2020, when the Cambodian population is estimated to grow by about 1.5% annually.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pa Socheatvong, President of Phnom Penh Capital Council, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Chbar Ampov District Council for the third mandate on June 17, 2019. The third mandate council of Chbar Ampov district has Mr. Oum Mareth as its chairman and has 20 members.
This morning's inauguration ceremony was held at Chbar Ampov District Hall with the participation of the District Governor, Police Inspector, Gendarmerie Commander, Sangkat Chief, Village Chief and the people.
It should be noted that in the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council elections of the third mandate in 2019, the Cambodian People's Party received overwhelming support and control of almost all council seats, followed by the Khmer United National Party and FUNCINPEC. .
The official results announced by the NEC on June 08, 2019 show that in the Capital and Provincial Council elections, the CPP won 550 seats, the Khmer United National Party won 6 seats and FUNCINPEC won. Three seats out of a total of 559 seats.
