The Minister said that the priority of the Provincial Council for the third mandate is to prepare a five-year development plan based on the three-year rolling investment sector. Therefore, the provincial governors and deputy governors are requested to consult and divide the roles and responsibilities in this meeting in a timely manner in accordance with the announcement of the NEC. Not more than 14 days is required for the announcement to take office.
Mr. Pich Bunthen further stated that the provincial governor must assign the provincial director of administration to have a systematic office of the staff to start some work that implements the work of the Capital and Provincial Councils that have been implemented in the past and the new councilors must Declare their assets and liabilities in accordance with the law and send them to the Anti-Corruption Unit no later than 30 days after taking office.
