Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Inspects Coal Waste Processing Plant, Concerned About People's Health
(Preah Sihanouk): The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Yon Min, on Monday, June 17th, led the officials of professional institutions to inspect the location of “Simao” Coal Waste Conversion Plant located in Group 4, Village 2, Otres Commune, Stung Hav District, Province. Sihanoukville.
The inspection came after 42 families living around the "Simao" coal ash processing plant complained and worried about health problems caused by the ash emitted from the factory.
Mr. Yon Min said that the factory has a valid permit from the Ministry, but now has an impact on the people living around the factory and affect the environment and the well-being of the people living around.
However, Mr. Yun Min claimed that according to the direct inspection of the expert team, it was found that the factory did not cause too bad an impact on the lives of the people. The provincial governor explained that the ash from the coal-fired power plant was removed for processing to supply the concrete or cement plant.
Mr. Yon Min explained that as a solution, the working group agreed to the above factory to improve the technical characteristics to make sure that there is no ash on the houses of the people and reduce the impact and protect the environment well.
"This work, the Sihanoukville provincial administration has set aside two or three months for the coal processing plant to improve its plant. But if the factory does not follow the instructions of the Sihanoukville administration, the company will have to stop operating or find a new location away from the homes of people living. This is the warning of the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province.
The provincial governor continued, "If the owner of the coal processing plant works to improve the environmentally friendly factory, the provincial administration will allow him to continue his business." Because the solution is we do it to win together. This means that investors also benefit, people also get jobs from investing. "Because the company also pays taxes to the state budget and people also have jobs to benefit each other."
However, Mr. Yon Min asked the people to be understanding, if there is no serious impact, to be understanding, because the people also benefit from investment and get jobs.
Chen Song, manager of the coal waste processing plant, said that his plant currently dries 100 tons of waste from the coal plant to supply to the cement plant daily. He also promised to improve the environment inside the factory so that there will be no more dust coming out of the factory in the future so as not to affect the people.
