Senior official of the Ministry of Health warns to close restaurants and restaurants that are not clean
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ngy Mean Heng, Advisor to the Ministry of Health and Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, warned to revoke the license of any restaurant and restaurant that is not hygienic in cooking.
The warning of the senior official of the Ministry of Health was made during a workshop on food hygiene practices for the people of Cambodia on the afternoon of June 16, 2019.
Dr. Ngy Mean Heng said that food hygiene is part of food safety. When it comes to food safety, it covers a wide range of topics, from farming, raising livestock to harvesting or slaughtering, transporting meat, transporting vegetables, marketing to cooking. Restaurants, canteens and homes as well.
He said that in relation to food safety in restaurants and canteens, the Ministry of Health has taken measures only to guide and educate, there is no punishment for restaurant and canteen owners. But if restaurant and restaurant owners who have had food problems and refuse to change, the ministry will take action to revoke the license to stop doing business again.
Dr. Ngy Mean Heng stated that "the Ministry of Health today is still only education and guidance. When we have shortcomings, we only educate and guide him, but if he still refuses to change, we will take action to revoke the license and not certify him. It could put him in a difficult position to apply for a license to continue running restaurants and eateries. ”
As for those who sell food on the streets, Dr. Ngy Mean Heng confirmed that the Ministry will not punish them. He said that in neighboring countries, Cambodia also has the same problem of food hygiene on the streets, so Cambodia can not touch hands, feet, feet, law enforcement faster than other countries.
According to a senior official at the Ministry of Health, the food situation in Cambodia is now better compared to 10 years ago. Nowadays, there are many restaurants and canteens that implement this principle of hygiene, and people who sell food in the market are beginning to understand food hygiene. For the food he sells, he does not put food on the ground, he puts it at least 60 cm from the ground, and he begins to know how to cover food.
"We think there is progress. "We hope that as we continue to open this course, his understanding will increase and his performance will improve." This is the assertion of the advisor of the Ministry of Health.
At the same time, Mr. Samohak Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors and President of the Federation of Medical, Pharmaceutical and Dental Association of Cambodia, said that the issue of food hygiene, the relevant parties have cooperated well with the Department of Health, Phnom Penh, as well as officials at all levels. He said that this issue must be emphasized and involved together.
Dr. Ley Sopheap stated, "For any person in the restaurant and canteen, the place of import and distribution related to the food of the people of Cambodia, any part that is wrong in terms of the law and other legal standards, we cooperate with the local authorities. The land is legally enforced by the Royal Government at both the national and sub-national levels.
He also called on restaurants and canteens, restaurants, festivals, chefs and food producers, all kinds of canned goods related to food and water, must consider food hygiene issues. If any restaurant and canteen has a problem with hygiene, it is necessary to take hot measures.
Mr. Thong Khon announced the composition of the national working group in the 9 cities and districts of Kampong Thom province and introduced some recommendations.
After Mr. Kong Solida, Director General of Administration and Finance of the Ministry of Tourism and a member of the National Working Group, announced the names and roles of the working group members, Minister Thong Khon introduced some recommendations to continue the work of the National Working Group. Smooth, efficient and sustainable.
The Minister instructed the national working group and sub-national administration to work together to achieve the following important tasks:
1: The chairmen of the nine recently announced National Working Groups at the Municipal / District Levels should hold emergency meetings at their Municipal / District Levels to hear reports and raise concerns, challenges, needs and Requests of local people.
2. Each national-district-level national working group shall set up a secretariat to coordinate the general work and report the results to the chairperson of the national working group in Kampong Thom province.
3. Each national-district-district-level national working group shall prepare a decision on the establishment of its own national-district-local-level working group in accordance with the work structure.
4: The national working group at the local level of each city-district must prepare a clear action plan, working mode and organization of public forums at the commune / sangkat level.
5: Continue to promote the examination and resolution of some necessary work, such as land clearing work in 3 areas, 2 land areas, whiskey conservation areas, land clearing work from the inventory of the department-unit to the people, land issues, people living in the satellite area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple area.
