(Phnom Penh): The draft law on the establishment of an international network for bamboo and rattan was approved by the National Assembly on June 17, 2019.
The National Assembly discussed and reviewed this important draft law under the chairmanship of Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly. The National Assembly approved the content of the entire draft law by 107 votes.
Mr. Chea Vandeth, Chairman of the Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources Investment Planning Committee of the National Assembly, read the report on the results of the study of the draft law to the National Assembly, while Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and his colleagues represented the Royal Government. Defend the draft law.
According to Mr. Veng Sakhon, the draft law on "Establishment of an International Network for Bamboo and Rattan" aims to improve the livelihood of the people and communities by changing their habits and encouraging people to use bamboo and rattan. Development period, production, conservation and processing of bamboo and rattan in accordance with the principles of sustainable and sustainable development of bamboo and rattan.
He added that the draft law covers the details of: First: the history of the International Network of Bamboo and Rattan, second: the policy and strategic plan, third: the statute of membership, fourth: the preparation: Enough before joining and 5th: the benefits of membership.
The Minister stated that through this agreement, he hopes and believes that Cambodia will achieve a good international cooperation in strengthening the capacity to protect and develop bamboo and rattan resources sustainably for the benefit of society, economy and green environment brotherhood, including Biodiversity conservation and national cultural heritage as well.
