(Phnom Penh): As planned, on the morning of June 17, 2019, the National Assembly convened its second plenary session of the sixth legislature to approve six agendas. The meeting was chaired by National Assembly President Samdech Heng Samrin and was attended by 108 members of the National Assembly.
(Kampot): China has shown great satisfaction with the cultivation techniques and the use of Cambodia's yellow banana harvesting techniques, which are in line with modern technology and high standards, while China has allowed Cambodia to export bananas. Yellow to China directly.
This past weekend, a delegation from the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries accompanied by Hu Wei, Deputy Minister of the General Administration of Customs of the People's Republic of China, and a delegation visited yellow banana plantations. Agro-commercial according to market) at Banana Farm, Longmet Agricultural Co., Kampot Province.
Speaking to reporters after the visit, Deputy Representative of the General Administration of Customs Hu Wei confirmed that he was very satisfied with the fresh yellow banana packaging factory of Long Met Agricultural Co., Ltd. Export yellow bananas to China for both cultivation and harvesting techniques.
According to Mr. Oknha Hun Lak, Managing Director of Leng Met Agricultural Co., Ltd., more than 400 hectares of banana plantations are currently being harvested, packaged and exported, with the hope that by 2019 more than 22,000 tons of fresh bananas will be imported. By 2020, this volume is expected to increase to more than 30,000 tons.
Mr. Oknha Hun Lak also stated that the company will cultivate a series of steps until the total area of 1,000 hectares by 2020. Mr. Oknha continued that today, the company harvests the yellow bananas every day, while for 9 months, the bananas can be harvested.
At the same time, Mr. Oknha also confirmed that the cultivation of bananas in the territory of Kampot province also helped the people to earn money, and according to the forecast, there were about 2,000 people coming to work. Next year. At present, there are about 900 people working here.
Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon has stated that China is the country with the largest demand for bananas, accounting for 40% of the world, with about 4 million tons per year, and the export of yellow bananas to China. The Chinese side has not set a banana export quota for Cambodia.
In addition to banana exports, the ministry is negotiating with the Chinese side to export mangoes and other agricultural products directly to the Chinese market, including longan, dragon fruit, coconut, pepper, saliva, lobster and trout. .
It should be noted that Longmet Agricultural Co., Ltd. is the largest and most modern banana plantation company in Cambodia with an investment of 32 million USD, cultivating more than 1,000 hectares in Kampot province and exporting yellow bananas to the Chinese market. At the beginning of 2019.
