Ministry of Public Works starts inspecting vehicles and driver's licenses at Phnom Penh Autonomous Port and Sihanoukville City, found 29 illegal vehicles
(Phnom Penh): The Technical Inspection Team inspected vehicles and driver's licenses at the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port and Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, inspecting 201 vehicles, including 29 vehicles, and fined them. In the amount of 4,175,000 Riels.
Commencement of inspections and restrictions on the implementation of the Road Traffic Law by imposing transitional fines and correcting the technical characteristics of vehicles for heavy vehicles and drivers of trucks that do not meet the requirements as stated in the Road Traffic Law and Relevant legal documents in force at the original destination in Phnom Penh Autonomous Port and Sihanoukville Autonomous Port.
As a result, the Working Group on Enforcement of Road Traffic Law at the original destination in Phnom Penh Autonomous Port found that: The owners of heavy trucks entering and exiting Phnom Penh Autonomous Port in the early stages of implementing this measure Required and is continuing to adjust the technical characteristics of vehicles under its control in accordance with the technical standards of vehicles to be able to enter and exit the cargo port.
According to the conclusion of the working group, this campaign has yielded significant positive results, as we have observed that some of the vehicles inspected have just been technically modified according to the deadline set by the National Road Safety Committee. Land and some do not dare to travel yet, waiting for the correction first to bring the traffic again.
Under the shadow of peace! Residents of Ba Phnom District, Prey Veng Province Celebrate the Ascension Ceremony
(Prey Veng): Every year, the people of Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, always celebrate the Ascension Day to commemorate the merits of the ancestors who have made great achievements in managing the construction of land since the Phnom Kingdom period (during the 5th century AD). .S) To be prosperous until now.
During the 3 nights and 3 days of the festival, there are various programs in accordance with the ancient traditions that the villagers remember and keep up to date, associated with Buddhism and cultural programs, folk games, mixed arts, both ancient and modern. .
Under the shadow of peace and the fruits of the nation's development, under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for the last 20 years, the Ascension Ceremony has been re-organized with greater pomp and circumstance. From year to year, local people, villages and close relatives and friends participated in large numbers.
Speaking on the occasion of meeting with nearly 1,000 people before the counting ceremony for 173 monks on the morning of the third day of the ceremony, Mr. Prum Sokha, Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group, praised the solidarity of Ba Phnom people. All who have strived to preserve the fine traditions of the village to pass on the legacy to the next generation to always remember the virtues of the patriotic ancestors of the previous generation.
The value of remembering the lessons of the past is the peace for building and developing the land towards a prosperous future for all generations.
