All three suspects, along with exhibits, are currently being held in custody at the provincial police commissioner's office to build a case to be sent to court for legal proceedings.
General Kheng Someth Donates to Orphans in Varin District, Siem Reap Province
(Siem Reap): General Kheng Someth, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, Ministry of Interior and Commander of the National Police in the 4th and 5th Zones, and Ms. Koy Salina donated rice, food and money to a poor woman with a disability. She raised six orphans in Varin district, Siem Reap province.
The donation was handed over by Major General Kheng Ra, a representative of General Kheng Someth, to the disabled woman in Siem Reap on the morning of June 16, 2019, while the team was transporting them from Varin district to the city. Siem Reap.
The general donated 100 kilograms of rice, noodles, soy sauce, fish sauce, water, pots, bowls, spoons, mosquito nets, blankets, knives, forks, water pipes, kettles and many other items, as well as a large amount of money. The orphans also received school supplies and funds.
Separately, another family who lives in Siem Reap and is in poor condition, named John Srey, 33 years old, living in Slor Kram village, Slor Kram commune, Siem Reap city, received the same gift as the grandmother's family.
