Advisor to Samdech Heng Samrin told UME students that "Success depends on physical strength and determination"
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Muon Veasna, Advisor to Samdech Panha Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Chairman of the Management Committee of UME University of Management and Economics, said that human success depends on the use of two forces, namely physical and mental strength.
Mr. Muon Veasna's remarks were made this morning, June 16, 2019, as he and she presided over the opening ceremony of the defense of nearly 200 students of UME University in Kampong Cham Province.
Speaking to the students who have to defend their dissertation today, Mr. Muon Veasna continued that in order to be successful, all of our students must be healthy, that is, physically strong, with the determination to be brave and strong-willed. Towards its goal, especially on the day to defend this dissertation.
Mr. Muon Veasna added that four years of our students' bachelor's degree has been completed, but we must continue to study other subjects throughout our lives.
Please note that on the day of the defense of this dissertation, there were 15 7th generation undergraduate students. Separately, there are 185 14th generation undergraduate students.
Mr. Mao Dung, a member of the management team of UME University, also sent a message to all students who have to defend the dissertation that after our students have been studying hard for 4 years, he hopes that today all students will work hard to To the best of my ability, I have defended my dissertation, which in this program has 6 subjects that need to be defended to pass the bachelor's degree that you have been trying to study in the past.
Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Calls on Pregnant Women to Stop Giving Birth at Home at Maternal and Child Health Center
(Preah Vihear): Four maternity wards and waiting rooms in Preah Vihear province's Choam Ksan district worth more than $ 100,000 were inaugurated in the presence of Preah Vihear provincial governor Un Chanda. People need to change their attitude from giving birth by traditional midwives at home to giving birth at health centers for the safety of mothers and babies.
The ceremony was held on the morning of June 16, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Kuong Lo, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, as well as leaders of government officials from departments around the province in Yeang village, Yeang commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province. .
Mr. Un Chanda said that currently the Ministry of Health has provided a lot of construction, especially in remote border areas. This shows the attention of the Ministry of Health, especially the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who always thinks about the health and well-being of people, especially in remote areas.
The Governor of Preah Vihear Province also requested all health officials to make more efforts to provide equitable and quality health services to the people without discrimination. Let the district, commune and village authorities support and cooperate well to make the new maternity ward run smoothly to reduce maternal and infant morbidity in accordance with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Plan.
Dr. Kuong Lo said that the four health center buildings and waiting rooms that are now inaugurated are located in Choam Ksan District Referral Hospital, Rong Roeung 4 Health Center, Yeang Health Center and Antul Health Post in the district. Choam Ksan, Preah Vihear Province.
