(Phnom Penh): Through the evolution from one era to another, the protection of human rights has become an important topic that each nation pays close attention to and promotes. In addition, the violation of individual rights by torture and cruelty is an inhumane act that should not happen to any person under any circumstances.
To better understand what acts are considered torture and cruelty? And to what extent will those who commit such acts face punishment? Fresh News Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation will present and share to the following students:
In order to prevent and reduce the occurrence of this inhumane act, the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia stipulates in Article 210 that "Torture or atrocities committed against any person shall be punishable by imprisonment from 7 (seven) to 15 years. Fifteen) years.
In short, torture and atrocities are taken seriously by human beings, and the 2009 Penal Code criminalizes those who commit severe crimes.
Meanwhile, through Royal Decree NS / RKOT / 0817/691 dated 22 August 2017, Cambodia established the National Committee against Torture with the aim of preventing and combating torture, atrocities, atrocities, persecution or punishment to Strengthen the protection of all deprived people of their freedom from torture.
