Please be informed that Khun Reap Forest Research and Rehabilitation Station was established in 2012 with a grant from the Republic of Korea in the amount of $ 3.5 million.
The station aims to research, disseminate and plant seedlings for people to plant to create forest cover in Banteay Srei and throughout Siem Reap. On average, the nursery plant produces 100,000 seedlings a year and has set up a memorial garden for the public to plant and set up seed plantations.
In addition, the station also acts as a place for research on forest genetics, training and disseminating techniques to students and residents related to tree planting techniques, effective care and protection of land use, and training of various agricultural techniques.
