BEIJING: After the attack on two oil tankers in the Gulf of Oman on Thursday, Chinese President Xi Jinping said that Beijing will strengthen ties with Iran. But given the current situation, some experts believe that China could use the Iran case as a subject for mediation with the United States, which is calling on the international community to stop doing business with Tehran.
To counter US sanctions, Iran has relied heavily on China for years, with 30 percent of the Islamic Republic's exports and imports being in trade with Beijing. In addition, China sees Iran as an important route for transporting its influence to the Middle East, or in other words, the two countries are not only trading partners, but also Strategic partners as well.
But because of trade disputes with the United States, experts such as Jon Alterman, director of the Middle East program at the US-based Institute for International Strategy and Studies, believe that China may one day abandon old friends like Iran.
To promote the use of cyclos in tourism, Cambodia will host a major cyclo tourism event on June 22-23.
(Phnom Penh): Seeing that the use of cyclo as a means of transportation has decreased significantly, some public-private partnerships have jointly organized the "Cyclo Tourism 2019" event in order to promote the use of cyclo in the sector. Tourism aims to improve the lives of cyclo riders and create new tourism products for tourists.
Under the collaboration between the Ministry of Tourism, the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents (CATA), the Cyclo Conservation Association and the Informal Occupation, the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC), Phnom Penh Capital Hall and other partners, this cyclo tourism event will be held from 22-23. This coming June 2019 at Preah Neang Prachha Bormey Park (near Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh).
The president of CATA stated, "Looking at this challenge, we have pushed for the organization of the 2019 Cyclo Tour race in order to increase the popularity, increase the use of cyclo and the income of cyclo riders to support the cyclo business. "Lost through the use of cyclos in tourism."
Ms. Chhay Sivlin continued that the organization of this event is also to participate in the implementation of strategies and policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially cooperation with the Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries - institutions to promote the expansion of tourism destinations in Cambodia and encourage People learn more about the potential of tourism and get the latest information in tourism.
Mr. Im Sambath, President of the Cyclo Conservation and Informal Business Association, said that the composition of the cyclo that will be organized in the race on June 23 is 136 cyclo divided into 68 pairs, including 178 cyclo riders. .
CATA and Cyclo Conservation Association also called on organizations, institutions, companies, partners, philanthropists, citizens, youth and other stakeholders to participate in this cyclo tourism event in large numbers, especially to donate money, clothing, food and supplies. To cyclo riders as much as possible.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin and Mr. M. Sambath also stated that all participants can also visit and enjoy many other activities such as cyclo ride in the park of Preah Neang Prachha Bormey, showing the history and how to make Sito. With many food and beverage sales. There will also be live acoustic concerts with a special rustic decor.
