(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for June 15, 2019 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 25 cases, including 8 cases of use and 17 cases of trafficking, arrested 52 suspects.
According to the report, from January 1 to June 15, 2019, law enforcement forces cracked down on 3,716 cases and detained 7,876 people (597 females), including 167 foreigners. Also. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Leaders of 28 Other Countries Attend the 5th Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence-Building Measures in Asia
At the summit, CICA leaders reaffirmed their commitment to the UN Charter and the universally recognized norms and principles of international law in promoting the goals and principles of the CICA. As stated in the Declaration of Guidelines on CICA Member States Relations of September 14, 1999 and the Almaty Law of June 4, 2002.
At the same time, the leaders of all CICA countries recognized the importance of a global partnership in mobilizing financial resources and investing to achieve sustainable development goals. Increasing the deployment and use of state-of-the-art technology to reduce low-energy fossil fuels, renewable energy and energy efficiency are critical to addressing climate change and achieving the seventh Sustainable Development Goal (SDG7). ).
At the summit, the leaders discussed the importance of an open world economy, connecting all countries and peoples in sharing the benefits of globalization, which must be firmly committed to the trading system. Multilateralism focuses on the rule of law, transparency, non-discrimination, an environmentally friendly and open multilateral trading system based on the WTO.
The leaders also stressed the joint efforts to promote regional connectivity, especially integrated and competitive logistics and transportation systems, and to help achieve more efficient use of trade opportunities between states. Member and accelerate regional and international transit and transit cooperation.
