Mr. Kun Nhem requested ASEAN Customs to take care to prevent the smuggling of plastic waste from developed countries to ASEAN (Video inside) (Laos): Dr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise Request customs from ASEAN member countries to pay attention and prevent the smuggling of plastic waste from developed countries to ASEAN member countries.
She also highlighted that the 28th ASEAN Customs Director-General Meeting is a forum for monitoring the progress of the implementation of initiatives under the responsibility of the ASEAN Customs Administration in order to increase transparency and predictability. Implement customs procedures and aim to increase trade facilitation and reduce business costs in ASEAN member countries.
During the meeting, Dr. Kun Nhem also raised some issues that the ASEAN Customs Working Group needs to pay more attention to and raise as a working activity to respond to new challenges. Challenges that Kun Nhem asked ASEAN Customs to pay more attention to include increased drug and wildlife smuggling, the smuggling of plastic waste from developed countries into ASEAN, and the threat of new terrorism. In the area and so on.
The 28th ASEAN Customs Director-General Meeting decided on a number of important issues, such as:
Recognize the entry into force of the Seventh Protocol and urge ASEAN Member States to expedite the ratification of the Second Protocol to the Transit Agreement Framework.
2: Establish a sub-working group to study the establishment of the ASEAN Agreement on Recognition of Mutually Authorized Economic Operators
3. Encourage the customs administrations of all ASEAN countries to continue to cooperate with institutions and stakeholders in building the 2022 ASEAN Customs Tariff Schedule.
4: Welcoming the progress made in promoting law enforcement by the ASEAN Customs Administration and emphasizing the importance of cooperation to meet new challenges.
5: Agree for the ASEAN Customs Working Group to start preparing the Strategic Plan for Customs Development for 2021-2025
6. Welcoming the progress in building the ASEAN Single Window System and urging all ASEAN member countries to implement the electronic source certificate exchange by the end of 2019.
