3.5 tonnes of ivory and 4 tonnes of scorpions were found Wednesday in several containers as customs officials inspected a container shipped from the northern port of Haipong, Vietnam.
The metal container containing ivory and scorpion shells has been mixed with other rubber containers to conceal the trafficking of wildlife fragments from the customs authorities.
No one has claimed that the goods are theirs, and no details are available as to the origin of the goods.
Hunting and trafficking in ivory and carnivores is punishable by up to five years in prison in Vietnam. In addition, Vietnam is a common destination for wildlife trade and a transfer point for ivory and other wildlife trade to China.
The pangolin is arguably the most trafficked mammal in the world. The carcasses of this species are used to make traditional medicine.
Stopped the car for a while, the thief drove up and disappeared with his two children, but fortunately the police found
(Phnom Penh): A case of car theft caused a shock to the authorities in Phnom Penh announced on the radio to open a search immediately, a woman stopped the car for a while near the house and was stolen by the thief The two children in the car went with him.
