Cambodia finds three winners for World Robotics Olympics in Hungary in early November
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has found three winners to prepare for the World Robot Olympics in Hungary in early November 2019. All three teams are set to represent Cambodia after winning the 2019 World Robot Olympiad in Cambodia.
The 2019 World Robot Olympiad in Cambodia took place on June 8, 2019, bringing together some of Cambodia's best young people who excel in Stem subjects.
This year's competition for children and youth includes installing and running software to make robots work. Candidates can also compete in freestyle under the common theme "Smart City" to create innovative robotic service projects for sustainable cities in the future.
The Cambodia Science Fair has organized this competition and this is the second year. The organization received the participation of 26 teams of contestants from various high schools, accompanied by teachers, school representatives and parents who helped make the 2019 World Robot Olympics a success.
The World Robot Olympiad is a truly international competition with 65 countries from around the world participating. This year, the three winning teams will represent Cambodia in the international round on November 8-10, 2019 in Győr, Hungary.
