Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 14, 2019 that the Ministry of Agriculture is working closely with the Chinese side to ensure the export of trout from Cambodia. To China will be achieved soon.
He said that in a meeting with Hu Wei, Deputy Minister of Customs Administration of the People's Republic of China, yesterday and today, the Minister discussed the export of fish and other agricultural products to China.
The Minister stated that for the export of fish to China, Cambodia has already prepared the infrastructure, with a Chinese company has set up a processing and packaging factory, set up cold storage and connected with some fish farms in Cambodia.
He added that in the past, Cambodia has sent many letters through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to China, but this letter has not been sent to the institution responsible for permitting the import of this fish.
"At this time, the delegation led by the Deputy Minister of Customs Administration has given us their names, contact numbers," he said. We will contact the Chinese side directly for this job. The Deputy Minister said that he had instructed the officer in charge of this work to cooperate with the Cambodian Fisheries Administration, and when he returned, he hoped for success.
Regarding the obstacles for the export of fish, the Minister claimed that there are no obstacles when the General Administration of Customs has already agreed that Cambodia can export because it has good partners and is preparing enough infrastructure. The export will go smoothly. He said the companies that invest in exporting fish are all experienced in exporting beef as well as some other agricultural products in China.
However, regarding the size of fish exports to China, the Minister has not yet been able to determine how much to export, but as long as there is a green light from the country, Cambodia's farming can happen because now farmers do not dare. Expand fish farming due to market challenges. So if we have a market, we will reach out to expand more large farms and increase fish exports.
The Minister of Agriculture said that in addition to the three-party export, China is satisfied if Cambodia expands on the export of pineapple, honey and durian because China is willing to accept because it is known that honey pineapple has a delicious taste that is grown in the province. Pailin and Battambang. China hopes that Cambodia will make further requests for exports to China. He said that each year China imports no less than 10 million tons of fruit.
In connection with the export of trout in the neighboring country of Cambodia, Vietnam annually exports more than 8 billion dollars to the world market.
The reason why Vietnam is able to export a lot, he said, is because Vietnam is in a good position to raise fish, and in Vietnam, the low cost of electricity is easy to process, refrigerated before export. The port also has better accessibility.
According to reports from banana exporters, shipping per container costs about $ 1,000 and takes about two weeks to ship to Shanghai. So we need a lot of time and money, this is a point that makes investors hesitant that we are trying to lower the cost of services to supply our processing in the future.
Please be informed that the Minister of Agriculture of Cambodia, Mr. Veng Sakhon, on June 13, 2019, in a meeting with the Deputy Minister of the General Administration of Customs of China, requested the Chinese side to accelerate the export of mangoes and other agricultural products such as lentils, dragon fruit, coconut, pepper. And ear saliva to China as soon as possible.
