(Tbong Khmum): A couple always quarrels because the husband is jealous of his wife. The fire of jealousy eventually ignited, making the unlucky husband brutally pull out a machete and kill several wives, leaving them dead on the spot and fleeing.
According to a source from the police, this horrific incident caused a surprise at about 1:30 pm on June 14, 2019 at the side of the CPP headquarters in Tbong Khmum district in Tuol Vihear village, Chiroth II commune. Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province. The suspects were identified as Preap Mai, 23, and Chum Theary, 17.
According to Mr. Chum Yuth, 58 years old, the father of the victim, said that the couple often had verbal conflicts with each other often, and the wife left the parents of the man who was close. Each came to live with his birth parents. On the afternoon of June 14, 2019, the husband went to his wife and caused a quarrel that led to a brutal chase.
The victim's father stated that the cause was due to a jealousy dispute. On the other hand, the son-in-law also used drugs.
However, after careful research, the killer, the husband, was arrested by the authorities at 6:20 am on June 15, 2019.
Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Ben Rath told Fresh News that after receiving this information, he ordered the force to launch an immediate search and take more than 17 hours to catch the perpetrator on the paved road. Teuk Chech village, Chiro II commune, Tbong Khmum district, while the suspect was getting ready to take a taxi to Siem Reap to escape.
The commissioner confirmed that the assailant, Pheap Mai, 23, was the victim's husband. Currently, the competent authorities are building a case to be sent to court to be punished according to the law.
