Minister Say Sam Al sets out four priorities for the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Working Group to address
Sihanoukville has been identified by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a potential economic hub for Cambodia, on the advice of Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as Cambodia's long-term vision. At the same time, the chairman of the working group urged the Sihanoukville provincial authorities at all levels to continue to strengthen the efficiency of providing public services to the people.
Minister Say Sam Al said that in the work of managing its locality, the authorities must transform and build themselves into a modern administration and know how to lead their local economy by knowing where their economic sources are and making good plans. Accurate and comprehensive to reap the benefits of development for local development.
"We must all work together to reap the benefits of development in order to maintain the national economic growth of more than 7% per year, create jobs for Cambodians, reduce poverty, increase living standards," he said. "Of the people and ensure sustainable development, respect for environmental sanitation."
The Chairman of the Working Group said that in order to accelerate the process of economic development, from now on, Sihanoukville will process the construction of road infrastructure in Sihanoukville, as well as the construction of other roads to create entrances. The more you come to Sihanoukville, the easier it is for the people.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that the construction of road infrastructure for Sihanoukville is a strategy to boost economic growth in the province, and the Minister said that the road from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville is not just a road. But it is also an economic lifeline for Cambodia. In addition, Sihanoukville will focus on solving some challenges such as traffic congestion, lack of electricity, lack of clean water.
The Minister urged the establishment of working groups to strengthen control, strengthen local development, respond to and address the needs of the people from the provincial level to the local level. The Minister announced the provision of funds and technical equipment for waste management by providing municipalities, districts, as well as in communes as garbage storage bins and garbage trucks for a clean and beautiful city.
At the same time, the Minister urged the administration at all levels to participate in expanding the infrastructure for dealing with pollution, cleaning and environmental sanitation, he said that "environmental sanitation is the daily work of local authorities." In managing wastewater, the minister said more wastewater treatment plants would be built.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of Preah Sihanouk Provincial National Assistance Team, presided over the inauguration ceremony of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Council for the third mandate at the Provincial Hall. Sihanoukville on the afternoon of June 14, 2019.
