Mr. Say Sam Al said that today is the opening day for Sihanoukville because it has increased its capacity to achieve economic growth of 7% in the last 20 years. The minister said that Sihanoukville, as well as the government, will continue to maintain good economic growth in the coming years.
Starting from this issue, Mr. Say Sam Al believes that the members of Sihanoukville Provincial Council of the third mandate will become the true representatives of the people and continue to work to solve the concerns of the people in a transparent, fair and effective manner. High.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has identified Sihanoukville as the largest economic pole among the three economic poles of Cambodia, including: Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville.
The Minister said that according to the steel strategy, the first is that Sihanoukville has increased economic growth by 7% and the second is to increase employment for people, especially young people can earn a high monthly income.
However, Mr. Say Sam Al stated that along with the progress of the administration of Sihanoukville, there are still some challenges that need to be addressed by the relevant parties immediately, such as: the construction of additional drainage systems. , Poor water or sewage management problems, lack of clean water, road problems before ensuring good quality and so on.
At the same time, Mr. Say Sam Al also requested the competent forces to continue to strengthen public security activities to ensure the security of the people, especially tourists and foreign investors more. In addition, it is necessary to participate in promoting the provision of public services to the people easily and quickly in order to turn Sihanoukville into an international province.
During the ceremony, Mr. Cheam Him, Chairman of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Council of the third mandate, also thanked the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia and His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, for recognizing the members of the Council. 19 Sihanoukville for the third mandate.
