This statement was made by Mr. Laslow Moore in a working meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on June 14, 2019 in Hungary.
The Speaker of the Hungarian Parliament recalled that he was the first Speaker of the National Assembly of Hungary to visit Cambodia and see the progress of Cambodia's sectors, such as the economy, all kinds of development, unlike in the past, Cambodia has suffered. Destroyed by the war, but now Cambodia has made remarkable progress.
He said that during his visit to Cambodia, he also met with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, so now the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen And the Prime Minister of Hungary has been successful and has achieved many remarkable results.
"Therefore, Hungary will continue to strengthen cooperation in all fields, including tourism, education, culture, and will continue to strive for people-to-people contacts, and Hungary will continue to provide more scholarships to Cambodian students," he said. Much more. ”
He also expressed the hope that Cambodia would send more students to study in Hungary, and that after graduation, students would use this knowledge to help their country. The three between the two countries also reflect the new level of relations between the two countries.
Samdech also stressed that his visit will continue to develop the relationship that the two countries have had in the past and this is not a new beginning. In particular, Samdech wants to see the main goal of economic cooperation to strengthen trade and tourism between the two countries to be more fruitful.
Samdech Techo also thanked Hungary for supporting Cambodia, but when Cambodia needed a cooperative relationship with the Hungarian Parliament, he also congratulated the success of the recent European Parliament elections, including Hungary, which Won the lottery.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also invited the President of the Hungarian Parliament to visit Cambodia again and requested a Memorandum of Understanding between the two countries' parliamentary cooperation. Hungary to attend Asia-Europe Parliamentary Meeting to be held in 2020 on the occasion of Cambodia hosting the Asia-Europe Summit.
In response, the President of the Hungarian Parliament thanked Samdech Techo for his invitation to visit Cambodia, including the invitation to attend the Asia-Europe Parliamentary Summit, and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for establishing a mechanism between the European Parliament. And the Cambodian Parliament, and in particular the drafting of a memorandum between the two parliaments to strengthen and expand cooperation between the two parliaments.
He added that the parliament as well as Hungary will continue to support Cambodia, so Hungary will continue to strengthen cooperation in all areas, including tourism, education, culture and will continue to strive for people-to-people contacts. Hungary will continue to provide more scholarships to Cambodian students. Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Hungary for providing justice to Cambodia regarding EBA
Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, said after the meeting between Samdech Techo and the President of Hungary: "Samdech Techo thanked Hungary for its support for the EBA. "What Cambodia wants is for the European Union to do justice to Cambodia."
During the important meeting, the President of Hungary welcomed Samdech Techo Hun Sen and considered that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's first official visit as Prime Minister had significantly contributed to the strengthening of bilateral relations between Cambodia and Hungary.
The President also emphasized to Samdech Techo Hun Sen that during the meeting between the two Prime Ministers, many achievements appeared, especially the signing of three agreements signed between the two countries.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the President for meeting with the President. This is his first visit as Prime Minister, but he had visited Hungary 33 years ago to strengthen ties between the two countries.
Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo stated that Hungary had helped Cambodia in 1979, which helped Cambodia during that difficult time, and when Samdech visited for the first time, he was a young foreign minister to seek support from Hungary. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that in terms of bilateral relations, we have agreed to promote cooperation in a number of areas, including: culture, education, tourism, especially education, which we have been cooperating since the 1960s. 70 and 80 so far.
Samdech Techo also emphasized that Hungary's assistance to Cambodia after 1979 was the establishment of the Cambodia-Hungary Orphanage Center to help orphans in Cambodia.
In the framework of multilateral cooperation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Hungary for supporting Cambodia in hosting the upcoming ASEAN Summit in Cambodia in 2020.
The Prime Minister also invited the President of Hungary to visit Cambodia. On behalf of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, the Prince brought greetings and wishes to the President and invited the President to visit Cambodia. He will return to Budapest, Hungary in October 2019 to attend the World Water Summit.
The President thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister, especially for bringing the wishes of the King of Cambodia and thanked His Majesty the King.
The President also accepted Samdech Techo's invitation to visit Cambodia in the near future. He emphasized that Samdech Techo's visit is to strengthen the relationship between the two countries and the opening of embassies in the two countries is an important factor in strengthening bilateral relations, especially the participation in the World Water Summit. This coming October.
The President is expected to receive Samdech Techo again in October when he attends the World Water Summit in Budapest, Hungary.
"For this World Water Summit, we have invited people from all walks of life, including business, science, education and politics, who would like to see an exhibition of technologies that address global water challenges," he said. .
At the same time, the President exchanged views with Samdech Techo Prime Minister on the challenges of climate change, especially the management of natural resources. The Prime Minister responded to the challenges of the effects of climate change affecting all countries, including Cambodia, such as: floods, droughts, typhoons and so on.
He also stressed that Cambodia and Hungary should exchange views in response to climate change.
