Discover the history of Tajikistan while Samdech Techo Hun Sen is leading a delegation to the CICA Summit there
Tajikistan, officially the Republic of Tajikistan, is a mountainous, landlocked country in Central Asia. It borders Uzbekistan, China, Afghanistan, Pakistan and Kyrgyzstan.
* Important history of Tajikistan
1991 - Former Soviet Union declares independence from Tajikistan. Rahmon Nabiyev, a communist leader, won Tajikistan's first direct presidential election with 57 percent of the vote. But in 1992, anti-government protests turned into a five-year civil war that ended.
After concluding his visit to Hungary on 14 June, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation flew to Tajikistan to attend the 5th Asia Inter-Confidence and Confidence-Building Summit (CICA) Summit. Launched on June 15, 2019 in Dushanbe.
At the summit, the Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address focusing on key issues facing the common challenges of Asia and share in-depth views on "Asia will work together to address security, economy and politics through "Strengthen trust and relations among CICA member countries."
In addition to the summit, the Prime Minister will hold bilateral talks with Tajikistan President Imo Maliramon and other heads of state / government from other member states.
The CICA is a multilateral forum aimed at promoting cooperation among its member states in areas such as peace, security and stability in Asia and the world. The conference currently has 26 permanent members, and Cambodia joined in 2011. Iran calls on US, allies to stop blaming Iran for failing to do so (Photo inside)
