Ministry of Agriculture issued a notification on the prevention and control of the epidemic of corn from new swarms
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, this new group of worms is considered to be the main pest native to South America, which can destroy more than 80 species of crops and plants, including corn, a crop that worms like to eat more. They.
In order to prevent the spread and destruction of the above new species of worms and ensure the sustainability of production and export of corn products, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to recommend to all relevant units under the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Fisheries of the capital, provinces and farmers who grow corn must cooperate to implement some of the following measures:
1: The General Department of Agriculture must plan a program to prevent and eradicate this new species of worms to be highly effective to ensure the sustainability of corn production in Cambodia.
2. The General Department of Agriculture shall research, predict the level of destruction of this new species of worm and promote crop protection measures to eradicate and prevent the spread of this new species of worm to provinces throughout the country.
3. The General Department of Agriculture shall implement integrated crop management measures, identifying the primary options of biological, physical, mechanical or agronomic measures, and implement chemical measures as a last resort in order to minimize the negative impact on humans, animals and the ecosystem. Environment.
4. The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital and Provinces shall cooperate with the General Department of Agriculture to continue to monitor and evaluate the epidemic situation of this new species of worms and to participate in the implementation of crop protection measures.
5: The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital and Provinces must pay attention to inspect and encourage farmers to inspect corn fields regularly and when there are any suspicious signs of destruction - this new species of worms must be reported. General Department of Agriculture immediately. At the same time, it is necessary to inspect and evaluate the actual damage in order to have timely remedial measures.
