Announcing the new mandate of Kampot Provincial Council, Senior Minister Cham Prasidh urges provincial councils and authorities to perform their duties effectively
(Kampot): Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister and Minister of Industry and Handicraft, on the morning of June 14, 2019, presided over the inauguration ceremony of 25 members of Kampot Provincial Council for the third mandate. Remind the councils and provincial authorities to perform their duties professionally and responsibly.
The ceremony was held at the meeting hall of Kampot Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, Mr. Chim Phalla, Chairman of the Provincial Council of the third mandate and representatives of the Ministry of Interior, provincial and district leaders, relevant units in the province. Many other distinguished guests.
On that occasion, Mr. Cham Prasidh congratulated the members of the Provincial Council, who are the representatives of the people, the members of the Commune / Sangkat Council, trusting to be elected as a member of the Preah Vihear Provincial Council for the third mandate to continue to lead. Kampot province to develop and grow in all fields.
Mr. Chim Phalla, as the Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council for the third mandate, representing all newly elected Provincial Councils, is committed to fulfilling his duties to serve the interests of the nation and the people responsibly. High and strive to strengthen the provincial administration to have the authority to manage and manage its functions effectively, transparently and accountably by complying with the principles of laws and regulations in force.
Please note that the elected council of Kampot province of the third mandate has 25 members, of which Mr. Chim Phalla was elected chairman of the provincial council. Operation to check the drug on the driver in Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, found 13 people with drugs in their body
(Kampong Cham): The Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Bureau, in cooperation with the traffic police and local authorities, continued drug control operations on the driver of a car and a truck in Batheay district, resulting in the discovery of 13 people with drugs in In the body.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that the operation was carried out in accordance with the Royal Government's 4th Anti-Drug Campaign Plan and the order of General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police. Order from Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Drug Control Commission.
The General Commissioner confirmed that this operation was carried out twice, on June 12, 2019, inspecting the water test for drugs on the driver of the truck and the workers in Batheay district, as a result of inspecting the car. Thirteen vehicles were tested, including 13 drivers, 5 drivers, 15 workers, including 4 drug addicts, 1 driver, 1 driver and 2 workers.
Separately, on June 13, 2019, the police continued to test the water for drugs on the drivers of trucks and workers in Batheay district, as a result, inspected 71 vehicles, tested a total of 140 people, 71 drivers. Twelve truck drivers, 57 workers, including 9 drug addicts, 5 drivers, 3 truck drivers and one worker.
During the two-day operation, the police also detained 5 vehicles temporarily stored at the Batheay District Police Inspectorate and sent the cases of all drug addicts to proceed with the procedure.
