(Koh Kong): Dr. Vong Sandab, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Food Reserve System Commission of Cambodia (CPRC) in cooperation with the Koh Kong Provincial Administration on the afternoon of June 13, 2019. Workshop on "Promoting the free supply of vegetable seeds and other mixed crops to farmers who need to grow vegetables" in Koh Kong province.
The seeds provided to the people include: In each family, 4 varieties, a total of 7 packages of seeds, which were studied and cultivated by Kbal Koh Station, a state station under the Ministry of Agriculture, and this vegetable is a vegetable that can be stored. Can be used again.
Dr. Vong Sandab said that with the consideration of the leadership of the provincial administration, especially the Koh Kong provincial authorities have requested seeds and provide agricultural techniques to the people. 1000 families in Sre Ambel district, Koh Kong province have just organized the workshop of the Secretariat of the Food Reserve System Commission of Cambodia.
He said that Koh Kong is the 11th province to supply seeds in a systematic manner after Kampong Thom, and as of now, the Royal Government has supplied seeds to 72 people. 633 communes with more than 250,000 families receiving seeds from more than 1 million people who have benefited from the Royal Government's programs.
Mr. Vong Sandab stated that the reason for this program was not accidental, it was due to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to encourage and help farmers. In addition to farming, mixed crops, because mixed crops allow them to get food, vegetables without having to buy in the market, and especially self-grown crops are also crops that are safe for health and can save money. Extra income.
He would like to suggest to those who participated in the workshop that after the seminar, please help to disseminate widely to those who wish to cultivate and participate in planting together for health, safety, food and development, including officials. Expertise has also been shown to be highly productive in increasing agricultural yields.
Police seize 17 kilograms of narcotics at the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Svay Rieng province while the mastermind escapes (Video inside) (Svay Rieng) 17 kilograms of drugs between the Cambodian-Vietnamese border near the Bavet International Airport, but unfortunately the suspect escaped at around 8 pm on June 13, 2019.
According to Svay Rieng provincial police, Border Patrol No. 611 patrolling the border belt at border post 170 on the left wing of the Bavet International Gate also encountered a suspect walking through a field near a wind farm with a crane. A large suitcase, with suspicion, the police called to stop for questioning, but the suspect dropped the suitcase and fled into the wind farm.
After checking the suitcase, the police found 17 pieces of white crystalline powder suspected to be amphetamines, equivalent to about 17 kilograms.
The source added that in this case, the suspect was trying to bring drugs to Vietnam, but when the police called to interrogate the suspect, he ran away. However, he is currently working with the Vietnamese side to work on the case.
Currently, 17 kilograms of drug exhibits are being kept at the Thlok border checkpoint to be processed and brought to the Svay Rieng Provincial Police.
