Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police: According to the estimated value of more than $ 300 million lost in traffic accidents per year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): General Him Yan, Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Subcommittee Second, the Road Traffic Safety Commission on June 14, 2019 confirmed that according to the annual assessment, more than $ 300 million was lost due to traffic accidents in Cambodia.
General Him Yan's statement was made on the occasion of his participation in a workshop on the consultation of the draft road safety action plan for workers held at Himawari Hotel in Phnom Penh this morning. June 14, 2019.
Speaking to the media, General Him Yan stated, "All traffic accidents with all social components, not just workers, are the first victims, then the families, then the economy. National. "Every year, according to the estimated budget, more than $ 300 million is lost due to traffic accidents (unofficial assessment)."
General Him Yan also said that some of the current workers, due to a better life, they can afford to buy self-driving vehicles, determine the fate of driving, they used to take a taxi to send destiny Their send at the driver of the car.
"Now they have a comfortable life and can afford to buy a ride to work on their own, so driving requires them to know the traffic rules and drive carefully," he said.
At the same time, General Him Yan also instructed the workers to respect the traffic law, drive at the speed limit, do not overtake at risk, wear a helmet and wear a seat belt properly, before leaving to check the vehicle properly. And must not ship overdue.
