Husband burns gas, catches fire, catches fire, causes wife to die
(Takeo): A man, due to a mental illness, used gasoline to burn his luggage, grabbed a mosquito net and a blanket in the middle of the night, but his wife saw him and ran to grab the gas bottle, causing the oil to come out of the burning bottle, causing serious injuries and he died. After being sent to Preah Kos Mead Hospital, Phnom Penh.
Separately, the husband also took a knife to commit suicide later, but did not achieve serious injuries. This incident happened at dawn on June 13, 2019 in Trakiet village, Trapeang Sap commune, Bati district, Takeo province.
Meanwhile, the husband ran away from home and only in the afternoon did the family find him sleeping in the blood block behind Phnom Tamao Zoo, using a knife to kill himself, but did not die, but was seriously injured and was hit by the group. The family was taken to Calmette Hospital for treatment.
The Chinese Ministry of Commerce said in a statement that the tariff increase on steel pipes, which Beijing believes is cheaper than the international market, will take effect on Friday with a tariff increase of 57. 9% and 147.6% on some US and EU companies.
China, one of the world's largest steel producers and consumers, already raised tariffs on steel pipes imported from the United States and the European Union by 13-14.1 percent in 2014. . However, the tariff increase expired on May 10, 2019, and the new tariff increase was made at the request of local Chinese steel pipe manufacturers.
