(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, announced that from June 15, 2019, officials of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport will start implementing hot measures by inspecting the technical characteristics of water vehicles. Goods and driver's license to Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and Phnom Penh Autonomous Port.
In an interview with reporters during a road inspection in Kampot province on June 13, 2019, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that the measures were taken to help prevent traffic accidents caused by unlicensed trucks. The technical specifications are correct or may be due to the driver not having passed the proper driving training.
The Minister confirmed that "without a valid driver's license, this is what caused the accident. So we do not sit and smoke, there are a lot of traffic accidents on the road. So go and grab at the target. ”
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, vehicles found to have not been properly inspected or the driver does not have a driver's license are not allowed to leave Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh ports.
Mr. Sun Chanthol called on all transport company owners to take the car to check the technical characteristics and check their drivers for a valid driver's license.
