Mr. Ith Sam Heng said in Switzerland that Cambodia has achieved great achievements in the field of labor after becoming a member of the ILO for 50 years.
(Geneva): The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Ith Sam Heng, addressed the 108th Session of the International Labor Conference in Geneva, Switzerland on June 13, 2019. During the 50 years that Cambodia has been a member of the ILO, Cambodia has achieved great achievements in the field of labor through its cooperation in the implementation of various projects.
The Minister said that Cambodia is the first country to successfully implement the Better Factories Cambodia (ILO-BFC) project, which has improved the lives of workers in the textile, garment and footwear sectors by linking working conditions with And international trade.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng continued that Cambodia is a leading country in implementing the decent work program in the country and is currently implementing the fifth program for 2019-2023. Cambodia has ratified the ILO's eight core conventions, incorporating these provisions into national law.
The Minister further stated that in 2017, the Royal Government of Cambodia established the "National Commission for Monitoring the Implementation of the International Labor Convention, which Cambodia has ratified", a tripartite mechanism in line with the ILO Monitoring Mechanism to monitor and promote implementation. Effective.
Minister Ith Sam Heng added that Cambodia has been implementing a roadmap on the implementation of professional freedom in accordance with ILO recommendations.
According to Minister Ith Sam Heng, Cambodia is also recognized as a leading country in expanding social protection through the introduction of a national social protection framework, which is planned to launch a pension system for workers in 2019.
At the 108th International Labor Conference, Cambodia asks international partners to continue to help develop employment and vocational training
(Geneva): On the occasion of addressing the 108th Session of the International Conference on Labor in Geneva, Switzerland on June 13, 2019, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, requested the international partners in particular. The ILO would like to continue to help develop employment and vocational training in Cambodia in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
On that occasion, Minister Ith Sam Heng said, "While some types of work have been changing in the process of technological development and the Industrial Revolution 4.0, Cambodia believes that all parties involved will join Cambodia to put in place. "Measures and solutions to potential challenges in the job market and future jobs for all citizens."
Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that in order to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals, especially the eighth goal "decent work" in the context of the fourth generation industrial revolution, ILO member countries need to ensure that workers and youth have access to education. General and quality technical and vocational training and the opportunity for lifelong learning to acquire a skill that can meet the needs of the local and regional labor market.
In this regard, ILO member states should focus on increasing the professional capacity of the workforce, increasing productivity, narrowing the skills gap, strengthening labor market information and employment services, and improving the quality of education and vocational training to maximize benefits. And to reduce the negative impact of changes in the world of work and to respond to future skills needs.
Cambodia hopes that the ILO's founding principles, which focus on tripartite mechanisms and social dialogue, will achieve a one-century statement that clearly defines the role and mission of the ILO at the beginning of its second century. Decent, productive work for everyone.
Minister Ith Sam Heng expressed confidence that the ILO will continue to play an important role and as a tripartite body that will make a significant contribution to turning the challenges that have been happening in the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution into Brilliant job opportunities for everyone without giving up on anyone.
