In this meeting, Dr. Ng Eng Hen reaffirmed the close relationship between the two countries in the field of defense. He also thanked Cambodia for always supporting Singapore in organizing international events. He reiterated that the two countries' defense ministries will continue to work together to maintain peace and stability in the region.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet said that peace and stability are factors that promote rapid development, in fact, due to the peace and stability of the last 20 years, Cambodia has developed so rapidly in the ASEAN region. Peace and stability are the driving forces for the region to continue to develop and prosper. The lieutenant general believes that this visit is a continuation of the friendship between the two countries, the army and the people in the future.
The Lt. Gen. thanked Mr. Dith and key Singaporean leaders for their warm welcome and for sharing their views and experiences on some important issues. Through these dialogues, it is confirmed that the consistency and will of Cambodia and Singapore in strengthening and expanding relations between the two countries both now and in the future.
(Phnom Penh): The case of fire at an engine oil storage place near Doeum Thkov market roundabout in Sangkat Toul Tum Poung 2, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh has been completely extinguished at around 4 pm on June 13, 2019. Authorities intervened to put out the blaze.
