Materials and exhibits must be stored at the Environmental Office for legal action. Cambodian investors set up Earth Sign Natural Fertilizer Plant to supply domestically and export!
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the need for using natural fertilizers in Cambodia, Cambodian investors have set up a natural fertilizer factory called "Earth Fertilizer" to supply demand in Cambodia and export to foreign countries. In the past, it relied entirely on imports from Japan.
Mr. Chan Vannak, General Director of Japan Earth Sign Natural Fertilizer Company, said at the press conference on June 13, 2019 that "Earth Sign Natural Fertilizer Factory was established two years ago in collaboration with the team. Work in Cambodia and team from Japan. "The company produces an average of 200 tons of fertilizer per day and about 100,000 tons a year."
He added that in the past, Earth Sign natural fertilizer was imported from Japan, but after receiving support from customers, we have set up a factory and have a partner from Japan to set up a factory in Cambodia.
Mr. Chan Vannak added, “Apart from domestic supply, the company also exports natural earth fertilizer made in Cambodia to be distributed in Burma. "This fertilizer export is a positive point for Cambodia, which was previously just a country that imports products, but now becomes a country that produces and exports to other countries."
He said that in addition to exporting to Myanmar, Earth Sign Natural Fertilizer Company plans to export to other countries, including Laos, Vietnam, the Philippines and Malaysia.
(Phnom Penh): By now, the Japanese-funded public bus (blue) has been in Phnom Penh for a year. On the occasion of the one-year anniversary of the bus donation, Mr. Hidehisa Horinouchi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, encouraged Cambodians to use this public bus for safety and comfort.
Please be informed that at present, there are 190 buses of Phnom Penh Capital Administration and 7 routes are traveling, while the number of people traveling by this bus per day has increased to more than 10,000 people.
According to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, on September 28, 2018, announced the modification of 7 existing bus lanes and the addition of 4 new lanes to a total of 11 lanes to expand the scope of Transportation of the Autonomous Authority, public transport, buses, as well as facilitate the travel of people in the capital.
According to the announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, the revision of the old lane and the revision of the new lane will start on October 1, 2018, as Japan has provided assistance to 41 vehicles. At the same time, by the end of 2018, 39 more buses, a total of 80 with Japanese assistance, will arrive in Cambodia.
