Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, expressed his anger and announced that the company would improve and rebuild the road, otherwise the Ministry would not accept it. The senior minister's reaction came when he visited the road in person on June 13, 2019 and saw the damage to the road with his own eyes.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to authorize a foreign company to rehabilitate and rehabilitate 54.30 km of National Road No. 3 between km 147 + 100 to km 201 + 400 at the Veal Renh roundabout at a cost of approximately 12 million USD. This section of road is repaired and improved by AC paving.
This section of the road started repairing and improvement in February 2018 and is scheduled to be completed in August 2019. To date, over 67% of repairs and improvements have been completed.
But sadly, as the section of road was nearing completion, the road at some points gradually began to deteriorate and the company began to touch the damaged area, which made the Minister of Public Works and Transport angry and dissatisfied with the repair. And improve this stretch of road.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated, "The Ministry of Public Works and Transport does not accept the quality of the road from Kampot to Veal Renh." "A lot of damage, wrong technical characteristics, sometimes damaged and can not be touched properly."
The Minister ordered the company to inspect, repair and renovate, otherwise the Ministry will not sign to accept this road. Mr. Sun Chanthol also warned that if the company continues to build such poor quality roads, the Ministry will blacklist companies not to participate in road construction in Cambodia.
With this case, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also asked for understanding and tolerance from the people. He promised to monitor the repair process of this road to be quality and correct to the standard. The chicken slaughterhouse in Sangkat Toul Sangke II, Khan Russey Keo, which smells and disturbs the people, continues to operate despite the order of the Phnom Penh Governor to close
(Phnom Penh): Police at the Prek Pnov Police Inspectorate's Kork Roka Post, in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, arrested a man who hit his uncle with a machete in the middle of his head, causing him to faint. Bleeding to death.
Colonel Chhin Kim Thuy, police inspector of Prey Knov Pnov district, said that the suspect was immediately detained by the police at the point in front of the house No. 1 in Andong village, Kork Roka commune, Prek Pnov district at 15:50. Morning, June 12, 2019.
Prek Pnov District Inspector further stated that according to the explanation around the scene, combined with the actual examination by the force of the Office of Science and Technology of Dr. Oknha Dr. Nong Sovannaroth and after the arrest of his nephew to be interrogated a few hours later, they answered He admitted that he took a corner stick from his uncle and hit his uncle, causing his death.
Police confirmed that before the incident, the victim got off his tuk-tuk and picked up a corner stick and walked towards the suspect, while the suspect grabbed the corner stick from his uncle and attacked his uncle. The left side of the head causes bleeding and fainting.
After beating his uncle, the suspect's nephew hid a corner stick under the bed and hid in the house without running. After the incident, the victim's wife, who was the suspect's aunt, reported to the police in cooperation with the specialized office to besiege and arrest the suspect as a nephew.
The inspector said that the suspect in the murder was Heng Chan Sophal, 28, a homemaker (paralyzed). The victim was an uncle named Kem Kirivuth, 44 years old, a Cambodian who runs a tuk-tuk. Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Meets with Human Rights Officials to Understand the Process of Land Allocation for Social Affairs and Economic Development Phase II
