Discover the history of Hungary where Samdech Techo Hun Sen is on an official visit
Hungary is a country in the middle of Europe (Central Europe) and has no borders with the sea. Hungary was under the Ottoman and Habsburg colonies until the 16th century and became an independent country after World War I, adhering to the communist regime for decades before becoming a liberal and democratic republic. As a member of the European Union as it is now.
Hungary's GDP per capita ranks 52nd, with a per capita income of $ 15,923 per year. Hungary's economy, on the other hand, relies heavily on sectors such as mining, electronics, textiles and information technology.
Hungary became a member of NATO in 1999 and the European Union in 2004, as well as a member of the United Nations and the World Bank. Please say no to drugs! Nationwide drug crackdown for June 13: 33 cases cracked, 63 arrested
