Embassy: Filipinos can enter Cambodia for 30 days without a visa (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Philippine Embassy in Phnom Penh on June 13, 2019 issued a notice on the first 30 days of residence permit. In Cambodia, visa-free visas are required for Filipinos with regular passports.
According to the statement, Filipinos who wish to stay in Cambodia for more than 60 days should apply for a visa upon arrival in Cambodia to avoid any inconvenience. .
However, according to Tho Samnang, Deputy Director General of Legal Affairs and Consular Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Cambodia has indeed changed the 21-day visa waiver to more than 30 days, but no An additional 30 days are allowed. He suspects the Philippine embassy may be mistaken for an additional 30 days.
Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that Cambodia's favor on the Filipino people was a compromise on behalf of the same ASEAN member.
"My first response was to establish a common coordination point in ASEAN member countries to remind everyone that we are building a community to have fewer visa restrictions," he said. "
Please note that regarding the 30-day visa waiver, apart from the Philippines, Cambodia is implementing with some other countries in the ASEAN region such as Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, Laos and Vietnam.
