Phnom Penh Governor Leads Officials and Authorities to Inspect Canal Rehabilitation and Drainage to Release Water North of Phnom Penh International Airport
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, this morning, June 13, 2019, led the relevant departments, authorities and professional officers of Phnom Penh Capital Administration to inspect the condition of the construction of the open canal in the area north of the International Airport. Phnom Penh, Sangkat Kakap I, Kakap II, Khan Por Sen Chey and Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, while the area is still facing flooding due to heavy rains.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that in order to alleviate the flooding in the rainy season, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration under the guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng decided to restore canals and sewers to release water. Rain fell from some areas in Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Sangkat Kakap 1, Sangkat Kakap 2 and another in Sen Sok district.
In order for the process of rehabilitation and drainage to be smooth and complete according to the plan and according to the technical specifications, the Governor of Phnom Penh also led professional officers and local authorities to check the actual situation.
During the inspection, it was found that some unregulated houses were built in violation of the canal. Regarding this issue, Mr. Khuong Sreng advised the local authorities to make a notice to the people to remove their houses from the ditch so that professional officials as well as specialized departments can easily restore the canal.
Separately, a factory in Trapeang Chrey village was instructed by the Governor of Phnom Penh to urge the local authorities to install a 2-meter sewer to replace the old 8-foot sewer with a length of 200 meters, connected to the canal of Chamkar Ovulk village. In addition, the Capital Administration must install a 2-meter-long drain with a length of 1,170 meters.
At the same time, the Governor called on the people to cooperate with local authorities and specialized departments to address the impact of the construction of projects in their localities to facilitate the construction.
