Preah Vihear provincial governor tells officials not to use their power to solve problems and to serve the people in a transparent and efficient manner
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on June 13, 2019, instructed officials at all levels not to use their power to solve problems, to use laws to solve problems, and especially to serve the people in a transparent manner. Effective and acceptable.
This instruction was made on the occasion of the inauguration of the OWSO and People's Office in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province on the morning of June 13, 2019. This.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the OWSO, which was inaugurated now, is the third building to appear in the Preah Vihear provincial administrative framework. Initially, we had a One-Stop-Shop in Preah Vihear City and then moved on to establish a One-Stop-Shop of the Provincial Administration, and in 2019, the One-Stop-Shop in Rovieng District came into being. Guidance of the Ministry of Interior.
He said that seeing this problem, the Royal Government reformed the decentralization and co-operation and demanded that all ministries and institutions delegate functions to the sub-national administration so that the sub-national administration has the right to manage these functions in accordance with the needs. And citizen requests. To reduce the time and reduce the cost and get a satisfactory service back.
Mr. Un Chanda also advised officials to make efforts to provide services to all people is transparent, efficient and reliable. At the same time, he also instructed the officials to try to solve all the problems that arise and the solution is not to use power, but to follow the law, to check the facts and the law clearly to make the parties Both conflicts are acceptable.
