(Phnom Penh): More than 10 Nepalese tour companies have organized a meeting with tour operators in Cambodia under the auspices of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents (CATA) to promote tourism in both countries. There is also confirmation of a study on direct flights from Nepal to Cambodia.
On the occasion of participating in the above program, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of CATA, stated that this program is designed for Cambodian and Nepalese tour operators to understand and establish cooperation with each other in order to promote the tourism potential of the two countries.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin said that Cambodia-Nepal has many similarities, such as respect for Buddhism, traditions, customs of the people and rich in cultural and historical sites.
She added that the number of Cambodian tourists visiting Nepal and from Nepal to Cambodia is still small, which is why the Nepalese side is studying to open direct flights to Cambodia as soon as possible to promote. The number of tourists coming to both countries is increasing.
Ghana Sayam, Secretary of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of Nepal, said that Nepal has many tourist attractions that have not been promoted to Cambodia, but now he believes that Cambodian tour operators will be very interested in bringing tourists. From Cambodia to Nepal, and for Nepal will also promote Cambodian tourist destinations to its people as well.
"The key point for Cambodia and Nepal to continue is to promote direct flights as soon as possible," said the secretary of the Nepal Ministry of Culture and Tourism.
It should be noted that the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Federal Republic of Nepal established diplomatic relations in 1964, but it was not until September 7, 1999 that the two countries re-established diplomatic ties. Missed by the war in Cambodia.
During the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to Nepal, Cambodia and Nepal signed an agreement on direct flight cooperation in the near future.
800 pump wells in Tbong Khmum province with grant from Indian government inaugurated today
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Try Meng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, on behalf of Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, this morning, June 13, 2019, participated in the handover ceremony of 800 Afridev wells under a grant. From the Government of the Republic of India in Tbong Khmum Province.
During the ceremony, Mr. Try Meng stated that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, has achieved great success in all areas, including the economy, society and culture, which has transformed from a middle-income country. Low to middle income countries.
Mr. Try Meng added, "Cambodia is ranked as the fifth largest developing country in achieving the Millennium Development Goals and the first in the Asia-Pacific region to achieve good progress." "Better to improve social indicators."
The Ministry of Rural Development, as a staff of the Royal Government, has successfully implemented the Strategic Plan for Rural Development 2014-2018, bringing about positive changes in living conditions, health, sanitation and other public services in harmony in the family society. Rural areas. Many of the activities that the Ministry of Rural Development has implemented include:
1: Construction of new roads, concrete bridges, roundabouts, all kinds of corner drains, annual maintenance of rural roads, regular improvement of pavement from red gravel to two-story rubber road, rehabilitation of flood-damaged rural roads, construction of safe havens for Prevent flood disasters.
2. The supply of clean water, education, health and hygiene to improve the living conditions of rural people in order to achieve the vision of the Royal Government, which states that "by 2025, all people in rural communities must have "Adequate water supply and sanitation and living in a hygienic environment."
3. Provide jobs, businesses, small enterprises and many other economic activities to change the living conditions of rural people for the better.
Taking this opportunity to ensure the management and effective use of long-term and good hygiene, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development would like to make the following suggestions:
* Project officials and all stakeholders, please promote the management and maintenance of wells that have been built in accordance with the conditions and technical validity.
* Please advise the management and professional officers of the project to continue to work together to fulfill the task even more to provide all wells in the project on time to the people with good quality.
According to the report of Mr. Sok Sophally, Deputy Director of Rural Water Supply Department of the Ministry of Rural Development and Project Director, the project has decided to build and provide 800 wells as the first step to the people in Memot Tbong Khmum and Wedges in Tbong Khmum province.
