According to the announcement of the National Assembly on the results of the Standing Committee meeting on June 13, 2019, which was received by Fresh News, the six agendas that the National Assembly will discuss and approve at the plenary session of the National Assembly are as follows: Next:
1: Decision on the validity of the mandate of Mr. Sok Pheng as a Member of Parliament for Prey Veng Province.
2. Discussion and approval of the draft law on the management of oil and petroleum products.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of Bangladesh on the promotion and mutual protection of investment.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates on the promotion and mutual protection of investment.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Turkey on the promotion and mutual protection of investment.
Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the agreement on the establishment of an international network for bamboo and rattan.
Please note that for today's meeting of the National Assembly Standing Committee, the agenda is as follows:
1. The meeting approved the request to recognize Mr. Sok Pheng as the new Member of Parliament for Prey Veng Province to replace Mr. Pov Samy who passed away. The announcement of the validity of the mandate of Mr. Sok Pheng as a member of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature will be made in the upcoming second session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature.
3. The meeting approved and handed over the draft law on the approval of the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 to the Committee on Investment Planning, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources of the National Assembly for review and report to the Standing Committee of the National Assembly.
4. The meeting approved to include in the agenda of the 2nd session of the National Assembly the 6th legislature the draft law on the management of oil and petroleum products.
5: The meeting approved the resumption date of the second session of the National Assembly, 6th legislature, on Monday morning, June 17, 2019 at 8:00 AM.
