(Phnom Penh): One More Restaurant has been serving Khmer food to customers for more than 10 years. In addition to taking care of all the needs of customers, the restaurant also does not forget to consider the staff who have worked hard both physically and mentally to refine, cook and serve the perfect service to its customers.
On the afternoon of June 12, 2019, One More Restaurant held a signing ceremony for the purchase of life insurance services for 30 employees who renewed their employment contracts with the restaurant from 5 to 10 years. The event was held in person at One More Restaurant, located at # 37, Street 315, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
On this occasion, Mr. Nal Sinath, General Manager of One More Restaurant, said that the active participation of employees is very important to drive this business to run today and continue for decades to come.
He added that in order to compensate for the efforts of employees and their entire families to avoid risks, the restaurant has decided to buy life insurance for employees who have renewed their employment contracts with restaurants from 5. 30 to 10 years with the following benefits:
* First: Receive $ 4,000 compensation in case of death or complete and permanent disability that is not caused by accident * Second: Receive $ 8,000 compensation in case of death or complete and permanent disability Caused by accident
* Third: Receive an annual income benefit of $ 400 after an accident occurs until the term of the policy.
* Fourth: No need to pay insurance premiums in case of accident * Fifth: Receive a savings of $ 4,000
