It should be noted that Cambodia and Hungary established official diplomatic relations with each other on August 20, 1956. This relationship was severed during the Khmer Rouge regime and re-established in 1979.
Through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's current visit to Hungary, the relationship and cooperation between the two countries will be further enhanced.
Please be informed that in the sixth trip abroad for 2019, after concluding his visit to Hungary on June 14, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation will fly to Tajikistan to attend the conference. The 5th Asia Interaction and Confidence-Building Summit (CICA) was held on 15 June 2019 in Dushanbe.
The CICA is a multilateral forum aimed at promoting cooperation among its member states in areas such as peace, security and stability in Asia and the world. The conference currently has 26 permanent members, and Cambodia joined in 2011.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia, in the presence of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia, organized a workshop on "The role of the Central Bank in the current situation" with the participation of about 400 participants.
The purpose of this workshop is to provide internal training to the staff of the National Bank of Cambodia to share information, updates and new knowledge related to the Central Bank, especially to understand the mission and work direction of the National Bank in a consistent manner in the context of change. Rapid integration of finance and regional and global integration.
The workshop was attended by Mr. Som Sannith, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, on "Reforming the Framework and Mechanism of Supervision of Banking and Financial Institutions Based on Risks and Future Perspectives."
There was also a presentation by Mr. Khu Vuthy, Deputy Technical Director General on "Functions and Roles of Central Banks of Countries Around the World", especially in the developed countries in the Eurozone.
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has always strived to fulfill its main functions and responsibilities, such as: the monetary policy authority, the authorities and the guardians, overseeing the banking system, the authority developing the payment system, especially the core task of maintaining price stability.
In addition to these key roles, the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has paid more attention to its functions and responsibilities, such as: public relations policy to strengthen trust, raise financial awareness, and promote the financial environment in line with significant developments. Rapid technology and changes in regional and global economic integration.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia has strengthened its framework for overseeing banking and financial institutions, with a particular focus on risk and future prospects, in line with the international practice of the Basel Principles on the Supervision of Banking and Financial Institutions. The objective is to ensure a healthy banking system and financial stability, contributing to the development of the national economy.
