Representatives of Mekong countries and experts from some countries hold a meeting to discuss the future vision of the Mekong River to help reduce poverty for the people
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of Mekong countries, including experts from the United States, China, South Korea and India, held a meeting on June 13, 2019 to discuss issues related to the future outlook of the Mekong River to find solutions to participate. Reduce poverty for the people.
Uncle Sothyrak, Director of the Khmer Institute for Cooperation and Peace (CICP), who organized the discussion, said: "In areas such as the economy, society and defense, to discuss and exchange from other challenges to development to poverty reduction for the people."
He also said that the one-and-a-half-day discussion meeting will also study how to reduce poverty for the people at the grassroots level so that they can get special benefits. Along the Mekong River as well.
At the same time, Mr. Sothyra added that for the comments that the representatives of the participating countries, as well as experts today will also want to document for dissemination to politicians or leaders of the country. Which is not just for Cambodia.
"We consider our involvement with the Mekong region as an integral part of our strategy for the Indo-Pacific region and of our joint efforts to support ASEAN, including through the ASEAN Integration Initiative," he said. "The aim is to narrow the development gap between ASEAN countries and promote regional unity."
He stressed that our strategy for the Mekong region follows the principles that have been the foundation of prosperity throughout the Indo-Pacific region for decades, which is at the heart of our regional strategy: commitment to sovereignty, transparency, and good governance. A core and a system based on customary law with respect to international law.
Senior Minister Kun Kim urges Oddar Meanchey Provincial Council to monitor the performance of officials for the benefit of the people
(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Assistance Team, reminded the new Oddar Meanchey Provincial Council officials to work hard to perform their duties effectively, especially to monitor and promote the performance of provincial governors and officials. In Oddar Meanchey province, to strengthen for the better development of the province and bring benefits to the people in this province of the former battlefield.
The promotion and reminder of the performance of the provincial councilors was made during the inauguration ceremony of the new mandate of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Council this morning, June 13, 2019.
Oddar Meanchey is a province far from Phnom Penh on the Thai border. The province, which last closed in 1998, has a total of 19 provincial councilors, with Siprasit as chairman.
Speaking at the ceremony, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Mr. Kun Kim joined in congratulating, appreciating and highly appreciating all the provincial councils that were represented by the people, namely the Commune / Sangkat Councilors who gave their trust and were elected as members of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Council. Third mandate to continue to lead Oddar Meanchey province to continue to develop in all areas.
Mr. Kun Kim reminded the provincial council that as an elected council member, although composed of different political parties, in principle, the council is representative of the people of Oddar Meanchey province as a whole.
He said that whether sub-national councils are elected directly or indirectly, sub-national councils are part of the executive branch and have autonomy within the limits of the rules and regulations in force. Manage its local affairs to meet the needs of the people in its jurisdiction.
"Therefore, in carrying out the work of His Excellency, Lok Chumteav as a member of the council, we must strive to serve the interests and needs of all people fairly and fairly, regardless of political affiliation." This is the confirmation and reminder of Mr. Kun Kim.
On that occasion, Mr. Kun Kim also instructed the council of the third mandate to cooperate with the provincial board of governors to implement the work of high priority work for 2019. The main tasks that Mr. Kun Kim instructed the new provincial council to carry out after the announcement of the inauguration are:
1: Go to the meeting to announce the inauguration of the municipal council and shall hold the first ordinary meeting and the second ordinary meeting as scheduled.
2: Need to prepare a development plan for 5 years, continue to participate in the implementation of various reform programs of the Royal Government, such as (promoting relations and accountability between the Board of Governors and sub-national level with the people), continue to promote the transfer of functions and Budget resources to sub-national administrations to promote transparency and accountability.
4: Encourage people from all walks of life to participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes.
