Senior health official: Cambodia's health sector is not as weak as they say
"If the health sector is really bad, you should check that the average life expectancy of the Cambodian people may not be as long as the international average of about 70 years, both men and women," she explained. Women who have many other factors that motivate our people to live so long.
This statement was made by Dr. O Vandin on the occasion of the official inauguration of Akhit Koh Pich Hospital and attended by Mr. Ma Emerson, Executive Director of Akhit Koh Pich Hospital, Prof. Dr. Ek Mengly, Co-Founder Akit Koh Pich Hospital and many honored guests on the morning of June 12, 2019.
"In this sense, I want to emphasize that the health sector is not all bad, inactivity is in a small number of places, while a large number are good," she said.
She said that, like Akhit Hospital, it was a hospital set up by Cambodian children, plus a team of doctors with experience in modern technology similar to neighboring countries. Public hospitals are also evolving into modern technologies such as Calmette Hospital, Preah Kosam Hospital and Preah Ang Duong Hospital, which are very crowded.
"I would like to congratulate Akit Koh Pich Hospital on its official opening in Cambodia now and wish Akit Hospital success," she added.
Dr. Ek Mengly also expressed his excitement at the opening of the Archive Koh Pich Hospital. The doctor is determined that Akhit Koh Pich Hospital will provide the best service to all patients, focusing on quality and good service.
She added, "Koh Pich Orchid Hospital was established in accordance with the health regulations of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia. Although Koh Pich Orchid Hospital has just started to operate, in the short term, the medical team has helped many families with special gifts with the smiles of parents by helping to give birth to their children. They are safe and healthy. ”
"I sincerely hope and believe that Orchid Koh Pich Hospital will receive the support of the people of Cambodia by providing highly professional health care services with a focus on good results," she said. "Because there are sufficient human resources, equipment and modern equipment to provide health services to customers."
She added that Akit Koh Pich Hospital provides many services, including: 1: Obstetrics, focusing on natural childbirth and caesarean section, 2: Gynecology, with examination and treatment of all women's problems, 3: Pediatric examination, focusing on the rescue of newborns and children with health problems, 4: General medicine and many other services.
The doctor stated that the hospital is also equipped with modern equipment to treat patients quickly, plus doctors are all highly experienced and clear in this field.
"Currently, Koh Pich Orchid Hospital has nearly 70 staff members and continues to play key roles in Obstetrics and Gynecology, ENT, ENT, General Medicine, Laboratory, Pharmacist and Management. In general.
