(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of Cambodian Children's Day, International Children's Day, June 1, 2019 and the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has set out a number of measures to achieve the goal of ending child labor by 2025. This day was presided over by Ms. Soeng Sor Socheata, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor on June 12, 2019 at the Ministry of Labor.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has made Cambodia one of the top five countries in the world in eliminating child labor and having better working conditions, a clear policy against child labor, and a moderate leader in Among the 13 leading countries in the world in progress against child labor.
At the same time, in order to achieve the Global Sustainable Development Goals (2015-2030), which stipulates the end of child labor by 2025, the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken measures and is committed to:
* Continue to strengthen law enforcement and labor inspection mechanisms and cooperate with employers 'and employers' organizations to resolve child labor disputes and occupational safety in a timely manner, especially to encourage employers to comply with labor standards and severe penalties for enterprises that use child labor.
* Expand cross-sectoral cooperation and find appropriate solutions to the problem of multidisciplinary child labor to ensure the best interests of Cambodian children and build human capital in line with appropriate work contexts.
* Encourage all stakeholders to work together to ensure occupational safety for young workers and call on the public to report cases of child labor in the workplace. At the same time, advising parents and employers on cases of child labor abuse, especially domestic workers, is a criminal offense to reduce the use of the most serious forms of child labor.
* Seek the support of resources and techniques to research and compile declarations related to child labor of recent economic activities and campaigns towards the end of child labor at the commune level.
In response to the elimination of all forms of child labor, Ms. Seng Sor Socheata offers the following recommendations:
1. The National Committee Against Child Labor (NCCP) must continue to coordinate the implementation of international conventions and national policies related to child labor, especially in cooperation with inter-ministerial institutions to promote the implementation of the National Action Plan on the Reduction of Child Labor and Elimination of the most serious forms of child labor in 2016-2025.
2: General Secretariat of the NEC And the Department of Skills must work to strengthen effective labor inspection measures to prevent occupational accidents and health vulnerabilities for young workers in order to eliminate child labor, especially to expand the scope of employment in the erratic economy, such as domestic workers, handicrafts and other services.
3. Continue training to strengthen the capacity of all stakeholders and mobilize financial resources and seek public support to participate in the fight against child labor.
4. Expand awareness and campaigns against child labor and forced labor to localities and communities to prevent the use of child labor.
5. Strengthen core interventions to save child labor and prohibit forced labor by type of occupation, and increase cooperation between ministries, institutions and stakeholders to prevent the use of child labor in all its forms.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls on Journalists to Strengthen the Implementation of the Law on Professional Ethics to Avoid Fraudulent Information, Insulting and Creating Social Insecurity (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia All media outlets must respect the law and professional ethics of journalism and refrain from publishing fake news, inciting anger and creating social insecurity.
The call of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made at the opening ceremony of the 16th Asia Press Summit on Digitalization of Emerging Media Focusing on Emerging Markets, held in Siem Reap this morning, June 12, 2019.
Addressing more than 500 journalists from more than 40 countries in Asia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made a recommendation to them to jointly increase cooperation to prevent information fraud and cybercrime through the media. Dissemination of real information to neutralize fake information.
Samdech stated that journalists must strengthen the implementation of the law, professional ethics, avoid spreading false information, resentment, insults, incitement to anger, hatred, discrimination, inter-ethnic conflict, religion or exaggerate the facts. To have social insecurity.
At the same time, Samdech Techo also called on all journalists to strengthen close cooperation to resolve media disputes that cause chaos and affect the use of digital technology.
Please note that Cambodia is now the host of the 16th Asian Press Summit in Siem Reap.
The Asia Press Summit is a leading international event in the field of audio-visual, providing opportunities for information ministers, audio-visual operators and media staff, industry leaders, universities, researchers, experts and policymakers around the world. He met to discuss the development of the quality of the media and to address challenges during the technological revolution.
