While China and India are embroiled in a trade dispute with the United States, Beijing has called for solidarity with the New Delhi government in order to combat the unilateral and protectionist policies that Washington is using to put pressure on the United States. Other countries since Donald Trump was elected President of the United States in late 2016 to the present.
On Tuesday, US President Donald Trump reiterated that Washington was ready to raise tariffs on Chinese imports following the G20 summit in Japan in late June. Negotiations with China have not progressed. But Beijing has also announced that it will retaliate if the United States raises tariffs on Chinese goods.
Turning to India, the United States last week announced that past tariff preferences on goods from India, Asia's third-largest economy and the world's sixth-largest, would no longer exist. This has led India to be deeply concerned about the impact on the economy as more than 200 million of India's 1.34 billion people (2017 figures) are still living in extreme poverty.
