Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the opening of the 16th "Asia Press" Summit
(Siem Reap): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of Wednesday, June 12, 2019, officially presided over the opening ceremony of the "Asia Press" Summit. The 16th held at Sokha Hotel in Siem Reap.
The following are the key words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was pleased to attend the opening ceremony of the 16th RUSC Summit on Digital Media Digitalization, focusing on emerging markets.
* The Prime Minister praised the leadership and officials at all levels of the Ministry of Information for collaborating with the Pacific Media Development Institute to organize this important conference.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that digital technology has replaced the potential use of analog technology to improve quality and efficiency such as sound, image, data transmission speed, data storage, saving on radio waves, reducing production costs. Increasing rich productivity.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that digital technology has made the management of the country a digital government in increasing the digital economy activities, improving the quality and efficiency of public services with accountability, transparency and connectivity, internal and global communication. As a whole.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that along with the positive effects, the digital technology of the media has provided various disadvantages that put the world at risk of fraudulent information, incitement to anger, insults, hatred and cybercrime.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the negative effects of digital technology, such as hacking and destruction of public documents, online extortion, and the violation of individual rights, have been threatening regional and global security.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all parties concerned must work together to increase closer cooperation in bilateral, regional and global frameworks to combat fraudulent information and cybercrime.
Samdech Techo stated that at the recent EU-EU summit in Brussels, all European countries have raised concerns about information fraud and information technology crime today.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for jointly promoting regional and global cooperation to exchange information, experience, technological development and the construction of physical infrastructure to take advantage of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the creation of digital technology opportunities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for joint cooperation to prevent fraudulent information and information technology crimes through the media through the dissemination of factual information to neutralize fraudulent information.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, calls for strengthening the implementation of the law on professional ethics, avoiding the dissemination of false information, resentment, insults, incitement to anger, resentment, discrimination, incitement to inter-ethnic, religious or exaggerated information. Create social insecurity.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for closer cooperation to resolve media disputes that cause chaos and affect the use of digital technology.
* Samdech Techo called for joint attention to increase technical and professional understanding to keep up with market demand, the development of media technology and the evolution of the global situation.
* Samdech Techo calls on stakeholders to work together to turn traditional media into a smart and flexible system based on the realities and developments of modern technology to meet market competition in the digital age.
* Samdech Techo calls for joint development of policies, strategic frameworks, legal regulations for the media and digital security standards regulations, which are essential for the management of data security in business, electronic payments and cyber security. To combat fraudulent information and cybercrime.
* Samdech Techo hopes that this conference will actively discuss the opportunities of digital technology, challenges and cooperation, partnerships, the fight against fraudulent information, methods for solving problems arising from the Fourth Industrial Revolution in the spirit. Contribute to regional and global socio-economic development with sustainable and lasting peace.
Addressing several government representatives at the United Nations on the afternoon of June 11, 2019, as a State Party to the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, Mr. Em Chanmakara represented Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. Cambodia has been investing in the disability sector for many years.
Cambodia is on the right track to develop the country, especially to ensure peace, political stability and economic growth as opportunities to promote the rights of people with disabilities, especially the provision of social land concessions and support for physical rehabilitation for the people. Disabled. "Mr. Em Chanmakara said this on the occasion of leading the Cambodian delegation to the 12th session of the States Parties to the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities."
The promotion of disability and economic growth in Cambodia is considered to be an incentive policy strongly encouraged by the Cambodian government. The government has vowed to recruit 2% of people with disabilities to work in ministry ministries. "This is an additional statement of Mr. Em Chanmakara"!
Speaking at this important conference, Mr. Em Chanmakara said that for inclusive education, Cambodia has published books for students with disabilities in both tactile and sign language at all levels. People with disabilities have access to equitable quality education and opportunities for lifelong learning.
Mr. Em Chanmakara continued that in order to provide the highest health standards for people with disabilities, Cambodia has established a social protection policy framework, which will continue to implement community-based allowance programs for people with disabilities, focusing on people with disabilities. Who is a family member with a poor card.
People with disabilities receive free health care and treatment from public hospitals and receive financial support for food and travel expenses during treatment. Every year, Cambodia produces 28,000 high quality accessories for our disabled people free of charge.
Overall, Cambodia has made significant progress in the field of disability, building a collective society in response to improving the welfare of people with disabilities, a government effort in line with the implementation of the 2030 Agenda.
Singapore Foreign Minister: Cambodia-Singapore must work together to maintain security and stability in the region
The statement by the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Singapore was made on the occasion that he allowed Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander of the Cambodian Army, to pay a courtesy call and discuss work at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Singapore afternoon, June 11, 2019.
"Singapore and Cambodia are old friends and have mutually beneficial relations," said Dr. Vivian Balakrishnan. "The two countries must cooperate both at the bilateral level and on behalf of ASEAN members to maintain security and stability in the region."
In response, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet supported the comments of the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Singapore, emphasizing the importance of relations between the two countries in maintaining security and stability in the region.
The Commander of the Cambodian Army added that the ASEAN Community must remain united for the development, growth, prosperity and sustainability of the region. The lieutenant general said that the visit will further strengthen the ties between the two countries.
