(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on June 12, 2019, issued a strict order strictly prohibiting the use of law enforcement forces to protect recreational areas. Especially karaoke clubs and casinos.
The head of the Ministry of Interior emphasized that the use of force to guard the area was completely illegal and that what was even more wrong was that all the entertainment venues embedding drug use was a serious crime. At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also said that the Ministry of Interior will issue a directive not to allow this to happen.
In this regard, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng encouraged all karaoke clubs or entertainment venues to use more private security agencies, while currently private security agencies also receive training from the National Police.
It should be informed that the order of the head of the Ministry of Interior was made after some time ago, the prince noticed that the law enforcement forces still had some problems, allowing the law enforcement forces to protect the karaoke clubs and Casinos and so on.
It should also be noted that the General Commission of the National Police, which is staffed by the Department of Private Security Management under the leadership of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department, has opened a series of training courses for all private security agencies that are serving in Cambodia to promote. This sector to be more effective.
Minister of Culture: ICC-Angkor has been doing well and is a model for the world for 25 years
(Siem Reap): In an interview with the media about the International Committee for the Coordination of Protection and Development of the Angkor Historic Site (ICC-Angkor), Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts and Chairman of the APSARA Authority, confirmed that ICC-Angkor Has worked well and is a model for the world for 25 years.
She said that the operation of ICC-Angkor for 25 years is also a great success of an international mechanism with the participation of UNESCO, France, Japan, the Royal Government of Cambodia and many other international partners.
According to the Minister of Culture, the strong will and policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to preserve the cultural heritage and the direct participation of the King, who is the Honorary President of ICC-Angkor Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is an important contributor to the success of ICC-Angkor.
The Minister added that the complete peace factor in the country brought development in all areas, allowing ICC-Angkor to strengthen to work with international experts as well as themselves.
Public support, understanding of national heritage values is also key to contributing to this success. Another success factor is the expansion and strengthening of the capacity of national experts.
Currently, Cambodian experts, especially young professionals, have the ability to perform well and further strengthen their capacity, because if ICC-Angkor is not strong, ICC-Angkor can not cooperate with external institutions. In fact, Cambodian experts are directing and implementing a number of renovation projects in the Angkor resort.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided some of the following initiatives to the conference:
1. Jointly promote regional and global cooperation to exchange information, experience, technology development and physical infrastructure construction to take advantage of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the creation of digital technology opportunities.
2. To jointly increase cooperation to prevent fraudulent information and information technology crimes through the media through the dissemination of factual information to neutralize fraudulent information.
3. Strengthen the implementation of the law, professional ethics, avoid spreading false information, resentment, insults, incitement to anger, resentment, discrimination, racial, religious or exaggerated information that creates social insecurity. .
4. Strengthen close cooperation to resolve media disputes that cause chaos and affect the use of digital technology.
5. To work together to increase the technical and professional understanding to keep up with market demand, the evolution of media technology and the evolution of the global situation.
6: To make traditional media a smart system and flexible to the real situation and the evolution of modern technology to face market competition in the digital age.
7: To jointly develop policies, strategic frameworks, legal regulations for the media and digital security standards regulations, which are essential for the management of data security in business, electronic payments and cyber security to counter And fraudulent information and cybercrime.
