Russian Ambassador to Cambodia, Russia National Day: Russia and Cambodia Enhancing Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): On June 12, we celebrate the National Day of Russia, which represents the unity of our country and shows the values we love the most. Today, the people of Russia recall its glorious past, which has paved the way for the country to stand strong in the present and enable us to face the future with confidence.
The progress of our society contributes to the wisdom of foreign policy and sustainability in order to maintain the system of international relations based on the fundamental principles of international law, non-violation of state sovereignty, mutual respect. Ensure a reliable and predictable global community order.
So it brings me pleasure and satisfaction to continue to develop our bilateral relationship on the basis that was established 63 years ago. Mutual respect and understanding, trust and support - these are not Yes, just a simple word, but an unchanging principle of our relationship that remains.
The talks highlighted the Russian economy's main interest in investing in Cambodia and launching joint projects in the energy sector (including geological exploration and extraction), transportation, construction and repair of agricultural machinery, tourism. Etc. We need to work actively in the IRCC format to integrate these ideas and make them a reality in the future.
The visit of the Cambodian delegation under the leadership of the Second Vice President of the Senate, HE Tep Ngorn, to the 2nd International Forum "National Assembly Development" to be held in Moscow in July this year will definitely contribute to a positive example. This.
It should be noted that further push was made in the interactive dialogue based on the relevant agreement signed between the Russian political party "Russia United" and the Cambodian People's Party in 2016. Close ties between representatives of the "United Russia" party and the Cambodian People's Party welcomed the official start of the ACC of the International Conference of Asian Political Parties earlier this year.
I firmly believe that the relationship between Russia and Cambodia will continue to grow stronger and more mutually beneficial. Our solidarity in resolving international issues facing strong experience in bilateral talks, accelerating communication at all levels on different platforms, clear mutual understanding and mutually respectful approaches will Lead us to great achievements both in our country and around the world.
