Minister Mam Bun Heng Addresses Boao Forum: Cambodia's Health Sector Has Achieved Many Major Achievements
The forum was officially opened under the chairmanship of the Deputy Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China and was attended by delegates from 55 countries, including more than 800 former prime ministers, former ministers, representatives of the World Health Organization and international organizations.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng addressed the official opening ceremony of the forum, emphasizing to the whole ceremony that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the health sector has achieved great achievements. Most notably, the achievement of the 4th, 5th and 6th Millennium Development Goals ahead of schedule.
At the same time, Minister Mam Bunheng also shared his experience and progress of the development of the health sector in Cambodia and the vision to achieve the goal of sustainable development and to achieve global health coverage through implementation. Some strategies such as the Equity Fund, the Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 and additional financial assistance programs for pregnant women.
At the same time, the professor also shared four main discussion points to the ceremony, including:
1: What we need to do to train smart human resources to respond to any infectious diseases that are occurring or will occur in the future
2. What is the role of the private sector in health financing?
3. What kind of health care system should be developed that is gentle but strong to respond to the future of the aging population and non-communicable diseases?
4. How can we benefit from advances in technology to help the health sector and ensure that all people have access to the health services they need at affordable prices?
