The Secretary General of the Veterans Association said that the house distributed to the veterans was born from the spirit of care of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who both Samdech always consider the veterans as There are great merits in the national cause, there is a village table in the face of the crisis of war.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that the house, which was a gift from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, has become a warm home for all veterans. On behalf of all veterans, Mr. Kun Kim thanked Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always thinking of the well-being of the veterans.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also thanked Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on behalf of Samdech Techea Hun Sen, for mobilizing philanthropists to help build houses for veterans and handing them over. More.
It should be noted that in the handover ceremony this morning, seeing the difficulties of the veterans in the development area of Square 2, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Veterans Association decided to help build a school. 1 health center, 10 km of access road, 20 water wells, 1 water bottle per house.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan also donated 100,000 Riels and other materials to the families of veterans who received a house. This morning, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan also donated another 45 houses for Cambodian veterans.
It should also be noted that 309 families of homeless veterans who came to live in this 2 square development area were given a plot of land 30 meters by 50 meters, a house and a hectare of arable land. . Amret organizes 4-day training course on "Financial Knowledge" in Siem Reap in the presence of about 300 participants
This "Financial Literacy" training program focuses on effective savings and basic knowledge in the financial sector.
Ms. Keo Thida, Senior Environmental and Social Officer of Amret Microfinance Institution, explained that the participants in this course will gain knowledge on cash management, how to save and safe depository, the benefits of saving and Use finances in daily life.
She added, "This is one of Amret's attention to the people in the provinces who lack financial knowledge, especially housewives."
Please be informed that this training course will be held for 4 days, which will be held on 11 and 12 June in Sangkat Krabei Riel, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, while on 13 and 14 June in Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. Approximately 75 participants.
Ms. Tun Nissay, who attended the "Financial Literacy" training course in Sangkat Krabei Riel, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, said, "Before, I did not know how to manage my money. After completing this course, I can Distinguish what money to spend and what money not to spend and save money in a bank or microfinance institution recognized by the Royal Government.
It should be noted that Microfinance Institution "Amret" has organized training courses on "Financial Knowledge" for trainees in 25 provinces since 2011. As of 2019, a total of more than 4 trainees have attended. "Amret" also promotes environmental awareness and measures to reduce the use of plastic bags.
By providing responsible and efficient financial services as well as customer protection and social responsibility, "Amret" received the 2018 Consumer Protection Certificate from Smart Campaign, an international organization responsible for the policy. Protect customers in the financial sector.
Amret currently has more than 4,000 employees serving a total of more than 465,000 clients through 156 executive offices across Cambodia with a total deposit of over $ 475 million and a total portfolio of approximately US $ 900 million. US and assets of more than 1 billion US dollars. China responds: We have no choice but to retaliate strongly against the US tariff increase plan!
