Ministry of Tourism urges all cities, towns, resorts to continue their efforts to promote clean and green
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and the National Committee for Clean City Assessment have urged all cities, towns, towns and resorts to continue their efforts to promote cleanliness and greenness in order to participate in the tourism city competition. Clean ASEAN and the Clean ASEAN Tourism Cities Competition Movement.
This promotion was repeated during the training course on ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities Standards and Procedures for the 2nd ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities Competition, chaired by Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Vice Chairman of the National Clean Cities Evaluation Committee. June 11, 2019 at the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Bora stated that the National Framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia has launched the campaign "Clean City, Clean Resort, Good Service, Good Hospitality", which is one of the most appropriate strategic options to participate in the development of green tourism and contribute to Cambodia. Go for clean and green.
He urged all cities, towns and resorts to continue their efforts to promote cleanliness and greenery, which is Cambodia's long-term vision, by adhering to the concept of "current development is for us now and The next generation.
It should be noted that Cambodia has already officially announced the launch of the National Clean City Competition Movement twice, which was announced on the occasion of the 2017 Tourism Review Conference and the direction. Implement 2018 in conjunction with the celebration of the 6th National Clean City Day on February 28, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In response to this, Cambodia participated in the first ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities Competition movement in early 2018 at the 2018 ASEAN Tourism Forum in Chiang Mai, Thailand. At that time, three Cambodian cities, including Battambang. Kep and Siem Reap won the ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities.
