Lt. Gen. Hun Manet Meets and Discusses with the Minister of National Security of Singapore
(Singapore): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, led a high-level delegation from the Cambodian Army Command to pay a courtesy call on Senior Minister Teo Chee. Hean) Minister of National Security of the Republic of Singapore on the afternoon of June 11, 2019.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister and Minister for National Security of the Republic of Singapore extended a warm welcome to Lt. Gen. Hun Neth and the delegation who came to pay an official visit to the Republic of Singapore.
The Minister for National Security of Singapore said that Singapore and Cambodia have had good relations for a long time and talked in the areas of education, trade, tourism and security. The Senior Minister strongly believes that the visit of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, the Commander of the Army, will further strengthen the ties between the two countries.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Manet thanked the Republic of Singapore for inviting him and the Army delegation to pay an official visit. "In fact, Cambodia and Singapore have had a relationship for more than 50 years and this relationship will continue into the future," he said.
Regarding security and stability in the region, Lt. Gen. Manet stated that Cambodia, as well as other countries in the region, must work together to maintain peace and stability without development.
The Deputy Prime Minister also stressed that Cambodia and Malaysia have a long history of diplomatic ties and cooperation, both in the bilateral framework, the ASEAN framework and in the international arena. The economic, financial, trade and investment sectors are also constantly strengthened and expanded.
He said that at present, many Malaysian companies are doing business in Cambodia smoothly and with remarkable progress. At the same time, many other Malaysian companies are looking at investment potential and opportunities in Cambodia, especially in the areas of infrastructure, affordable housing, tourism, health, and the digital economy.
The Ambassador pointed out that in 2006, the amount of foreign direct investment (FDI) from Malaysia in Cambodia ranked first. In this regard, the Malaysian government will encourage Malaysian companies to invest more in Cambodia to reach the largest investment in Cambodia again.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth informed the Malaysian Ambassador that Malaysia is one of Cambodia's major trading partners. The Royal Government of Cambodia welcomes further investment in Cambodia by Malaysian investment companies. The Royal Government of Cambodia provides equal treatment to all companies investing in Cambodia.
