(Phnom Penh): Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto said that the study, whether lazy or monk, must be done every day and regularly until it reaches a certain level as much as possible for the benefit of oneself. , Buddhism, religion and society.
Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto made this remark during the opening ceremony of the 2019-2020 school year at Wat Phneat Simpaly Buddhist Primary School in Snor Commune, Kampoul Sangkat, Phnom Penh on June 11, 2019.
Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto said that the training of resources in the field of monks as students is a good promotion of education to increase morality in society. Today, Buddhism is deeply rooted in the mindset and traditions of Cambodia.
She stated that at present, all monks have equal rights to study and absorb knowledge under the shadow of Buddhism, even though some monks are born in remote rural areas and have poor families.
She added that the practice of traditions, customs and participation in building achievements in the field of Buddhism in today's society is an expression of a strong will to promote morality and virtue in accordance with the Constitution, which defines Buddhism as the state religion. In that, the growth of the Buddhist sector is a mirror of the progress in the realm of the empire as well.
She continued that, under the current leadership of the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, he always pays high attention to social, economic development, especially infrastructure in the realm.
Monikosal Dr. Yorn Seng Yeak, Vice Chancellor of Sihanoukville Buddhist University, said that knowledge cannot be transferred to any individual without the effort of learning from the individual. Therefore, all education and training, whether in the field of Buddhism, are important because it increases the knowledge not only of the disciples.
Monikosal Dr. Yorn Seng Yeak continued, "Therefore, it is necessary to make efforts and manage the monks to behave well and thoroughly in accordance with the curriculum set by the National Inspectorate of Buddhist Studies and the Ministry of Cult and Religion." By quality and effectiveness on this study.
Please note that in the academic year 2019-2020, Wat Phneat Simpaly Buddhist Primary School has a enrollment of 95 students. There are 4 levels of study: 20 students in kindergarten, 1 student in the first grade, 30 students in the second grade, 25 students in the second grade, and 20 students in the third grade, focusing on the Pali language.
Agriculture: Preah Vihear farmers happy with pumpkin harvest due to high market price
(Preah Vihear): Farmers in Preah Vihear province are busy harvesting pumpkins to sell to traders after the odds of selling pumpkins are higher compared to previous years.
