Head of ICRC Mission in Cambodia: ICRC Acts as a Pioneer in Promoting International Humanitarian Law
(Phnom Penh): Roman Paramonov, Head of Mission of the International Committee of the Red Cross in Cambodia (ICRC), said that the ICRC plays a role in pioneering and disseminating international humanitarian law or the law on armed conflict, so it is important for the parties All parties clearly understand the activities covered by international humanitarian law and the principles of respect for humanitarian law at all times.
Roman Paramonov said all efforts were made to stop humanitarian principles as military security forces prepared to launch missions. The workshop will focus on the study of the differences between armed conflict and law enforcement operations, as well as law enforcement norms and guidelines.
He said the three-day regional workshop was a forum for soldiers, police and law enforcement officers to learn about current issues and law enforcement through a study of the various tools encountered. Past experiences as well as discussions to share experiences.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, General Ith Sarath highlighted the importance of the program as well as the strong commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia to host the event with the support of the ICRC.
The general said that through this workshop will raise awareness of all soldiers on their duties under national and international rules.
"All participants from Asia and the Pacific can exchange ideas and share experiences on technical work, obstacles they face and find common solutions," he said. "
General Ith Sarath added that the ICRC works closely with the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, including peacekeepers at the National Peacekeeping Force Management Center, who are out on missions following UN missions abroad to disseminate humanitarian law. International through training courses and workshops.
