(Stung Treng): The National Employment Agency (NEA) of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training this morning, June 11, 2019, inaugurated the Stung Treng Provincial Job Center, once a remote province in the northeast. Of Cambodia.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Pech Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and Vice Chairman of the National Training Committee.
In addition, through this job center, all types of educational and training institutions can also widely promote their training programs.
Dr. Pech Sophoan appealed to the people and children, students, youth who need to find work as well as employers in the whole Stung Treng province to use and take full advantage of the service package provided by the Stung Treng Job Center.
At the same time, he also encouraged all officers and staff of Stung Treng Provincial Job Center to continue to do their best to provide quality, timely and effective services to the people by expanding cooperation. And partnerships with authorities at all levels, employers, educational institutions, as well as NGOs and all stakeholders.
Currently, NEA strives to expand employment services and labor market information by establishing 13 employment centers across the country and 1 mobile job center is waiting to provide and bring employment services to all walks of life. .
