(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nong Veasna, Vice President of the Cambodian Rice Federation and a businessman with more than 20 years of experience in the agricultural sector, presented some factors that make the tycoons or rich people in Cambodia do not want to enter the business in agriculture. .
He added that in addition to that, there is also competition with neighboring countries such as Vietnam, Thailand, which have agricultural growth as Cambodia. All of these factors make some investors reluctant to enter the field.
He added: "Obviously, we are already farmers, although the profits from this sector are small, but this is a daily business. But in addition to these weaknesses that make investors reluctant, there is another factor: the agricultural sector is difficult, and combined with those investors have other businesses that are more profitable and convenient, so they do not want to invest. In this area.
