(Phnom Penh): Some key contents of the Cambodian Constitution will be incorporated into the curriculum of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in the near future to mainstream the nation's top legal knowledge to students and citizens. The content of the Constitutional Council's key provisions will be incorporated into the curriculum from primary to high school.
On the afternoon of June 10, 2019, Mr. Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, led the leadership of the members of the Constitutional Council to meet with Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports to discuss in detail the procedures for submission. The main content of the Constitution into this educational program.
During the meeting, Mr. Chhun Lim stated that the Constitution is the supreme law of Cambodia, which everyone must abide by as the owner of the destiny of his country. Understanding the major principles enshrined in the Cambodian Constitution is a necessary and important foundation for building general knowledge for all Cambodians in strengthening patriotic conscience and moral society.
Meanwhile, Mr. Put Samith, Director General of Education, stated that Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, accepted the proposal and the two institutions decided to set up a committee and working group to organize this work. According to educational norms.
He added that the Constitutional Council provides technical assistance in preparing the main content and lessons related to the basic provisions of the Constitution to be included in the curriculum at all three levels. The Ministry of Education is the editor and publisher of the main content and related lessons.
