(Siem Reap): The 16th Asian Press Summit 2019, Information Ministers from 5 countries will be the keynote speakers on technological developments to jointly modernize the media era of the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution and the fight against Fake information. This is according to the release by the National News Agency of Cambodia (AKP) on June 10, 2019.
The 16th Asian Press Summit 2019, hosted by Cambodia in Siem Reap, will be held from 10 to 13 June 2019. Five Information Minister Speakers from 5 countries will jointly discuss The evolution of technology and the fight against fake information that is happening in the world and related issues.
Has Sam Ath, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Information and Deputy Chairman of the Organizing Committee of the 16th Asian Press Conference, said that the five keynote speakers were Minister of Information Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information of Cambodia, Minister of Information of Laos, Myanmar, Philippines and Korea. South and Deputy Information Minister of Samoa.
He said that the 16th Asian Press Conference 2019, held in Angkor, Siem Reap province, was held from June 10 to 13, with a delegation of leaders and representatives of government institutions, as well as national and international journalists. About 500 people from more than 40 countries in the region and the world.
The 16th Asia Press Summit 2019, which will officially open under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on June 12, focuses on key issues such as: the impact of the media sector under the influence of the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution; Fight fake news and so on.
