General Ith Sarath: Army Considers Training a Priority of Reform and Capacity Building
(Kampong Speu): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, stated that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) still considers training as one of the priority areas of its reform to modernize and increase the professional capacity of the military. To ensure the effective protection of sovereignty, territorial integrity, peace, security and public order, as well as development in all areas of Cambodia.
This statement was made by General Ith Sarath on June 10, 2019 at the closing ceremony of the training course for officers of the 3rd Squadron, 3rd Generation Infantry Squadron at Infantry Institute of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Tlok Ta Sek is located in Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province.
On behalf of the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Army Institute would like to commend and appreciate the active implementation of their roles and responsibilities with a high sense of responsibility and support. Encouraged to continue more efforts to achieve better tasks for the nation and the people.
(Phnom Penh): In order to avoid possible accidents to children in the brick factory, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a recommendation to the Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of all capitals and provinces to introduce The owner or director of a local brick-making handicraft forbids children from entering the production line premises.
The instruction of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of June 10, 2019, states:
* First: Prepare large and easy-to-see signs such as: Prohibit children from entering the production line, any young people entering the production line may face criminal offenses, the use of child labor in Brick making can be a criminal offense.
* Second, it is strictly forbidden to use debt bondage to impose the burden of workers' freedom of work.
* Third: There must be regular monitors and children are not allowed to enter the production line or work in the brick factory.
* Fourth: Accommodation must be arranged away from the production line and there must be a safety fence that separates the production line and accommodation.
According to the Ministry of Labor, from 2019 onwards, the seniority of workers to receive seniority pay shall be calculated every 1 semester (6 months), the first semester to June and the second semester from July to December.
Full-time workers who work from 1 to 6 months in each semester and work until the end of the last month of each semester, June and December, then workers can receive compensation Seniority pay equal to 7.5 days on average in each semester.
The ministry added that in the event that workers resign before the end of June or December, they will not receive seniority pay in each semester.
