Health officials warn of an increase in dengue fever in Kratie province, 442 cases in the first half of 2019
In fact, at the beginning of 2019, there were 442 cases throughout Kratie province, whether children or adults and the elderly, and some areas suffered the most are some communes in Snuol and Chit Borei districts, including the elderly. In six cases, three people were killed, including one adult over the age of 15.
Mr. Chhnang Sovutha said that the factors that contribute to the disease is the weather because the dry season is long and the rainy season comes with heavy rain, causing a rapid onset and the disease occurs. Tiger mosquitoes bite during the day, where they are most likely to be found in watery and clear places, including: water bottles, pools, bottles, coconut shells, cans, flower pots, especially tires that are difficult to remove.
In this preventive activity, the department disseminated health education to the people in the vulnerable areas by car, put the medicine into the water bottles and sprayed the mosquito repellent, and the suspicious symptoms of this disease can be identified in children. High fever, bone pain, abdominal pain, vomiting, nausea, rash or scarring.
At the same time, Mr. Chhnang Sovutha added that if you encounter the above symptoms, please bring your children or members to the health center or hospital in time to avoid coming to the private clinic for examination and treatment. At present, no private clinic is able to diagnose and treat dengue fever like a public hospital, because the symptoms change rapidly and can be fatal.
He also appealed to the people throughout Kratie province to prevent the occurrence of tiger mosquitoes, to clean the water bottle, put abet in the water of 7 colors of fish in the pond, not to get muddy, clean the back of the refrigerator. It can also cause tiger mosquitoes, and both adults and children should wear long sleeves during the day and sleep under a mosquito net.
