Tycoon Pung Kheav Se: Cambodia has the most open investment policy in Southeast Asia
Duke Pung Kheav Se made the remarks at a reception for the delegation of the China Global Business Federation under the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural Development, held at City Hall, Koh Pich, Phnom Penh in the evening. June 09, 2019.
"Cambodia is the country with the most open investment policy in Southeast Asia, and China is Cambodia's main trading partner and largest source of investment," he said. "Through the implementation of the One Belt One Road strategy, more and more Chinese investors are coming to invest in Cambodia, bringing development opportunities for Cambodia, including many Chinese businessmen."
At the same time, Duke Pung Kheav Se also said that the Chinese Teochew businessmen living in all parts of the world are the most influential Chinese businessmen in the international arena. The efforts of the Teochew Chinese businessmen not only to develop their businesses but also to contribute to the economic development of the living countries have been highly praised by the local government.
During the ceremony, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly emphasized that Cambodia is a country with five main advantages for investment under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, including:
1. The potential for political stability and security, which has put Cambodia on the path of economic and social development with an average annual growth rate of 7.7 percent over the past two decades.
2. Cambodia has opened its economy to all investors in all sectors, including banking, insurance, agriculture, agriculture, industry, mining, electricity, real estate, tourism, education, health, special economic zones, etc., and foreign investors can invest 100% without Participation from local investors.
3. Cambodia has a large young workforce, with the Cambodian population under the age of 35 accounting for up to 72% of the total population, and this workforce is projected to increase in the next two years. The next three decades.
4. Cambodia is strategically located in the ASEAN region, which has been attracting investment for markets with a population of more than 600 million people, and Cambodia is also in the Mekong Delta, an area of economic growth and development. High connectivity, especially the implementation of the One Belt One Road project of Chinese President Xi Jinping.
5. The Royal Government of Cambodia has been carrying out many and in-depth reforms in various fields in order to attract investment, including reforms in the logistics system, transportation sector, energy sector, customs and tax sector, and amendments to the investment law.
