Pailin Governor Urges Provincial Veterinary Officials to Continue Vaccinating 4,565 Animals
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, urged the veterinary officers of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to continue to vaccinate 4,565 animals as planned due to the season. This heavy rainfall can make animals sick.
The provincial governor made this urge on June 10, 2019, when he inspected the vaccination of animals in Otavao, Pailin. Mr. Phan Chanthul said that the vaccination was aimed at preventing the disease (cattle) from becoming infected, if we are a little careless, it can cause cattle death, which can affect the family economy and time. Also.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul also instructed the people who have vaccinated animals now to help spread the word to our people who have not been vaccinated against cattle. Their buffaloes and veterinary officers of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will continue to vaccinate livestock to the people free of charge.
According to Mr. Say Sophat, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, people who raise cattle must know how to monitor their animal diseases regularly to know the disease status of animals, especially urgently. Inform local authorities and relevant experts so that veterinary officers or village doctors can come down and treat in time, avoiding the death of animals, which leads to loss of family economy.
According to Mr. Khieu Sothon, Director of the Pailin Provincial Production and Veterinary Office, there are currently more than 8,000 cows in Pailin province, and in the first half of 2019, the provincial veterinary officers vaccinated. 4,565 head of cattle, including 2,925 cases of dehydration and 1,640 cases of foot-and-mouth disease.
