(Phnom Penh): The General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce, in collaboration with the German International Cooperation Organization, from June 10-12, 2019, organized a basic training course on "Economy and Competition" in the presence of Mr. Kim Meas Sok Seiha, General Deputy Director of the General Department of CamControl and Advisor to the Ministry of Commerce and Frank Tibitanzl, Director of the COMPETE Program Project of the German International Cooperation Agency.
Mr. Kim Meas Sok Seiha said that currently, the draft law on competition in Cambodia has already completed the inter-ministerial level meeting at the Office of the Council of Ministers, yet Chapter 4 and Chapter 6, which stipulate the procedures and penalties that require the working group to draft the law. Of the Ministry of Commerce must meet with the Ministry of Justice before the draft law is sent to the Plenary Session of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
He added that at the same time, to increase awareness of competition as well as strengthen the knowledge of economic analysis to officials of the General Department of CamControl, which in the future will have to implement the competition law, requiring economic analysis.
This training will provide additional knowledge to all participants about the importance of competition law and market study, based on economic analysis, which is an important basis for fulfilling its obligations.
Another piece of knowledge that this course will provide participants with is identification of market power as well as identification of cartel offenses and other illegal leaks that could lead to competitive offenses.
