For his official visit to Hungary from 13 to 14 June 2019 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Hungary Viktor Orbán, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will pay a separate courtesy call. With Hungarian leaders and hold bilateral talks with their Hungarian counterparts on various issues aimed at enhancing and strengthening existing bilateral relations as well as close cooperation in multilateral forums.
During the visit, two documents: an agreement on economic cooperation and an education exchange program - will be signed.
During the summit, the Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address focusing on key issues facing the common challenges of Asia and share a deep view that Asia will work together to address security, economy and politics through Strengthen trust and confidence among CICA member countries.
In addition to the summit, the Prime Minister will hold bilateral talks with Tajikistan President Imo Maliramon and the heads of state / government of other member states.
The CICA is a multilateral forum aimed at promoting cooperation among its member states in areas such as peace, security and stability in Asia and the world. The conference currently has 26 permanent members, and Cambodia joined in 2011.
