Many farmers and plantation owners trust the use of Japanese earth fertilizer to grow crops
(Phnom Penh): More and more farmers and plantation owners of both fruits and agro-industrial crops are enjoying the benefits they enjoy thanks to the well-known Japanese Earth Fertilizer.
During the rainy season, farmers and plantation owners rush to grow their own crops and strongly trust the use of Japanese earth fertilizer by purchasing this natural fertilizer.
Ms. Phoeuk Pha, a farmer living in Ta Trav village, Kantraing commune, Ka Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province, who is satisfied with the use of Japanese earth fertilizer for her vegetables, said that the use of this natural fertilizer makes her crops have high yields and not grow well. There are loose soil diseases, there are also earthworms.
Another farmer who grows rice in Takeo province said that he uses only Japanese natural fertilizer, which has the benefit of maintaining good soil quality, good rice, good growth, no pests, can reduce the use of pesticides. Chemical poisoning with high yields.
Mr. Oknha Chan Sokheang, President of Japan Natural Fertilizer Company, Signs of the Earth, said that many farmers and plantation owners now use Japanese natural fertilizers actively.
"Quality is the key, it builds trust, confidence and continued use every day, Japanese natural fertilizer, our earth sign, we work every day for farmers, for our families, for our nation," he said. "Farmers are prosperous, have a good life, high yields, are healthy to use and consume."
Mr. Oknha Chan Sokheang added that the Japanese natural fertilizer, the sign of the earth, we initially imported entirely from Japan, but now we have opened our own natural fertilizer factory, located on Street 51 near Udong, Kampong Speu. He added that not only supply Cambodia, the fertilizer plant can supply exports to Laos, Vietnam, Myanmar, Thailand, Malaysia, the Philippines and Japan.
The use of natural fertilizers by farmers is in line with the call of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who recently encouraged farmers to continue growing rice using natural fertilizers to expand the prestige of Cambodian rice in International market because due to not using this chemical, Cambodian rice is able to compete with rice from other countries.
The head of the Royal Government has recommended to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to encourage people to cultivate rice and other agricultural crops using natural fertilizers instead of chemical fertilizers, because Cambodia still has a lot of agricultural land that people can afford. Use natural fertilizers.
