The Royal Government sends Mr. Em Chanmakara, Deputy Minister of Social Affairs, to attend the 12th Meeting of the States Parties at the UN Headquarters in New York, June 11-13
Before leaving, the Head of the Cambodian Delegation, led by Mr. Em Chanmakara, Secretary General of the Council for the Action of Persons with Disabilities, stated that the 12th session was decided by the States Parties at the 11th session of the 14th State Parties Conference. June 2018 ago. The session will be held under the theme "Ensuring the Participation of Persons with Disabilities for Global Change through the Implementation of the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities".
Three sub-topics for the roundtable will also be discussed at the meeting, focusing on digital and information technology for the empowerment and inclusion of people with disabilities in society. The right to the highest standards for the health of people with disabilities, the inclusion of people with disabilities in society through participation in culture, entertainment and sports. This was further stated by Secretary General Em Chanmakara.
