Ministry of Labor instructs brick kiln owners to take five measures to avoid accidents on children
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a directive banning children from entering the production line area of brick handicrafts, informing local brick kiln owners to implement five major measures to avoid accidents. Do not let it happen to children eventually in the craft.
The five guidelines include:
1: Prepare large and easy-to-see signs such as: * Prohibit children from entering the production line * Anyone who enters the production line at a young age may face criminal offenses * Child labor in handicrafts Brick production is a criminal offense.
2: Absolutely prohibit the use of debt bondage to place the burden of workers' freedom.
3. Have regular monitors and forbid children from entering the production line or working in the brick factory.
4. Accommodation must be arranged away from the production line and there must be a safety fence that separates the production line and accommodation area.
5. Absolutely prohibit all forms of child labor and forced labor to pay off debts.
The Ministry of Labor has also instructed the Departments of Labor and Vocational Training in all capitals and provinces to disseminate the above instructions to their local brick kiln owners.
The Ministry of Labor directive emphasizes that any owner or director of a brick-and-mortar craft who fails to comply with the guidelines will be fined or may close the business or may face criminal charges. Ministry of Health spokesman: So far there have been no cases of diarrhea, vomiting due to eating noodles.
