(Phnom Penh): Speaking to the media on June 9, 2019, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, confirmed that he is currently requesting a court order to arrest the owner of the "Lux Sary" entertainment club. The crackdown on the night of June 8, 2019 involved drug cases, arresting more than 400 people.
On the occasion of leading the workers to eat national unity noodles in Po Sen Chey district, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that in the past, the authorities have advised many times to the owners of the above entertainment club, but it does not seem to be effective. Open the same day and night, causing great disturbance to the people, students, until a few days ago there was a shooting.
Meanwhile, Major General Phuong Malay, Deputy Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, also confirmed to Fresh News this afternoon that as of now, the 400 detainees are being tested for urine. Finding drugs is almost done.
However, Major General Phuong Malay has not yet been able to confirm how many people have drugs in their bodies. But the authorities are burning hands and feet to lift this work according to the procedure.
Meanwhile, the relevant authorities have not yet revealed the identity of the owner of the "Lux Sary" club, what is the name and the role of the owner.
It should be informed that the police force of Phnom Penh Municipal Police under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police and led the operation force led by Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and the Phnom Penh Municipal Commissioner. During the night, they searched the "Lux Sary" entertainment club, found some drugs and arrested more than 400 club members.
After the search, the police closed the club temporarily and brought about 400 players to the Phnom Penh Police. According to sources from the authorities, most of the players in this club are Chinese and Vietnamese.
