People's Letter: Samdech Techo Hun Sen's call for the Cambodian people to eat this noodle together is really "an effective way to drive out the ghosts of politics, politics and politics from the feelings of the Cambodian people"
First, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's call for Cambodians to get together to eat this noodle is "an effective way to drive out political ghosts, cast out political elites and cast out political demons" from the feelings of the Cambodian people without fear of discrimination. Profiteering or political profiteering simply by eating the noodles. From today, Khmer noodles are not a political hostage of any wicked people.
Third, eating noodles today also reminds us that in the past, the wicked have eagerly persuaded the Cambodian people to "wear black on Monday" as a sign of training the color revolution to destroy Cambodia. Their blind extremist methods have failed and collapsed. Today's noodles are still the food of the Khmer people, the Khmer identity, and not the political food that the wicked abroad inculcate in their own ideology.
Once again, the gathering of Cambodians eating cakes across the country today sent a very valuable message: "The Cambodian people strongly believe in the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister and Prime Minister of Cambodia." President of the Cambodian People's Party! Cambodians love peace, need peace and want to live under the shadow of Techo Santepheap! "The Cambodian people want to see a more prosperous and prosperous nation."
