The border between Venezuela and Colombia was closed in February by order of President Nicolas Maduro to prevent opposition leader Juan Guaidó from bringing US humanitarian convoys from Colombia into Venezuela. Maduro has accused Washington of using the humanitarian aid as an excuse to oust him.
According to Colombian authorities, more than 30,000 Venezuelans have crossed the border into Colombian territory, most of them shopping, after the two countries' border crossings reopened on Saturday. According to the UN, more than 4 million Venezuelans have left the Latin American country since 2015 due to the country's economic crisis.
