Understand the law: actual drunkenness
(Phnom Penh): Drunkenness is a condition in which people with mood swings and dementia weaken the nervous system due to alcohol consumption. Excessive alcohol consumption can lead to uncontrollable alcoholism.
This lack of self-control causes many problems in society, such as rape, domestic violence, traffic accidents and many other negative factors.
Furthermore, even if a person who is intoxicated does not commit any serious crime, drunkenness may affect the honor and dignity of the individual as well as affect public order and good traditions of the society. Well. If a person is actually drunk on a public road, it is an offense under the Penal Code in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
For this week's Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with FRESH NEWS and the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, the topic of "actual drunkenness" will be presented to the following people:
According to the dictionary, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath defines the word drunkenness as a state of unconsciousness or delirium due to alcoholism. Drunkenness means that the state of drunkenness is known to the public or others, meaning that the person is clearly in a state of intoxication.
The reason is that the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia defines drunkenness as a crime punishable by the fact that drunkenness affects the public order, good traditions of society, especially affecting the honor and dignity of people and can Leading to committing other serious crimes if not prevented and prevented.
