National Police Delegation Visits Jiangsu Province of the People's Republic of China
(China): General Thong Lim, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, represented by General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, led a National Police delegation on a five-day working visit to Jiangsu Province of the People's Republic of China from March 3. Until June 7, 2019.
The visit aims to strengthen and expand all-round cooperation and exchange of information and experience between law enforcement agencies of the two countries, Cambodia and China.
Parties that did not win seats consider the results of the council election to be acceptable because they received surprising votes (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Some political parties participating in the third-mandate council elections claim that the results The 2019 council elections are acceptable, even if they do not win any seats, but they still get more votes than expected and more than the number of constituencies they have.
"This is not a small vote, it is an overwhelming majority because the Cambodian Youth Party has only three votes, now we get 11 votes, which means eight more votes than our constituency," he said. "All are party officials, elected through party quotas, so most of them do not vote for other parties, they vote for their party."
Kong Monika, president of the Khmer Will Party, which had no voters, also received two votes. He considers gaining votes but not seats an experience. He praised the NEC for organizing this election in accordance with the law.
The official results of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council of the third mandate 2019, announced on June 08, 2019, show that the CPP won the majority of seats. And behind this party are the Khmer United National Party and FUNCINPEC.
For the Capital-Provincial Council seats, the CPP won 550 seats, the Khmer United National Party won 6 seats and FUNCINPEC won 3 out of a total of 559 seats. In the Municipal, District and Khan Councils, the CPP won a total of 3,484 seats, FUNCINPEC won 33 seats and the Khmer United National Party won 38 out of 3,555 seats in the Municipal / District / Khan Council.
Immediately after the official results were announced, the Cambodian People's Party, which won the majority of votes and seats, issued a statement in support of the results of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal and District Council elections on May 26, 2019. Which was conducted in a free, fair and just manner in accordance with the Constitution and the laws of Cambodia, as well as election regulations and procedures.
The statement added that all Commune / Sangkat councilors who are voters went to the polls to vote independently and responsibly in a neutral and secure political environment. This is another new historical event that reflects more clearly Cambodia's strong commitment to move forward steadily on the path of peace, democracy, liberalism, pluralism and development.
Please be informed that the third mandate council election was held on Sunday, May 26, 2019. There are seven political parties competing in this election: CPP, FUNCINPEC, Khmer United National Party, Cambodian Nationality Party, Khmer Republican Party, Khmer Will Party and Cambodian Youth Party.
The number of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council seats for the third mandate in 2019 is 4,114 seats, of which 559 Capital / Provincial Council seats and 3,555 Municipal / District / Khan Council seats. The constituencies are 11,572 commune / sangkat councilors.
20 teams of professional cyclists from 19 countries will participate in the "World Cycling Event on the Cambodian coast"
(Phnom Penh): A team of 20 professional cyclists from 19 different countries around the world will participate in the "World Cycling Event on the coast of Cambodia" to be held on the coast of Cambodia in the near future. Journalists from 20 countries have also registered to cover the World Cycling Championships.
This was confirmed by Mr. Vath Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on behalf of Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, at a press conference on "Organizing the First World Cycling Event in Cambodia's Coastal Areas" organized by the Ministry of Tourism and the National Committee. Olympic Cambodia at the headquarters of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia on the afternoon of June 7, 2019.
The first Cambodian Coastal Cycling Event will be held on the Cambodian coast from January 4 to 6, 2020, which is divided into three circuits:
* Preparatory phase: Held at Darasakor Resort, Koh Kong Province, January 2 to 3, 2020.
* Circuit 1: On January 4, 2020, depart from Darasakor resort in Koh Kong province, cross the roundabout on Say Phu Thong Street to Koh Kong provincial town.
* Circuit 2: January 05, 2020, departing from Darasakor resort of Koh Kong province (at the roundabout of Say Phu Thong Street), crossing Sre Ambel junction to Veal Rinh roundabout and continuing to Thansur Bokor resort. Of Kampot Province.
* Circuit 3: January 6, 2020, departing in front of Kep Provincial Hall, passing the White Horse roundabout towards the Duren roundabout in Kampot province, then continuing to the Veal Rinh roundabout and ending at the two lion roundabouts in Sihanoukville ( Includes three rounds around Sihanoukville, departing from the Two Lions roundabout, crossing the road behind Sokha Beach Resort, Independence Beach Resort, Reach Damnak, and descending the Independence Road to the two lions roundabout.
The Secretary of State called on all parties concerned, the private sector and especially businesses and people on the streets to organize this event to be ready to support, celebrate and watch this great event in large numbers.
Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution donates blood to improve the welfare of Cambodian society and save the lives of anemic people
(Phnom Penh): Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Limited has organized a blood donation program to promote the welfare of Cambodian society and save the lives of people who are anemic.
The program is organized under the theme "One blood donation can save one life" with the participation of leaders at all levels and staff, teachers, doctors and about 150 blood donation volunteers at the head office. Hattha Kaksekar.
This blood donation program is another new social responsibility work of HKL, which aims to contribute to the improvement of social welfare by reducing the rate of loss of life due to anemia and to celebrate World Blood Donation Day and inspire Involve staff and the public in donating blood for revival.
Mr. Oknha Huot Ieng Tong, General Director of Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution, said, “Today's program clearly shows the strong will of Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution and its staff to contribute to social responsibility through "Volunteers donate blood to save the lives of victims who need blood and to celebrate World Blood Donation Day, which falls on June 14 every year."
Mr. Oknha expressed his confidence in organizing this event in the future and strongly hopes that in the future, this event will continue to be organized and there will be more people to register to donate and organize events at HKL branches across the country. Cambodia.
Mr. Ly Sovit, Vice President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said, "Today's blood donation is very important to save lives, it is also a humanitarian force for the nation."
He added, "The blood donation of the management and staff of Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution today is to share the humanitarian side, which is a gift to save lives and a gift of love." "Our gift now flows from the heart to our humanity and our compatriots."
He wished the leaders of all levels of HKL, the private sector and other institutions to continue to participate in blood donation programs in all forms to save the lives of victims who need blood.
Please note that Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution is a leading public microfinance institution and has been operating in Cambodia for more than 25 years. HKL has been providing a wide range of financial services to customers such as: credit, savings, transfer, local money, ATM, mobile banking, payroll and other services.
