It should be informed that this is the news of the death to close relatives and leaders to attend the funeral of General Dom Hak. General Vong Pisen ordered the army to protect peace at all costs, because peace is not easy to find
(Kampong Cham): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, has once again ordered all troops to maintain peace at all costs, as peace is not easy to find. .
General Vong Pisen stressed that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces must be very careful to protect the legitimate Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and strongly oppose all enemies who seek to undermine the existing peace and development. In Cambodia.
The order of General Vong Pisen was made this morning, June 08, 2019, on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the 2nd Military Command Building with the participation of senior officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. As well as a delegation of the Vietnamese People's Army and officers, deputies and soldiers of the 2nd Army Division.
In addition, the Commander-in-Chief also introduced and reminded 10 important points to be additional capital for work in their respective places:
* First, understand the role and duties of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which is the core force of the defense of the people's national independence to ensure the defense of the country and the national interest. That is, must be active in carrying out the work as assigned by the unit leadership to achieve the task and succeed.
* Second: To be an example in respecting and enforcing the law, especially to respect the rules, regulations, general statutes of the soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces with a vigilant spirit. Study, understand and understand the laws, procedures, documents, norms and regulations related to border issues in order to promote good cooperation with neighboring countries with mutual respect.
* Third: Implement consistently and regularly the principles and recommendations of the head of the Royal Government, which is a compass for building character and leading units and institutions, including: Five approaches "mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery. Two mottos "Internal reform, increase external friendship in the spirit of independence" and the Prime Minister's Ten Commandments on the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Army.
* Fourth: Hold on to the security situation in the country, especially the situation involving the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be ready to implement the regulations. Raise awareness of divisive tactics, destroy the unity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces through the use of false information in the social network Facebook. Must believe in the leadership of the Royal Government and must respect and implement hierarchical regulations.
* Fifth: Strengthen and expand the bonds of solidarity and unity within the organization to listen to opinions and accept new experiences from the environment and pay high attention to collective views, both living and working, to be considered Unity is at the core of the success of the task. On the other hand, it is necessary to have good relations with the masses because the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is the people, created by the people and serving the people.
* Sixth: Prepare, maintain and repair equipment, weapons, ammunition and technical equipment to prevent wastage and loss, promote awareness, use economically and maintain a technical level. In particular, care must be taken to maintain and renovate the camps, buildings, and buildings that were donated by Vietnamese friends, which are considered as invaluable contributions and shares.
* 7th: Continue to learn general knowledge, new skills and foreign languages that need to share the knowledge and skills gained from learning to colleagues in the unit with brotherhood, as well as promote morality, living, fitness and entertainment.
At the same time, it is necessary to raise awareness of the consequences of illegal drugs, as well as to take precautionary measures to prevent and cooperate in the timely suppression of the production, traffic and use of all kinds of drugs in the area of responsibility to contribute to maintaining village policy. The commune is safe.
* Eighth: Participate in building a unit under the leadership of its commander to become a unit to live and work clean and hygienic, and to take care of raising animals and growing crops to ensure the livelihood of soldiers in addition to the base Determined regime.
* 9th: Actively participate in rescuing people when faced with natural disasters, evacuating people to safe areas, providing security and rebuilding damaged infrastructure.
Tenth: Enhancing relations with the forces and authorities along the borders of neighboring countries to implement the Royal Government's policy based on the principle of respecting each other's sovereignty, especially with the forces and the Vietnamese border authorities in cooperation. Closely and regularly provide information to each other, solve problems in a timely and peaceful manner if necessary, as well as help make it easier for people to do business and cross the border.
