Minister Mam Bun Heng Leads a Team of Volunteer Doctors to Treat Nearly 1,000 People in Sangkat Teuk Thla
(Phnom Penh): Under the leadership of the Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng has helped to improve the health of the people, especially the people are very satisfied with the free medical services and visits. Right next to their house.
In fact, on June 7, 2019, Minister Mam Bun Heng led a group of volunteer doctors to treat nearly 1,000 people in Sangkat Teuk Thla.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "As officials, doctors, and doctors, we are committed to fulfilling our obligations as health care providers with the ability and a high sense of responsibility to provide this service better. If you are not feeling well, please come to the 24-hour / 24-hour check-up service at the public hospital, referral hospital or health center near the house of your grandparents, uncles, aunts, relatives who are near and close to home.
(Preah Sihanouk): Officials from Preah Sihanouk Provincial CamControl Branch, in cooperation with officials from the Department of Commerce and Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall, inspected the quality of goods and foodstuffs at markets in Sihanoukville to ensure food safety and well-being for the people. And tourists who come to visit in Sihanoukville.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial CamControl Officer Kim Barang said on June 7, 2019 that he led professional officers to inspect and educate traders in some markets in Sihanoukville to check the quality of goods. Check the date of use or shelf life of the goods and do preliminary experiments to find chemicals on those foods and groceries.
Mr. Kim Barang stated that the purpose of the CamControl officers who regularly inspect food to help protect the safety and health of people and tourists.
Mr. Kim Barang stated that for the 7th of June, the activities of CamControl officers in Sihanoukville Province were especially to check and advise the makers and sellers of noodles not to use chemicals that could harm the health of consumers.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo urged CamControl officers to continue to inspect food, especially where there is a wholesale and retail sale of noodles in the upper market and commercial market, as well as at home, etc. for preliminary experiments or preliminary tests for substances. Chemicals that can be mixed in noodles and vegetables Ingredients in markets, wholesale and retail noodle shops Use to make sure the food is free of chemicals.
Officials from the Sihanoukville Camcontrol branch said that although today, officials did not find chemicals on food items. In particular, noodles and vegetables, various ingredients, but officials continue to promote food safety to traders and call on the public to prevent against the use of chemicals on food that causes harm. Citizen health or human health.
Mr. Kim Barang also appealed to all residents of Sihanoukville, if you suspect that any location sells goods containing chemicals or expired, please contact Camcontrol officials in Sihanoukville as soon as possible to take action. Continue.
Meanwhile, some vendors selling food and goods in Phsar Leu and Phsar in Sihanoukville claimed that they have a lot of knowledge about food safety because the CamControl Sihanoukville branch team came down to educate Food safety at their markets and stalls often or almost weekly.
The traders of Phsar commercial and Phsar Leu expressed their support and requested the CamControl officials in Sihanoukville to continue to inspect food safety on a regular basis for the health of all consumers. That is, when eating food, do not worry about mixing chemicals in the future.
In this regard, according to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Chapter 5, Article 64 states that the state prohibits and severely punishes anyone who imports, produces, sells drugs, counterfeit goods and expired goods that affect health. Human or consumer life.
