Senior Minister Osman Hassan Congratulates Cambodia on OIC Special Envoy
The ceremony was held at the Sunway Hotel in Phnom Penh with the participation of diplomats from OIC member countries, including Pakistan, Malaysia, Indonesia, Turkey, Chargé d'Affaires, Kuwait, representatives from the Brunei Embassy and senior leaders of the Senate, National Assembly, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of the Ministries. Lots of crowds.
After the welcoming remarks by Mr. Sman Manan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Mr. Amjad Ali sher, Ambassador of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan to the Kingdom of Cambodia spoke in support of and appreciated Samdech Techo's right decision. Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Sen has established a special relationship with the OIC by appointing Osman Hassan as Cambodia's special envoy to the organization.
The more than 800,000 Cambodian Muslim community in Cambodia is very proud to be given such a great opportunity to contribute to the development and maintenance of peace in Cambodia. "Cambodia is a model country for other countries in the region to follow in the context of peaceful interfaith harmony among the Muslim and non-Muslim communities," the ambassador said.
On this happy occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that he was very pleased that Cambodia had become a special envoy to the OIC, which has 57 member states representing the people. 5 In the world, the second largest organization after the United Nations.
So far, Cambodia has applied for membership in the Observatory, which met in Kuwait, with 56 countries supporting only one country, Cambodia, which is continuing this work, including the Secretary-General of the OIC.
He added that as Cambodia's special envoy to the OIC, he had warm expectations under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has been making progress in Cambodia. Samdech has constantly made Cambodia harmonious in religion and ethnicity and has good policies for all nations to live together in harmony.
