Cambodian child receives US government scholarship to study at US Air Force Academy
(Phnom Penh): A young Cambodian student named Nou Chanyuthea, who successfully graduated from the 12th grade at CIA First International School, received a scholarship from the US Government to study at the US Military Academy for 4 years in the field. Bachelor of Aircraft Engineering
The US Embassy added that the Office of Military Cooperation at the US Embassy in Cambodia is pleased to invite young Cambodians to take part in the 2024 U.S. Military Academy Exam for students entering the academy in July 2020.
In fact, on the afternoon of June 7, 2019, CIA First International School organized a get-together with Nou Chanyuthea, a former 12th grader at the school and to celebrate the US Government Scholarship. Studied at the United States Air Force Academy.
Yuthea said excitedly, "Receiving this scholarship is very valuable to me because as a result, I have struggled for more than nine months. Being rigorous in selecting candidates for this scholarship requires me to be determined. My family is very happy because they understand the value of this scholarship for me.
"They have a philosophy that success comes from failure, reform and the struggle to achieve something," Yuthea said. In particular, the curriculum I studied at CIA First International School was in line with the conditions and requirements of the scholarship program, which made me one of the most prominent candidates.
Mr. Oknha continued that because the competition for scholarships is both national and international, in which the ability of Cambodian candidates is compared with candidates from other countries before the committee. Scholarships are awarded to any candidate.
He also emphasized that the school will continue to participate in the development and improvement of the quality of education in Cambodia with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, so that human resources in Cambodia can compete on the international stage.
Please be informed that after completing four years of study in the United States, Nou Chanyuthea will return to Cambodia to serve in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
Minister of Commerce Shows Positiveity of Cambodia-France Trade Relations
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, noted that the trade relations between Cambodia and France have improved a lot and are very positive and have pushed the trade volume between the two countries to increase continuously.
The Minister's remarks came during a welcome reception at the annual forum of the French Foreign Trade Advisers Forum in ASEAN, hosted by French Ambassador to Vietnam Eva Nguyen Binh. Kingdom of Cambodia at the French Embassy in Cambodia on the night of June 6, 2019.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak warmly welcomed the ceremony. Especially to the French advisers in ASEAN, business people and all the participants who attended the event.
Mr. Pan Sosak informed the ceremony that Cambodia is an open country and has many favorable policies for investment, trade and business. Through the policy of supporting business and trade of Cambodia, the total trade volume between Cambodia and France reached 1.26 million US dollars in 2018, equivalent to an increase of 9.2% from 2017 by 91% of trade volume This is an export from Cambodia to France.
The Minister briefed the Prime Minister on the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in ensuring peace and political stability, which is the foundation of development. In addition, the Royal Government of Cambodia is implementing reform programs to facilitate the business environment to attract more investment, all of which are the vision set out in the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025.
