According to Mr. Tan Saroeun, in Suong Keut village, Suong commune, Suong city, Tbong Khmum province, his family has been making noodles for almost 40 years, since the 1980s. Less than 300 kg, and if there are more orders up to one ton per day.
The noodle maker, who has been making noodles for nearly four decades, says that using noodles to grind rice into flour, then mix the flour together and put it in a pen, press it in hot water, cook it until it boils and then take it as a gift.
Mr. Chea Naron, Governor of Suong City, said that there are more than 10 families who are making noodles in Suong as a family, not a big handicraft, and they do it for distribution in some areas and districts. Accept resale as a whole, they never sell the rest. According to the mayor, this business looks very lucrative, just because their livelihood is good, they have big houses and some even have luxury cars to drive.
