The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation expressed its deep regret that Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong posted on his Facebook page on May 31.
"This is an insult to the sacrifices of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, which helped liberate Cambodia from the genocidal regime," the Foreign Ministry said.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the night of June 6, 2019, gave a serious reaction to the Prime Minister of Singapore that the Singaporean leader really contributed to the killing of the Cambodian people and questioned Do you consider the past trial of the Khmer Rouge leaders to be correct?
The Singaporean prime minister's remarks also drew a backlash from Vietnam. Vietnamese Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Le Thi Thu Hang publicly responded on June 4 that the Singaporean Prime Minister's remarks "do not reveal the facts of history, leading to a negative impact on the views of the Prime Minister." The public.
According to the Vietnamese Foreign Ministry website, the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) issued a verdict on genocide and crimes against humanity committed by the Khmer Rouge in November last year.
"This verdict is concrete evidence of historical fact and it provides justice and reparation to the victims, which is welcomed by the United Nations and the international community."
This suggests that at the time, Singapore supported the genocidal regime and wanted the genocidal regime to return to Cambodia.
Singapore has hosted a conference that has led to the formation of a tripartite coalition government of Democratic Kampuchea and to prolong the war in Cambodia and the suffering of the Cambodian people for more than 10 years, which equates to opposition to the people's revival. Cambodians too.
This statement is also an insult to the sacrifice of fresh flesh and blood of the Vietnamese volunteer army that helped liberate Cambodia from the genocidal regime. His Excellency Lee Hsien Loong's remarks today also show the people of Singapore and the world that the Singaporean leaders at the time actually contributed to the killing of the Cambodian people.
Lastly, I would like to ask His Excellency Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong whether he considers the past trial of the Khmer Rouge leader to be correct or not.
