Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on June 6: 507 illegal vehicles were found and 322 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for June 6, 2019, traffic police forces inspected 3,016 vehicles, found 507 vehicles violating the law (69% motorcycles), 185 education vehicles and 322 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,855 helmets and goggles were inspected on June 6, 95 education helmets and 227 glasses were fined.
The Deputy Prime Minister's presentation took place on the occasion of the Deputy Prime Minister leading a Cambodian delegation to the "Belt and Road Forum for the Development of Land and Sea Connections" from 2 to 4 June. In Chongqing, People's Republic of China. The Belt and Road Forum was attended by senior officials from 37 countries from Europe and Southeast Asia. In that, the Cambodian delegation was given the most attention by the Chinese side.
The Deputy Prime Minister also said that the land and sea connection is a twin of the Belt and Road Initiative, as the development of the land and sea connection has led to a wide range of cooperation in the field of infrastructure cooperation. Exchanging people and cooperating within win-win frameworks and other areas.
The Deputy Prime Minister also said that the world is currently going through a complex period of change and the global economy is shaking and globalization is facing many new challenges due to protectionism and unilateralism. Needs globalization and multilateralism, with belts and roads as a driving force.
Regarding direct flights, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong asked the mayor to encourage more flights due to the increase in tourists and asked Chongqing to help buy more rice and agricultural products from Cambodia. In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong also asked the mayor of Chongqing to provide scholarships to Cambodian students. At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister invited the mayor to visit Cambodia.
On that occasion, the experience in Cambodia within the framework of the Belt and Road Initiative was also highlighted. As a comprehensive strategic partner with China since 2010, Cambodia has been a strong supporter of the Belt and Road Initiative since its inception, including the Belt and Road Initiative, including:
During his stay in China, the Deputy Prime Minister also met bilaterally with Chongqing Mayor Thang Leang Chi. In this meeting, the mayor praised and highly appreciated the friendship between China and Cambodia in terms of politics, economy and trade has grown significantly. He added that the modernization of belts and roads is in line with the rectangular strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Currently, there are direct flights from Chongqing to Cambodia three times a week and may increase in the future due to the increase in tourism from Chongqing to Cambodia from January to May, the mayor said. May 2019 is equal to the number of tourists throughout 2018 who visited Cambodia. He added that in the future we will expand our relationship in other areas such as education and agriculture.
During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister said that Cambodia and China are best friends and have good economic relations. He assessed that China's Belt and Road Initiative is linked to the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy.
