Senior Japanese Foreign Ministry Official Visits Sihanoukville Potential as Development Accelerates
(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of June 6, 2019, the Director of East Asia of the Department of East and West Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Japan, Mr. Yukyu Saiphea, met with the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Yon Min. To understand the potential of Sihanoukville, while the province in this area is a foreign investment, especially from China is rushing to invest heavily.
He thanked the Japanese government for its support to Cambodia, both economically and politically. Through this meeting, the Governor of Sihanoukville asked Japan to help spread the word about the province's potential to Japanese businessmen and people so that they can come to invest and enjoy in Sihanoukville.
For the Sihanoukville administration, welcome all legal investments, regardless of China, Japan, the United States or Europe, and the Sihanoukville administration guarantees complete security and safety in accordance with the law.
Mr. Yon Min emphasized that in accordance with the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 of the Royal Government, Sihanoukville is considered by the government as the only multi-purpose industrial province of Cambodia and the country's economic throat. Today, multi-sectoral investment is active and has made Sihanoukville proudly improve its living standards.
At the same time, Mr. Youkyu Saiphea said that Sihanoukville is now developing very fast and he praised the Governor of Sihanoukville who led the province to develop rapidly. He said that Japan has helped develop the Sihanoukville International Port for many years.
According to Yukyu Saipa, Japan will continue to help develop the port and pledge to promote the potential of Sihanoukville to Japanese people, investors and tourists to encourage investors and tourists to come and invest. Lots of entertainment in Sihanoukville.
It should be noted that Sihanoukville currently has 5 special economic zones, 210 factories and enterprises with a total investment of more than 8 billion US dollars and employed tens of thousands of people.
In addition, the province has a Japanese-invested deep-sea port that is currently expanding and has 73% of goods entering and exiting through this port, and there are plans to expand another port in Stung Hav district. In addition, the international airport is expanding to make it possible for large aircraft to operate, with interconnected lanes and expressways being built, with beautiful islands and beaches.
