Samdech Techo Hun Sen Urges Continuation of Chemical-Free Rice Production to Increase Competitiveness and Expand International Market (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, encourages farmers to continue growing rice By using natural fertilizers to expand the prestige of Cambodian rice in the international market, because due to the non-use of chemicals, Cambodian rice is able to compete with rice of other countries.
Such encouragement to farmers was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the graduation ceremony for 1,356 health students from the University of Puthisastra on June 6, 2019.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo said that because Cambodian farmers do not use chemicals on their rice, Cambodian rice has a high ability to compete with rice of other countries, especially countries along the Mekong River. Such as Thailand, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and so on.
However, the Prime Minister from the family of farmers also said that some Cambodian farmers are using chemical fertilizers on their crops because they want their crops to grow faster and have higher yields, which is a big problem. In agriculture and related to serious food safety as well.
To prevent and solve these problems, the head of the Royal Government has recommended to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to encourage people to cultivate rice and other agricultural crops using natural fertilizers instead of chemical fertilizers, because Cambodia still has agricultural land. So much so that people have access to natural fertilizers.
The Prime Minister said that some countries use chemicals and chemical fertilizers in the cultivation of agricultural crops, the products of which are exported to foreign countries, and some also flow into Cambodia.
Samdech Techo continued that in order for agricultural crops to grow fast and to get high yields, some Cambodian farmers also use a lot of chemicals, which has led to the impact on the health of consumers and consumers.
In that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Ministry of Agriculture as follows: "Let people use natural fertilizers and reduce the import of products that use chemicals, which leads to the destruction of people's health."
In this regard, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on people to pay more attention to the cultivation of crops that do not use chemicals. Cambodia can certainly do the above because Cambodia has a lot of agricultural land left and farmers have access to natural fertilizers.
For CamControl, the Prime Minister also strongly recommended "to control the sale of products that use chemicals beyond the limit to damage the health of the people."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also recommended to the Ministry of Health to take the lead in preventing and solving problems related to food safety, must be responsible for the health of the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this remark on the occasion that Samdech Techo presided over the awarding of diplomas to a total of 1,356 health students from the University of Puthisastra after they successfully graduated this morning. This is June 6, 2019.
Speaking at the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to recommend for the university and for the students, and also for the health field, because this university has a field of medicine and medicine, in general, related to medicine."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "We must pay attention to the subject of medicine and medicine because it is related to human life. If it is not clear, we must do our best. The Ministry of Health must orient because there can be no "Training to have doctors outside the list of legal framework."
The Prime Minister of Cambodia also stressed that despite the efforts of some, recently, some media outlets have come down and it is true that some doctors are injecting without a degree and without recognition. From the health department in some villages and communes in our country.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that now in some private schools, some private universities also have medical training as well as medicine, so it is necessary to make efforts to coordinate to become a system that is a unified system.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that even if you study in public schools, you should study in private schools, but this issue should be clearly recognized because the subjects of medicine and medicine are related to human life.
