ADB vows to expand support for Cambodia's agricultural sector to support economic growth and reduce poverty
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has reaffirmed its commitment to expand support for Cambodia's agricultural sector to support economic growth and reduce poverty. This is according to the statement of ADB released on June 6, 2019.
"The ADB will need to develop and expand its support for Cambodia's agricultural sector to support the country's economic growth, mitigate the effects of climate change and attract climate change," the ADB said in a statement. "More involvement from the private sector to meet the needs of the growing population in urban areas."
The ADB acknowledged that although Cambodia has achieved significant economic growth over the past few years, prioritization of the agricultural sector continues to play an important role in boosting economic growth and reducing poverty. As such, it is still limited compared to the tourism and garment industries.
Cambodia is one of four case studies that included Bangladesh, China and Tajikistan in an assessment of ADB's $ 12.2 billion in agricultural support. Natural Resources and Rural Development in 2005-2017. These countries made significant contributions to ADB sectoral operations during the assessment period.
