This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen handed over diplomas to more than 1,000 students of Puthisastra University
According to a report from the university, this morning's graduation ceremony is the third since the university began training in 2007. Today's undergraduate students have a master's degree, a bachelor's degree and an associate's degree in dentistry, medicine, nursing and midwifery.
According to the university, many of these successful graduates have visited and volunteered at universities and health institutes abroad, such as Korea, China, Japan and the United States. America.
Sok Puthivuth, Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the University of Puthisastra, told Fresh News that the graduation ceremony was a congratulation to the students who successfully graduated from the hard work, dedication and dedication of time. And the physical and mental strength to achieve their dreams is an admirable achievement for them as students.
The President of the Board of Directors said that the awarding of this degree is another step forward for all the successful students towards starting a career where society is in need of human resources for development in the country.
The University of Puthisastra was established in 2007 and has been operating for 12 years now. The University has evolved day by day to become stronger in improving the quality of human resource education. Many successful achievements have been made, with the first generation of dental students passing 100% and the medical students passing 99% in the recent 2018 national exam. This.
The University considers these achievements as a manifestation of the hard work of the students, as well as the provision of high quality education in the field of health and other fields, which encourages students to be proud of Their successful graduation from the University of Puthisastra itself.
Ian Findlay, Rector of the University of Puthisastra, said that the University of Puthisastra always pays attention to education, training and encourages students to become future leaders with a wide range of international knowledge.
