NEW DELHI: Thousands of businesses in India on Wednesday will be the victims after US President Donald Trump decided to end tax exemptions for India under the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP). As a result, many Indians are facing job losses. This is according to a quote from the BBC on Wednesday evening, June 5, 2019.
The GSP was first established in 1976 between the United States and 120 countries to help developing countries strengthen their economies and at the same time reduce the price of imported goods for the American people.
India is considered to be the largest beneficiary under the GSP, with $ 6.3 billion worth of Indian exports in 2018 being taxed at low or no tariffs in the United States. United States.
