2019 marks the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Russia. The two countries have repeatedly stated that bilateral relations are at the best stage of history. Chinese President Xi Jinping has paid a state visit to Russia for the most important historic visit, which will push China-Russia relations from the beginning of a new era of greater development.
In the past five years, the heads of state of China and Russia have met more than 20 times and established close and friendly working relations.
Diplomatic ties at the head of state have become one of the hallmarks of maturity and stability for Sino-Russian relations. In April this year, President Putin arrived in China to attend the second summit of the International Cooperation on the Belt and Road Initiative. Less than two months later, Chinese President Xi Jinping traveled to Russia to attend the St. Petersburg International Economic Forum. Petersburg.
The positive role model of the top-level design and strategic guidance of the two heads of state for the development of Sino-Russian relations has become a model for high-level diplomatic ties at the head of state. High level of Sino-Russian relations.
In the context of the current complicated international situation, China and Russia always adhere to each other's development path, do not interfere in each other's internal affairs, strongly support each other in matters that Attention is important and relevant to each other's core interests, which is the main reason why Sino-Russian relations have been developing steadily and steadily.
Putin once said that this data is very important, bilateral trade reflects the development situation of the two countries' relations as a result of increased trust between the two countries.
On the occasion of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Russia, the actual cooperation between China and Russia is welcoming another "harvest year". One week ago, a highway across the border between the two countries was successfully connected, and the first railway bridge is nearing completion, as well as the eastern natural gas pipeline between China and Russia. In 2019 as well.
Cooperation between the two sides in the fields of energy, infrastructure, science and technology, e-commerce, agriculture, North Pole development and regional cooperation has also made great progress. Recently, Dmitry Peskov, the Russian presidential press secretary, told reporters that the trend of Chinese investment in Russia has not slowed down, but has increased significantly.
In the 70 years since the establishment of diplomatic ties, China-Russia relations have gone through all kinds of challenges, such as historical and domestic changes, respectively. In recent years, in the face of a series of sanctions, Russia has voiced its support for fair competition and protectionism through the International Economic Forum in Saint Petersburg.
