Two Suspects Arrested After Renting Motorcycles to Sell and Pawn in Siem Reap
According to the police report, between May 29 and 31, 2019, one of the suspects, Ieng Kea Heng, and his accomplices pretended to rent five motorbikes for tourists in Siem Reap City. Of the victim, Hong Sothol, male, 33 years old, living in Vihear Chen Village, Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
On June 1, 2019, the suspect also came to rent more motorbikes, but the victim wondered and asked the suspect where he could not find the five motorbikes before taking them. The suspect replied that the motorcycle he rented was at a guesthouse, as he did not see many of the motorcycles he rented and continued to rent. The victim complained to the authorities and brought the suspect. Sangkat Svay Dangkum Administrative Police Station to interrogate and receive complaints from victims.
After receiving the information from the victim and the Siem Reap City Police, they immediately requested through Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, to request the cooperation of Stung Sen City Police Inspectorate and Kampong Svay District of Kampong Thom Provincial Police to arrest the person. Suspects, including the victim's motorcycle, were taken to the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate for questioning.
After questioning, the suspect admitted that he actually took the victim's motorcycle to sell in Phnom Penh. According to the suspect's confession and the victim's complaint, on June 4, 2019, the suspect was charged by the Criminal Police of the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate and sent to court for legal action.
