Switzerland pledges more than $ 4 million a year to Kantha Bopha Hospital (Phnom Penh): The Swiss government has pledged to continue to provide financial support to Kantha Bopha Hospital for the next four years. 4 million Swiss francs or about 4 million US dollars (1 Swiss franc equals 1.01 US dollars).
The confirmation of the position of the Swiss Government was made this morning, June 5, 2019 by Mr. Ivo Sieber, Swiss Ambassador to Cambodia on the occasion of his farewell to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. After the ambassador successfully completed his diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
According to Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Switzerland has pledged continued financial support to Kantha Bopha Hospital for the next four years, from 2019 to 2023. In addition, Switzerland has also promised to support the demining sector in Cambodia indefinitely.
