Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth holds an inter-ministerial meeting to review and discuss the "Draft National Strategy on the Financial Environment 2019-2025" and the "Draft Law on Social Security"
The draft strategy focuses on improving the financial environment in Cambodia as a tool to support the effective implementation of the "Financial Development Strategy 2016-2025". In order to promote the improvement of people's lives through the financial environment.
The draft strategy outlines policies, visions and directions to boost the financial environment, increase access to quality formal financial services, reduce the rate of underserved women, and expand access to formal financial services. Improve family well-being as well as support economic growth.
The draft strategy also highlighted priority activities such as: encouraging savings in formal financial institutions, promoting credit product innovation for small and medium enterprises, expanding payment system capacity, expanding insurance services. Broaden, strengthen the capacity of financial sector regulators and enhance customer rights and increase transparency in the financial sector.
The strategy will benefit people who do not yet have access to formal financial services, as well as small and medium enterprises, business opportunities, increase investment opportunities and access to financial services consulting services.
2: Law on Social Security:
The meeting highly appreciated the importance of these two strategies and laws, as well as discussed in more detail the content of each section as an additional input for the working group to continue to improve.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, thanked and appreciated the working group for their cooperation in preparing the two important documents and instructed the working group to prepare the two documents and the inter-ministerial working group to continue to cooperate and Work directly with stakeholders to correct missing gaps to make this document more complete, practical, and comprehensive.
