(Siem Reap): Many of the 2,000 missionaries arrived at Siem Reap International Airport on June 4, 2019 to celebrate the "Cambodia-China Year of Culture and Tourism 2019" and Start a tour of Cambodia.
To celebrate the "Year of Cambodia-China Culture and Tourism 2019", the Government of the People's Republic of China sent a delegation of its Ministry of Culture and Tourism led by Deputy Minister of Culture and Tourism Zhang Xue, along with about 2,000 Chinese envoys. To visit Cambodia from June 2-8, and many of the 2,000 envoys have already arrived at Siem Reap International Airport.
A Chinese delegation from the Ministry of Culture and Tourism led by Mr. Zhang Su, Deputy Minister of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of China, will also arrive at Phnom Penh International Airport on the evening of June 4 to receive a delegation from the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia.
On the afternoon of June 5, Mr. Zhang Su, Deputy Minister of Culture and Tourism of China, will meet with Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Ouk Socheat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture, representing Minister Pheung Sakona at the Ministry of Tourism.
On the evening of June 5, the Ministry of Tourism and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia, in cooperation with the Chinese side, will hold a joint Cambodian-Chinese art performance at the Koh Pich Theater under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Then there will be a welcoming dinner for all Chinese missionaries that same evening.
Please be informed that the cooperation between the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of China and the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia is in line with the designation of 2019 as the Year of Culture and Tourism of Cambodia and China to further promote cultural and tourism exchanges between the two nations.
A 2,000-member Chinese delegation visited Cambodia to learn about investment opportunities in tourism, helping to promote Cambodia's tourism potential to the Chinese people, as well as attract more Chinese tourists to Cambodia.
Please be informed that this "Year of Cambodia-China Culture and Tourism" was initiated by the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of China in collaboration with the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia to further strengthen and expand cooperation on tourism and culture between the two countries. These include joint tourism promotion, exchange of study tours, training of human resources, joint art performances and so on.
