The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists (CJJ) also urges all parties, including government officials, to refrain from using abusive language, physical contact, confiscation of media equipment and destruction of journalists' material resources by fully cooperating with your information. Press. This is according to a statement obtained by Fresh News.
According to this statement, the Federation of Cambodian Journalists (CJJ) has received information that eight online journalists, along with other associates, have filed a complaint with the Kampot Provincial Prek Chak Customs Officer against the Kampot Provincial Prosecutor. For public servants, charges of infringing on the image rights of individuals and illegal interference in the performance of public functions "demanded $ 100,000 in compensation.
The lawsuit was filed after an incident on May 28, 2019 at the Prek Chak customs checkpoint on the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Kampot province between a customs official and a group of online journalists who covered the incident. Freight through Prek Chak customs checkpoint, Kampot province.
The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists would like to request all stakeholders and law enforcement agencies to consider using the Law on the Media Regime to apply to lawsuits involving journalists. The Union of Cambodian Journalists also welcomes if both parties reach an agreement to reconcile and drop the complaint.
The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists calls on journalists to adhere to the code of ethics of journalism, especially when covering news, to avoid threats, abuse, obstruction of the role of public officials and not to abuse Physical rights, values and personal identities.
The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists (CJJ) also requested the relevant parties, including government officials, to refrain from using insulting words, physical contact, confiscation of media equipment and destruction of journalists' materials by fully cooperating to provide information to Journalists to jointly promote "access to information" and promote the dissemination of information that benefits the public.
According to the statement, the Union of Cambodian Journalists will continue to pay close attention to the court's procedures and actions in this case.
