Russia tells Donald Trump: Our military personnel remain in Venezuela
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Reports that the Russian military and technicians have left Venezuela are untrue as cooperation with Caracas continues to grow and expand. This is according to Russian officials quoted by RT on Tuesday, June 4, 2019.
Moscow's reaction comes after the Wall Street Journal reported on Sunday that Russian troops and technicians had left Venezuela on a large scale, with a reduction of 1,000 people. Only a few dozen. The newspaper also claimed that the departure was due to Caracas' inability to pay for Russian military and military services.
