(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ky Sereyvath, President of the Chinese Studies Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the trade war between China and the United States will definitely affect other countries in the world if this war is long, but Along with this war also provided a good opportunity for Cambodia to invest and export.
"Clearly, trade wars between the two economic powers will have an impact on other countries in the world, such as Korea, which is facing a crisis," Ky Sereywat said. "The challenge is that there are tariff barriers on exports from China to the United States, and some goods imported from Korea to be made in China for export to the United States will also be suspended."
Speaking on the program "Special Guest of the Week", Dr. Ky Sereyvath added that these are the real impact if you look back at Cambodia, even though Cambodia did not bring anything to China, but Cambodia imported from China. On the other hand, considering the impact of exports from Cambodia to China, there is no serious impact, but another problem is Chinese investment.
He added that investors coming to Cambodia are Chinese investors, but if Chinese companies in China suspend operations, there may be some impact on investment in Cambodia, but it is an opportunity when Chinese trade barriers can not. Export to the United States, but Cambodia can export to the United States is an opportunity for investors to invest more to produce in Cambodia and export back.
