(Pursat): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, on June 4, 2019, led the working group officials with the participation of Pursat Provincial Governor Mr. Mao Thunin to visit and guide the people who come for medical treatment. Maternity and childbirth at Phnom Kravanh District Referral Hospital, Pursat Province, how to receive cash benefits for women from poor families from pregnancy to children under two years old.
Mr. Mam Bunheng stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to provide cash to poor women, pregnant women and children under 2 years old. Poor women who come for prenatal check-ups 4 times get 40,000 riel, at the time receive 200,000 riel, postpartum check-ups and care for children 10 times for 1,000 days.
In addition, the specific case of providing cash support is in case of miscarriage, get 40,000 Riel (once), fetus under 12 weeks and 40,000 Riel twice, fetus from 12-24 weeks, in case of stillbirth or postpartum At the time of childbirth, the allowance is 200,000 riels at the time of delivery and 40,000 riels three times.
Minister Mam Bunheng stated, "The implementation of this cash subsidy program will be handed over to poor women through the Wing Bank system." This is to improve the well-being of mothers and babies, as well as to reduce maternal and infant morbidity and mortality and to provide nutrition to children in poor families from the time the baby is two years old. In particular, encourage poor women, pregnant women and children to receive regular health care.
