(Kampong Thom): Choam Merech community forest, which covers more than 2,000 hectares in Tralek Chas village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balang district, Kampong Thom province, is being encroached upon by the people.
According to the villagers, the community forest is currently estimated to be less than 300 hectares, and they are encroaching on the plantations and cutting firewood from the villagers.
Residents of firewood in the community forest, who asked not to be named, confirmed that he paid Mr. Som Sopheak 20,000 riel per truck for logging here in exchange for not logging and not Grab the bullock cart when leaving.
Another villager who was cutting down trees in the community forest said that his current activity was to pay the landlord 20,000 riel a day, which the landlord hired him to tell him to beat. The demolition of this land is claimed to have already been bought and sold by the community.
At the same time, Mr. Som Sopheak replied that he had stopped being the chairman of this community for more than a year, because being the chairman of this community was not of any use to him and it was often difficult for him to solve his own problems.
As for Mr. Ly Sreng, the director of Boeung Per Wildlife Sanctuary and who is also in charge of protecting the forest, he also said that he has handed over the management to the commune council, as he only helped as an intervention force to prevent the crime. Only.
However, Mr. Chin Hin, the head of the school district, stated that he did not go into the management of the forest land because all the authority was under the control of the community leader and Mr. Lee. Sreng is the same.
It should be noted that at present, the forest land is being gradually encroached upon and set on fire, and some of the land has been told by local people that Mr. Som Sopheak and Mr. Ly Sreng are preparing to sell it to traders. There is also a series of money.
