The Ministry of Health stated that in order to minimize the impact on the health, lives of victims and health facilities from natural disasters, especially floods that may occur in the future, Professor Mam Bun Heng, Minister of Health, calls for All citizens follow the instructions below:
* Before the flood - Monitor the flood situation, prepare safe places and food. Build a fence around a pond or a place with deep water, keep the environment clean, and build toilets that need to be upgraded from low to high to prevent flooding.
Do not enter an old house or a dilapidated building because it can cause a ruined district. Do not touch electrical appliances with wet hands or standing in water while traveling by boat or ferry at night, keep the lights on.
Sleep under a mosquito net at all times to prevent dengue fever, malaria and other diseases.
For pregnant women, follow up and check the pregnancy according to the schedule of the health center or hospital. If the woman is close to giving birth, find a place to stay near the health center or hospital nearest to you.
Get your child vaccinated as prescribed by your doctor and feed them properly.
Be careful of girls and girls in a safe place, lest there be sexual violence.
- Help the elderly in your family or the elderly in the neighborhood and provide support to family members or children with disabilities such as crutches, wheelchairs or some of the medications they are taking on a regular basis that are essential to their needs.
Be careful to avoid drowning, prevent small children from drowning, explain to children the dangers of drowning, take children to higher ground and have a caregiver use a jacket or plastic bag every time a child leaves the house. When traveling by boat or ferry, do not overcrowd if someone drowns, call for help immediately.
To avoid respiratory infections, it is necessary to wear a mask or towel or scarf to cover the mouth when coughing or sneezing and to stay away from patients who cough or sneeze for more than 1 meter and not near the place. There is dust, if necessary, must wear a mask. When the weather changes suddenly, take care of your health, such as dressing properly and avoiding going out for long periods of time.
* After the flood
Continue to eat clean food, clean water and clean body to avoid various diseases.
Must continue to sleep under a mosquito net at all times to prevent dengue fever and malaria.
- Check the house for collapse or danger, be careful not to have snakes or other venomous animals.
Clean the environment around the house and inside the house because after the water recedes, leaving a lot of dirt and germs living in the water, avoid putting water around the house and inside the house, leading to water worms, tiger mosquitoes and nail mosquitoes that can cause To have dengue fever and malaria.
Wells must be restored and cleaned before use.
As well as repairing and rebuilding toilets by always having to defecate in the toilet at all times.
