China urges students to consider risk of studying in US
According to Chinese state television, citing the Chinese Ministry of Education, some Chinese students wishing to study in the United States have encountered problems with the length of their restricted visa validity. Along with the growing number of visa denials, this has had a profound effect on Chinese students who want to study in the United States or students who want to graduate smoothly.
For this reason, the Chinese Ministry of Education has called on all Chinese students to strengthen their thinking skills as well as assess risks before going abroad to study and be prepared to respond appropriately. At stake are the $ 14 billion economic flows, most of which come annually from the tuition and fees of Chinese students studying in the United States.
The warning comes as China and the United States continue to wage a trade war after talks between the two countries stalled.
