(Prey Veng): Buddhists at the foot of Kanhchum pagoda, Kanhchum village, Kanhchum commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province, on June 2, 2019, protested the eviction of the pagoda's chief priest after the construction of a pagoda was canceled. Build all the plans everywhere, but in the end owed up to 110,000 dollars in materials. People accused the pagoda chief of embezzling money and protested and expelled from the pagoda.
Buddhists at the foot of Wat Kancham told Fresh News on June 3, 2019 that the gathering was aimed at ousting the chief abbot of Kanhchum pagoda, Ros Sophan, who was suspected of embezzling more than $ 110,000. But until now, Ros Sophan has fled to live in Wat Trea in Trea village, Kanhchum commune, Pearang district.
According to the villagers, they are Buddhists who belong to the Kanchum pagoda. Initially, the monks and the pagoda committee agreed to build a pagoda in the pagoda as a place of worship.
Citizens and philanthropists near and far have participated in the construction, some in the pillars, some in the doors, some in the windows, roofs, tiles, receipts, paintings, in general, all the plans, all the people, all the money. With the name according to the plan everywhere, until recently the construction of Chan School suddenly owed more than 110,000 dollars for equipment?
Make people angry, where will they lose money if they pay all the construction costs? . Citizens stated that if they owe more than $ 110,000, if the chief abbot of Kanhchum pagoda refuses to leave the pagoda, ask the chief priest to issue a bill for the people or the monk responsible for paying the lost money.
(Phnom Penh): Myanmar Ambassador to Cambodia U Myint Soe said in front of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, that during his diplomatic mission over the years, he noted that Cambodia There has been tremendous progress.
The remarks of the outgoing Myanmar Ambassador were made this morning, June 3, 2019, when he said goodbye to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia after his term. Its diplomatic mission is over.
Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, told reporters after the meeting: "The Ambassador of Myanmar has confirmed that after the end of his term in Cambodia, he has noticed strong progress in Cambodia. . "As both countries are Buddhist, he noted that Cambodians are very hospitable."
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon said that the trade volume between Cambodia and Myanmar has doubled, but despite this increase, the two countries still have the potential to further expand trade volume. In this regard, the Cambodian head of diplomacy called for efforts to implement the agreements reached between the two countries and to push for the conclusion of other agreements being made to expand trade.
Another key point of discussion was media cooperation, the spokesman said. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon emphasized that the Ministry of Information of the two countries, Cambodia and Myanmar, was now close to agreeing to sign a document.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his position that Cambodia still supports Myanmar's process of national reconciliation as well as peace in Baku. At the same time, Cambodia will continue to cooperate with Myanmar, a brother of the ASEAN family, on regional forums as well as other international forums.
