The Prime Minister of Cambodia calls on pregnant women from poor families to get regular health check-ups, doctors must practice better (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, called for Pregnancy from poor families come for regular check-ups, so the doctors in charge of providing this service should practice better.
The Prime Minister made this call on the morning of June 3, 2019, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the graduation ceremony for students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP) about 3, 161 people at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
