(Battambang): The cave cave community of Phnom Sampov, Banan district, Battambang province receives nearly 2 tons of bat manure per month for sale and distribution to customers to make the most special natural fertilizer to use in plantations on various fruit trees. Individual needs.
He described that in 1995, there were very few bats, but by 1999, there were about 5 to 6 million bats, but now there are natural fluctuations or they go to live somewhere else, we do not Know exactly.
Community representatives confirmed that bat manure is the number one natural fertilizer with high efficiency and has been famous since ancient times. Currently, the bat manure that our community sells for less than 10 kg costs 25,000 riel, but the amount of bat manure collected per month is irregular because it is a natural result that we can not determine the figure. And collected.
On the other hand, according to old sources, bats have a breeding season twice a year, between June and November, to increase the natural production of bats.
Along with the sale of bat dung, the benefits of bats in Phnom Sampov, it can attract national and international tourists, especially rich foreigners, most of them come to visit every day and make food sellers in the foothills. Sampov can earn income to support daily family life, help reduce poverty and reduce the migration of some people.
