At the graduation ceremony for students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh on June 3, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he had received information that the procedure for renaming the ownership of the vehicle is still complicated, requiring Cut the name from the initial seller.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister added that if such a practice is true, it is different from Samdech's recent decision to allow the delisting of the vehicle to take place only between the last vehicle seller and the buyer. Must be deducted from previous vendors.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "So, if there is such a thing, we must try to solve it so that only the buyers and sellers can transfer the name together, and the price should be reasonable with agility, and do not require too many stages of transfer." "
It should be noted that in order to facilitate the procedure for renaming this vehicle, on May 27, 2019, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of Taxation, Meet to discuss the simplification of the tax payment procedure to deduct the name of this vehicle to make it easier through the automation system.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, through the automation system that the Ministry is working on, it is possible to transfer all vehicle ownership in one place, including the transfer of ownership and payment of stamp duty in one place and quickly. Also.
The senior minister said the automated system for transferring ownership of the vehicle could be completed soon.
Alumni of Tonle Bati High School Celebrate Teachers with Smiles and Intimacy
(Takeo): Alumni of Sok An Tonle Bati High School from the early 1980s until the students studying at this high school held a gathering of alumni and thanked their teachers for taking the time and great conscience to build Sok An High School, Tonle Bati and education from the founding of the school until today.
The alumni reunion program was held on May 2 at Sok An High School, Tonle Bati, Kraing Thnong Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province, with the initiative of Mr. Oknha Lim Leang, Governor of Bati District, alumni of all generations and by There was also the participation of singer Mao Haji, Neang Chhay, and Neang Peng Pong.
Mr. Oknha Lim Leang said that other alumni should have the same program throughout the country to have the opportunity to meet teachers and classmates, build friendships and share love to those who have helped us. Today. "Only love, understanding and gratitude can maintain peace in our society."
Phuon Chhim, Bati district governor and a former student of Sok An Tonle Bati High School, said that Sok An Tonle Bati High School has played an important role in educating students in three communes of Bati district: Kraing Thnong, Pot Sor and Kandeung communes. This high school has trained many intellectuals to participate in the development of the society.
The district governor also thanked the Korean friends who, through Mr. Sok Puthivuth, provided the panels to be converted into electricity for use in the school, facilitating the study of teachers in the school.
Also in this gratitude ceremony, Mr. Oknha Lim Leang and all high school students donated 55 teachers with a budget of 200,000 Riels each and organized a solidarity meal for all teachers and students. . In addition, singer Mao Haji and many other singers also performed and ate together.
Tycoon Lim Leang and all generations of Sok An Tonle Bati High School alumni also intend to establish the Sok An Tonle Bati High School Foundation soon to support the development and improvement of the school, as well as to support teachers who Meet the shortage. Mr. Oknha is determined to organize this alumni reunion program once a year and calls on all other generations of alumni to participate in this program as well.
