Legal Awareness: Incitement of Minors to Beg
So, to know more, we need to know what kind of actions and activities are considered to incite minors to beg? And to what extent should the person who committed this crime be punished according to the law?
In order to help solve the above questions and clarify the above issues to all citizens, students, the legal awareness program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "incitement of minors to beg". Explain and share as follows:
Minor refers to any person who has not reached the legal age or is under 18 years of age. The higher the rate of minors begging, the greater the impact on their rights and freedoms, including the exploitation of child labor, the creation of unrest in the community. Public risk of various accidents (eg traffic accidents) and may cause these children to miss out on learning opportunities.
In addition to the above, some crooks incited children to beg in public and gave them all the money in exchange for food as well as shelter. In the event of not being able to beg in any amount that the ringleader has limited, the minors may be threatened with starvation and evicted from their homes.
In short, any person who incites a minor to beg must be held accountable before the law, and all minors should be provided with care and education. And by eliminating all activities that violate their rights.
