Please be informed that Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, paid an official visit to the People's Republic of China from May 30 to June 1, 2019. Foreign Ministry Releases Results of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon's Official Visit to the People's Republic of China
(Phnom Penh): On June 1, 2019, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia released a press release on the results of the official visit of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the People's Republic of China to the People's Republic of China on the 30th. May-June 01, 2019.
Full press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia:
Press Release on the Outcome of the Official Visit of HE Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the People's Republic of China on May 30-June 1, 2019
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, led a delegation to pay an official visit to the People's Republic of China from May 30 to June 1, 2019. Pay a courtesy call on Prime Minister Li Keqiang and hold bilateral meetings with His Excellency Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China.
HE Prak Sokhon expressed his deep gratitude for China's great contribution to Cambodia's progress in many fields and reaffirmed its commitment to strengthen cooperation between the two countries in bilateral, regional and international frameworks. These include Mekong-Lang Chang, ASEAN cooperation, and the United Nations framework.
The bilateral talks between HE Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and State Councilor Wang Yi took place in a cordial and comprehensive environment. The two Foreign Ministers agreed that the current relationship and political trust between Cambodia and China, which is better than ever, is due to the frequent high-level exchanges, so this practice should be maintained.
The two sides agreed to work closely to ensure the successful implementation of the Cambodia-China Joint Community Building Action Plan 2019-2023, signed in April this year, aimed at bringing about security cooperation. Closer politics, expanding economic, trade and investment ties, and promoting growth, tourism and cultural exchanges.
Regarding ASEAN-China cooperation, the two Foreign Ministers pledged to work closely with other ASEAN member countries to strengthen the ASEAN-China Strategic Partnership and agreed to consider the possibility of fostering joint energy between ideas. Initiate the Belt and Road Initiative and the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan for the Benefit of Regional Development.
On the South China Sea issue, the two sides reaffirmed their support for the full and effective implementation of the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea (DOC) and the need to maintain the momentum of dialogue. ASEAN-China and joint efforts to achieve the Code of Conduct in the South China Sea (COC) within three years at the request of the Chinese side.
The two sides also discussed extensive developments in regional development, the impact of the Sino-US trade war, and further strengthening cooperation in international forums, as well as contributing to regional and global peace, security and development. .
