This is according to the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the 70th anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 18th anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 2 and the National Children's Day 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in this spirit to contribute to support the 70th anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 18th anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called as follows: :
1. The National Council of Cambodia for Children must continue to lead and implement the Convention on the Rights of the Child, disseminate and strengthen the implementation of legal documents related to child protection with the ministries, institutions, development partners, and civil society, effectively build additional legal documents with consideration. Child protection law to make the child protection system more comprehensive.
2: Ministries, institutions, all stakeholders, including the competent authorities, parents, guardians, communities and children must work together to find solutions, develop strategies to change social attitudes through education, counseling, positive teaching to children and must work together to solve and prevent all forms of violence against children. Appropriate and timely.
3: Ministries, relevant institutions, local authorities at all levels, development partners, civil society organizations must pay attention to consult with children every time to develop laws, policies, documents, norms related to their lives, needs, challenges and concerns. In particular, promote the comprehensive implementation of children's rights.
4: Continue to raise awareness and strengthen the implementation of the law on the prevention of domestic violence and the protection of victims and prepare legal documents for effective implementation of the law. Strengthen the implementation of action plans to prevent and respond to violence against children, contribute to the reduction and elimination of all forms of violence against children, to achieve the ASEAN Sustainable Development Goals and Action Plan on Violence against Children.
5: Ministries, institutions, local authorities, communities and all citizens must participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes, especially to take measures to protect children from all forms of violence, to educate children on how to protect themselves against abuse and sexual harassment in all its forms. Intimidate in any way and make children understand how to report to the authorities or their caregivers any forms of abuse.
6. Relevant ministries and institutions must continue to implement the core conventions of the International Labor Organization to eliminate all forms of child labor, raise awareness, train and disseminate the prevention of the use of child labor in all economic activities, and strengthen child labor inspection measures and mobilize resources. And the public movement to find appropriate solutions to save child labor.
7. All public and private radio and television stations, as well as social media, continue to promote the protection of children from all forms of violence and child labor, especially to strengthen the quality of the production of educational programs for children to prevent Prevent children from becoming victims.
8. Increase cooperation between relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities at all levels, development partners, national and international NGOs to prevent, intervene and provide appropriate and timely response services to contribute to the prevention of all forms of violence against children and Eliminate child labor in Cambodia.
