(Phnom Penh): The beautiful presenter of Bayon TV, Miss Sady, was chosen as the lucky star for the energy drinkers.
Mr. Michael Sovann, Head of Werk Award Management, said that Khmer Breweries decided to select Ms. Sady because she is a very eloquent presenter. On the other hand, she is a fan of energy drinks.
Mr. Michael added that Ms. Sady, in a simple blue-and-red dress of the energy drink, always travels everywhere to bring the prize of 40 million Riel to the winning customers from the earrings to the house.
Ms. Sady said, "I am very happy to be a part of changing the lives of Cambodians by bringing good luck to customers who have won from the earrings. I would also like to thank the company for choosing me as this lucky star.
Ms. Sady is determined to make the work of bringing good fortune to customers go well while her work as a TV presenter is still as usual. Cambodian Customs Chief Highly Committed to Implementing International Security Programs to Strengthen National, Regional and Global Security
(Tokyo, Japan): Dr. Kun Nhem, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, expressed his high commitment to participate in the implementation of international security programs in the context of prevention and counter-terrorism to strengthen national, regional and global security.
In this conference, Mr. Kun Nhim presented the results and experiences of the implementation of the "Asia-Pacific Security" project by the Cambodian Customs Administration. He said that in the context of the global threat of terrorism, the Cambodian Customs Administration not only strives to collect tax revenues and revenue into the national budget, security work is also an important part of the four pillars of the reform strategy and Customs modernization 2019-2023 of the Cambodian Customs.
He added that the participation in the implementation of the "Asia-Pacific Security" project is also part of the implementation of the "Strengthening Security" program of the Cambodian Customs, which requires cooperation in both national, regional and international frameworks.
He also mentioned Cambodia's efforts to combat money laundering and terrorist financing. In fact, the Royal Government has set out the "National Strategy on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing 2019-2023", which has a lot of work to be done by the Cambodian Customs Administration.
He also stressed that as a member of the World Customs Organization, Cambodia is highly committed to continuing to participate in international security programs in the context of counter-terrorism to strengthen national, regional and global security.
He also concluded that the World Customs Organization's Asia-Pacific Security Project can be successful only with the active participation of the customs administration in the Asia-Pacific region and relevant international institutions.
It should be noted that under the "Asia-Pacific Security" project, in addition to technical training related to the prevention of terrorism, the Cambodian Customs Administration also received some equipment / materials from the World Customs Organization, and those equipment / materials were put into use at the gate. Some important.
