Suspected case of killing a woman in Siem Reap, now the authorities came out to confirm that it was a suicide
(Siem Reap): A woman is suspected of being hanged in Phnov village, Sangkat Sambour, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, now the criminal police force of the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate came out to confirm the fact that Careful examination and research found that suicide.
The incident happened on the afternoon of May 29, 2019 at Phnov village, Sangkat Sambour, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, where the victim was 28-year-old Sok Vicheka.
Sok Vicheka and Pang Sophanna, a 39-year-old Cambodian man living in Canada, have been in love since April 2018 until January 24, 2019. Sok Vicheka and Pang Sophanna have agreed to be engaged. Elders on both sides participated.
Later, on February 11, 2019, Pang Sophana returned to Canada until May 28, 2019, Pang Sophana returned to Cambodia to prepare documents for his marriage to Sok. When Vicheka arrived, Pang Sophanna and Sok Vicheka usually lived together in a house in Phnov village, Sangkat Sambour, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, with Sok Srey Nuch living with them.
On May 29, 2019, at 9:00 AM, there was a dispute over 10 sets of cosmetics that Pang Sophanna brought from Canada for her fiancé to share with Sok Srey Nuch. Who was the younger brother of Sok Vicheka, but at that time, Sok Vicheka chose only good things, so Pang Sophanna was right.
Sok Vichheka then grabbed the steering wheel, causing the steering wheel to swerve. At that time, Pang Sophanna stopped the car and Sok Vichheka used his right hand on his head with four hands, then Sok Vicheka got out of the car. Into a stall near the parking lot, Pang Sophanna went down to negotiate, but was not able to drive back to Siem Reap.
According to the results of the joint investigation team led by Major General Tith Narong, the provincial commissioner, as well as Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth, the deputy commissioner in charge of criminal planning, and according to the relevant police force, Sok November actually committed suicide.
Currently, Pang Sophanna, with the approval of the Siem Reap Provincial Court representative, has been released on bail, while the family members of Sok Vicheka's body have agreed not to file a complaint and bail Pang. Sophanna to return to continue the funeral as well. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Establishes a Press and Quick Reaction Working Group to Respond to the Public in a Timed Time
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration held a meeting to organize a working group on information and quick reaction led by Mr. Kong Vithanak, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Chairman of the Information and Quick Reaction Team of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall on the 31st. May 2019.
Mr. Kong Vitan: "The establishment of this working group is to gather information and encourage the departments and units that own the case to respond in a timely and responsible manner to any issues that arise in their jurisdiction." "
According to the working group plan, the heads of all departments under the provincial supervision will be included as members of the working group under the supervision and coordination of a deputy provincial governor in charge of provincial information.
Principal of a high school in Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province, accused of pouring soil, encroaching on a canal, causing a dispute with the residents, the authorities have not yet resolved
(Prey Veng): The dumping of soil and encroachment on the canal by the principal of Kor Anteak High School caused the authorities to feel very dizzy because the aggressors of Ang Khsay did not respect the authorities' solution.
This controversial incident happened at the intersection of National Road 1 at the corner of ACLEDA Bank, Prasat Village, Prasat Commune, Kampong Trabek District, Prey Veng Province. The party that encroached on the canal land is known as Sao Art, the acting principal of Hun Sen Kandek High School, and the authorities have not yet resolved this issue.
According to the people living on the back of the canal, the canal is 4 meters wide and 5 kilometers long, connecting National Road No. 1 to the north, more than 2 kilometers long and more than 2 kilometers south. Km.
Residents said that last year, seeing that the canal was full of garbage and sewage, which affected the environment, especially the health of the people living on the back of the canal, the authorities planned to install a drainage system in the canal and pour. The concrete will be 2 meters on each side and the residents on the back of the canal will be required to pay $ 90 per person for the drainage, and the people will agree.
However, during the implementation of the project, the drainage contractor was not ready and it was easy. 130 meters long, without paying any money and violating the project of the authorities.
The villagers said that the land was poured almost half a meter higher than the sewer, causing the soil to fall into the sewer at the mouth of many bags. Sao Art refused to stop pouring soil, the soil still fell into the sewer again and again, causing a dispute between the people and the teacher, and so far the authorities have not resolved.
Mr. Yav Sanin, the governor of Kampong Trabek district, also confirmed that Mr. Sao Art had indeed poured soil into the canal and that he had ordered the officers to go down and arrest him several times, but he did not listen and kept stealing. Conflict arose, he was called in to settle, but he refused to enter. However, the district governor claimed that he would find a way to resolve this issue soon, without letting the wrongdoer do the arbitrary rainstorm.
