(Phnom Penh): The program to support about 760,000 Riel for women from poor families from pregnancy to children under two years old officially started on June 1, 2019. In the first phase, there are about 50,000 pregnant and postpartum women from poor families who will receive historical support.
Women from poor families who have had equity or priority cards in the past have been offered free pregnancy, childbirth and hospitalization services by the Royal Government. The decision to introduce an unprecedented new social protection policy is another consideration of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting the well-being of poor mothers and babies. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, considers the introduction of this new policy to be a meticulous consideration of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by the Cambodian People's Party, to alleviate the hardships of the general public after the Royal Government has done. Already financial support for women civil servants, the armed forces and workers when they give birth.
On the morning of June 1, 2019, the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, visited the program to provide cash to pregnant women and babies from poor families and inspected the implementation of this program at Referral Hospital "Samdech Ov Samdech Mey".
Families living in poverty when having children face many difficulties in life. The decision to subsidize the Royal Government in addition to not charging for these services has made mothers very happy.
In an interview with Fresh News, the mothers said that this decision shows the Royal Government's high concern for the well-being of mothers and children. Many mothers expressed their gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for launching this financial support program.
The Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, said that in the first phase, about 50,000 pregnant and postpartum women are under the program to receive funding.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the donation will cost nearly $ 5 million in the first year, increase to $ 7.7 million in the second year and continue to increase to more than $ 10 million in the third year. However, this expenditure will not affect the flow of the national budget, and Samdech expects that the amount of subsidies will decrease when the living standards of the people improve.
According to the joint statement of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Health, the 760,000 Riels is divided into three phases. The first stage is during pregnancy is to pay 4 times 40,000 Riel, the second stage is to give 200,000 Riel at birth and the third stage is after childbirth until the child under two. The year is to pay 10 times 40,000 riels at a time.
The statement also stated that in case of pregnancy and miscarriage, support is also provided. In that, if the unborn child is 12 weeks old, he / she will receive a subsidy of 40,000 Riels at a time. If the miscarried child is between 12 weeks and 24 weeks old, he / she will receive a subsidy of 40,000 Riels twice.
