A police officer who drove a car hit and killed and injured in Sen Sok district must be sent to court for legal action, the perpetrator's family pays additional compensation to the victim
(Phnom Penh): A police officer who drove a car and hit two motorcycles, causing one victim to die and another to be injured, came to solve and was sent to court for legal action on the morning of June 1, 2019 This is when the family comes forward to pay additional compensation to the victims.
The accident happened on the night of May 29, 2019 on Street 1019, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, caused by 38-year-old Ly Leang Chheng, a four-and-a-half-year-old police officer living at 12B Street. Lum, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok.
Colonel Sem Kunthea, Director of the Traffic Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News this morning, May 1, that after the incident, the police officer came to the office to be responsible for The law is its fault.
He added that after the interrogation today, the competent authorities have prepared a case to send the perpetrator to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action, and the perpetrator's family has come forward to pay compensation. The families of the two victims as well.
