Beijing prepares to list foreign companies endangering Chinese companies
BEIJING: China's Ministry of Commerce announced on Friday that it would draft a list of foreign companies, institutions and individuals that Beijing considers harmful to Chinese companies. This is according to a quote from Reuters on Friday night, May 31, 2019.
The move, which did not name any specific countries or companies, comes amid escalating tensions between the Sino-US trade war and the aftermath of Washington's decision to name the tech giant. China's Huawei is on a blacklist that bans US companies from doing business with the company without permission.
According to Gao Feng, a spokesman for the Chinese Ministry of Commerce, any foreign companies, organizations or individuals who will be on the list are in violation of market competition laws, violating the spirit of contracting, blocking supply to companies for no reason. Clearly or poses a serious threat to the rights as well as legitimate interests of Chinese companies.
The Chinese Ministry of Commerce will release more details on the list soon.
