Preah Sihanouk: A 100-megawatt coal-fired power plant was officially inaugurated in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone on May 31, 2019 under the presidency of Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Mr. Sey. XU LEJIANG, Vice Chairman of the China Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry
ZHOU HAIJIANG, President of Hodo Group, said that over the past 10 years, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has developed an area of 5 square kilometers in the first phase, attracting enterprises from China, Europe and other countries in the region. ASEAN has 161 enterprises employing 29,000 people with production lines such as garments, bags and suitcases, construction materials and kitchen utensils.
The special economic zone has developed the second phase of a coal-fired power plant project with five boilers and four generators capable of generating 100 megawatts of electricity. In the first phase, the power plant installed three boilers and two generators. After the completion of the first phase, the coal-fired power plant will be able to supply 190 million kilowatts of electricity and 540,000 tons of thermal energy.
He said that the coal-fired power plant ensures the stable supply of thermal power and electricity in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, it helps to improve the business structure and expand the business size, production line, improve the efficiency of regional competition. The second phase of special economic development to promote the construction of Sihanoukville Economic Zone has become a win-win project of the "One Belt One Road".
