Based on the records of the Council for the Development of Cambodia from 1994 to the first quarter of 2019, the Council for the Development of Cambodia registered 137 investment projects of Japanese companies with a total investment capital of approximately $ 2.5 billion. Focuses on the production of electrical and electronic components, auto parts and technical equipment, agro-industry, food processing, hotels, tourism, hospitals and supermarkets.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said, "This year, Cambodia is facing a shortage of electricity due to the weather, which makes our hydropower plants have not enough water, so we ask Japan to consider studying the power grid, especially Previous discussions between Jica and the Ministry of Mines and Energy, which visited the Lao-Cambodian border to Phnom Penh, which is 350 kilometers long.
The Prime Minister also reminded that the construction of the power grid, which is supported by the Japanese government to Cambodia, is designed to draw electricity from Laos and aims to increase electricity in Cambodia as consumption increases. Up from day to day.
Recall that in the dry season in 2019, Cambodia experienced severe drought, especially during April and May, the temperature rose to 40 to 42 degrees due to the indirect effects of El Nino (El Nino). The power grid can not produce enough power. Cambodia is short of about 400 megawatts of electricity, and Cambodia is also negotiating to buy 200 megawatts of electricity from Turkey.
Regarding the shortage of electricity, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, called on the people to be patient and understanding. Samdech stated that the lack of electricity has not affected the production line in factories yet, because Cambodia still has more than 1,000 megawatts of electricity.
