Kandal Provincial Military Arrests Man After Stabbing Another Man for Anger at Ang Snoul
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Armed Forces arrested a man after stabbing another man with a knife, causing him to be injured because he could not love the victim's wife when he was not married. This incident happened on May 30, 2019 at the point of the road in Kor Ko village, Samrong Leu commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
According to the report of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, in accordance with the core task of the Gendarmerie for Prevention, Suppression and Rescue, which is an effective leadership mechanism of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie. And Mr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, the Armed Forces immediately investigated the case and arrested the suspect on May 31, 2019.
Kandal Provincial Military confirmed that the suspect was Chuob Kong Tang, alias Rany, 29, a car mechanic, currently residing in Prey Sambok village, Penay commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province. Separately, the victim, Savon Chivoan, 27 years old, a driver living in Koh Kabay village, Samrong Leu commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, was injured in the right chest and back of the head, stabbed with a sharp knife and sent to the hospital.
Police described that before the incident, the suspect rode a motorcycle alone to buy a knife to stab the victim, but when he arrived home did not meet the victim and then riding a motorcycle to watch Road because the victim used to ride to get his wife every day. But when riding, did not see the victim, met the victim's wife (the suspect used to love), she did not talk to the suspect.
Under the direct guidance of Brigadier General Sam Tola, Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, the expert conducted a search with high willingness and led to his arrest. In front of the police, the victim confessed that he really used a knife to stab the real victim, and now the suspect is detained and is building a case to continue the procedure.
