(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yim Nol Sorn, Vice Chairman of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council and Chairman of the Legal Standards Executive Committee, stated that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has considered the private sector as its head. An important machine in promoting national economic growth and a real partner in national development.
Mr. Yim Nol Sorn also added that in order to achieve this goal, the Royal Government has been continuing to implement and develop policies, legal frameworks and legal standards to support the development of the private sector to be stronger and more prosperous. Therefore, the implementation of RIA is an important contribution to this effort.
He added that as a member of the International Trade Organization (WTO) and a member of the ASEAN Economic Community, Cambodia must be highly competitive in international markets. Therefore, businesses can not bear the high cost of obligations because it makes them less productive and less competitive.
"This RIA approach will require ministries and agencies to clearly assess the impact of all regulatory proposals or laws and regulations in force to avoid or minimize the negative impact on business." This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Yim Nol Sorn.
Mr. Yim Nol Sorn also added that the establishment of RIA working groups in ministries - institutions will really help strengthen the effectiveness and efficiency of those laws and regulations.
