(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) this morning held its 7th General Meeting of Shareholders in the presence of Mr. Sim Nara, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority. Phnom Penh will be attended by many board members and shareholders.
Speaking at the conference, Mr. Sim Nara confirmed the results that the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority strives to achieve in 2018, including:
He said that after the distribution of profits according to the statute of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority in the 11th session on March 27, the Board of Directors unanimously agreed to keep the profit of 47,321,091,148 Riels. $ 11 million) for future investment and the remaining amount of 18,925,360,051 Riels (nearly $ 5 million) to distribute dividends to shareholders.
Mr. Sim Nara also said that in 2019, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority must continue its operations to be successful, including plans to sell more than 214 million cubic meters of water with a new distribution network. 250 km extension and 22,000 new customer networks.
He said that in order to achieve this goal, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority plans to launch the Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant with a capacity of 52,000 cubic meters per day by the end of 2019, in addition to the current production capacity of 560,000 cubic meters. In one day. Thus, by the end of 2019, the total production capacity will increase to 612,000 cubic meters per day.
