According to the report of Mr. Hong Chan Sokha, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Speu Province, in the first three months of 2019, there were 48/35 traffic accidents in Kampong Speu Province, an increase of 12 deaths. 41 people / 23 people increased 9 people seriously injured 41 people / 34 people increased 7 people slightly injured 27 people / 27 people Total damage 102 units / 71 units increased 31 units.
The director of the department confirmed that the accident was caused by speeding, driving through, not respecting the right of way, overtaking in an accident, driving under the influence of alcohol.
(Kratie): Police in Chhlong district, Kratie province, in cooperation with Dambe district police in Tbong Khmum province, arrested a suspect who beat his wife to death and escaped. Tbong Khmum province on the evening of May 30, 2019.
Chhlong district police said on May 31 that a case of intentional violence with aggravated circumstances occurred on the evening of May 30 due to the death of the victim, Yok Moch, a 52-year-old female, at the point of the canal in Pralay village. Treak, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province, is the wife of the perpetrator, Suon Piseth, 49 years old, living with the victim.
Police said that the couple always quarreled every day, and on the day of the incident, arguing about grandchildren walking, then the suspect, the husband, rode away on a motorcycle, did not hear the neighbors, went upstairs to look The house suddenly saw the victim's wife lying dead, they immediately called to report to the police.
Police said that from the examination of the body from the technical officer, we can conclude that the victim died because her husband beat and hit the pig's leg with a nail about 7 times long, hit the right neck, causing death at the scene. After activating, the suspect, her husband, escaped on a motorcycle, after which the Chhlong district police cooperated with the Dambe district police to arrest him.
The suspect is currently being held at the Chhlong District Police Inspectorate in Kratie Province to build a case according to legal procedures. National Assembly Presidents Cambodia and Laos Agree to Strengthen and Expand Cooperation
(Laos): Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, during an official and friendly visit there this morning, May 31, 2019, met with Mrs. Paniya Thotou, President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
The meeting was held in a pleasant and cordial atmosphere, with the two National Assembly Presidents praising the traditional friendship, solidarity and cooperation between the two countries in both the legislative and executive branches.
On behalf of the National Assembly, representing the people of the two countries, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and Mrs. Paniya Thotou discussed many issues in the fields of economy, trade, education and social affairs for the benefit of the people of both countries.
The Presidents of the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos have pledged to urge the two governments to effectively and comprehensively implement all agreements signed between them. Regarding the cooperation between the two parliaments, Samdech Heng Samrin said that the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos, in addition to supporting each other in the inter-parliamentary forum, and the two parliaments signed a memorandum of understanding to strengthen and expand cooperation. Even better.
The President of the National Assembly of Cambodia said that over the past five terms, the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos have enhanced cooperation to exchange experiences on the work of the National Assembly, both at the level of leaders, expert committees and technical officers of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly. The two countries will continue to support the cooperation of the two governments.
Ms. Panya Toto supported the statement made by Samdech Heng Samrin and requested that Samdech continue to promote and enhance good cooperation between the two parliaments.
At the same time, she said that if there is an exchange of visits between the two parliaments at any level, there should be a clear theme for deeper and more effective cooperation. Samdech's current visit to Laos is at the General Secretariat of the National Assembly of the two countries, with a chairman to discuss.
43 Koh Kong Environment Officials Sworn in to Be Chief Justice's Staff to Crack Down on Natural Resource Crimes
(Koh Kong): In order to become good officials to serve the people, loyal to the Royal Government, 43 environmental officials of National Parks in Koh Kong Province were sworn in at the Provincial Court on May 30, 2019 to have the right to become The Chief of Staff of the Judicial Officer shows his sincerity in working to strengthen the capacity to protect, conserve and crack down on natural resource crimes that have been encroached upon more effectively.
The swearing-in ceremony of the 43 environmental officials was presided over by Mr. Min Makara, President of Koh Kong Provincial Court, Mr. Ros Saram, Provincial Prosecutor, and many other stakeholders.
He stated that his team strives to be a good official and implement the law that the government and the Royal Government submitted to crack down on the crime of deforestation of the state's natural forest by some corrupt people.
Mr. Min Makara said that the 43 environmental officials who were sworn in to become judicial police officers could not do it alone. Therefore, it is necessary to abide by the law and cooperate with the head of the unit and the provincial court at all times in case of completing the mission effectively.
(Phnom Penh): The police force of Po Sen Chey district has launched a hot operation to crack down on 4 active thieves who seize the property of people traveling on the streets.
For this operation, the police cracked down on the two thieves, while the other two escaped. During the crackdown, three members of the Por Sen Chey district police force were seriously injured during the operation.
Mr. Yim Saran, Police Inspector of Por Senchey District, told Fresh News on May 31, 2019 that the operation took place immediately after the suspect shocked the people at 7 o'clock. May 30, 2019 on Concrete Road, Sangkat Kakap I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the Por Senchey District Police Officer, prior to the incident, the Special Intervention Force of the Por Senchey District Police Inspectorate patrolled the local crime scene to protect the safety of the people under the direct command of Mr. Yim Saran, patrolling the vulnerable areas. Accident on National Road 4, Sangkat Choam Chao III.
Suddenly, when they met the suspect as an old subject, there were 4 of them riding 2 motorbikes, then they threw their hands on the radio to contact the force throughout the district and chased almost the whole district for almost an hour, then the suspect hit the motorbike of the police force, causing him to fall. Three people were seriously injured in the operation, and two suspects were arrested, while the other two escaped.
According to the inspector, the suspect who was arrested confessed that he had committed several electric shocks and had robbed a motorbike with more than 10 other members, and now they were planning another robbery, but the police cracked down before the action.
After the incident, the victim was sent to the hospital immediately. The two suspects have now been sent to the Criminal Division of the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate for legal action. Tbong Khmum Governor Gives Compassion to Community Kindergarten Children by Rebuilding Classrooms After Windstorm
