NagaWorld Wins Asian Responsible Enterprise Award 2019
This award recognizes the work of NagaWorld, which has helped promote social development and nation-building, leading a community-based sports development initiative, the "Football Development Program in Kampong Speu Province in Cambodia".
Organized by Asian Enterprises, the AREA Awards recognize companies and organizations that have the best CSR program for society. This year, more than 200 applications from 16 countries across Asia were submitted to the selection committee.
NagaWorld Managing Director Pern Chen said: “We are very honored that our community development work has been recognized. The football development program in Kampong Speu provides opportunities for young people to develop and improve their football skills. First, this program has trained and improved sports coaching skills for all sports teachers in the province.
"Secondly, it provides an opportunity for our talented young players to improve their skills by participating in international competitions and exchanging players with local football clubs." Young people are the future of the nation and we hope to play a part in helping them become the best athletes for Cambodia.
Pern Chen added that NagaWorld has organized a mini-football tournament under the age of 18 with the participation of more than 600 students with the aim of encouraging young players to show off their skills and gain experience and confidence. From live field matches.
