Lt. Gen. Chea Pov, Director of the Department of Technology Crimes, said that the young man was arrested on May 30, 2019 at the intersection of Street 182, Sangkat Teuk Laok 2, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh by his department. Led by Major General Siv Chhean in collaboration with the Office of Technology Crimes of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
This young man named Krouch Sichay, Khmer, born on May 17, 1997, unspecified occupation, his hometown is Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, his current address is Street 1981, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok. The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and was coordinated by Deputy Prosecutor Riel Sophin.
According to the general director of the department, the victim filed a complaint for hacking into another person's Facebook account without permission and then borrowed money from a friend on Facebook, requiring him to send money through a money transfer company. In the past, the Technology Crime Department has received many complaints from victims.
