The court adjourned the trial of Rath Rathmony in the video production of "My mother sold me" to June 12 (Phnom Penh): After the hearing ended on the evening of May 30, 2019, Trial Judge Koy Sao took the case. The trial is set to resume on June 12, 2019.
However, during the hearing, the accused, Rat Rathmony, claimed, "I was just a translator, and I did not know about the filming and video editing."
Mr. Rath Rathmony was detained by the court on December 13, 2018 after the Thai authorities arrested him and sent him back to the Cambodian government at the request of the Cambodian side in connection with the production of the video "My mother sold me" which It is a form of dissemination of false information that leads to the disgrace of Cambodia.
The video, titled "My mother sells me," tells the story of a Cambodian woman who sells her daughter due to poverty and describes the state of the sex trade in Cambodia. This video made the Royal Government perceive it as a slander of the honor, dignity and dignity of Cambodian women and affect the honor of Cambodia.
