Minibir Mitsubishi, headquartered in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, was established in 1951. Seeing the potential for investment in Cambodia, the company started operating in Cambodia in 2011 to produce small motors, fan motors, ball bearings, etc.
After a period of operation, the company has expanded its production line to produce lighting, glass, mobile phones, vibrators for games, computers, electronic circuits, LED panels, measuring instruments, and most recently, LED lighting systems in public squares in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap city.
The company recently signed an agreement with the Football Federation of Cambodia to become an official partner for two years to contribute to the promotion of football in Cambodia.
Cambodian National Council for Children strongly condemns and calls on the authorities to arrest the perpetrators of the rape and murder of two siblings in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian National Council for Children issued a statement on May 30, 2019, strongly condemning and calling on the authorities to pay attention and take strict action against atrocities. Of the criminal who raped and killed two siblings in Sihanoukville yesterday. The victim is Pha Sokly, more than 2 years old, and the older girl is Pha Srey Leak, almost 10 years old.
The Cambodian National Council for Children considers this act to be a serious violation of the right to life, the right to protection, the right to development and participation of children.
According to the press release, the Cambodian National Council for Children calls on all levels of competent authorities to pay attention and take strict legal action against the perpetrators of such inhumane acts so that such acts do not occur. New in society.
Please be informed that this brutal murder was caused by the perpetrator who raped a girl almost 10 years old and then killed both the girl and the child over 2 years old who were sleeping in the same house.
The younger brother died instantly in the house and the older sister was rescued by her family as far as Phnom Penh, but could not save her life and died in the car at 8 pm the same day.
Major General Chuon Narin, the provincial police commissioner, and his wife and colleagues, who were very sympathetic, also donated 1 million riel and a coffin fee, as well as budget for the cremation ceremony. The suffix of the Commission as well. At the same time, the commissioner would like to announce that he will arrest the perpetrators and bring them to justice.
