He said that the Rural Development Bank has provided loans to support agricultural production chains to farmers from small to large, regardless of the trend, and the provision of loans at favorable interest rates.
This statement was made by the Director General of the Development Bank on the occasion that he was invited to participate in the signing ceremony of the pure rice seed production agreement between the rice farming community and the green company under the chairmanship of Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province. Mr. Oknha Phu Puy, General Director of Green Company and attended by representatives of a total of 21 rice seed farming communities in Battambang province.
On that occasion, Mr. Kao Thach, General Director of Rural Development Bank, congratulated the rice farming community for reaching an agreement to supply pure rice seeds to green companies at a fixed price. As a result, farmers will no longer have to worry about prices and market issues when the produce is produced.
Mr. Kao Thach strongly believes that through the rice seed supply agreement with a clear selling price from the green company will make your production sustainable and in the coming season, farmers in Battambang will have good rice varieties for Cultivation. In addition, the Rural Development Bank is ready to provide credit financing to support the farming community for this pure rice seed project with the most favorable interest rates.
Mr. Kao Thach also requested the rice seed production community to produce high quality and clear standards, in which Mr. Kao Thach requested technical assistance from the Department of Agriculture of Battambang to check the quality of rice seeds before supply. Enter the market and continue to ask for support for this project from the Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors.
He is confident that today's agreement will lead to positive changes in rice cultivation, reduce production costs and increase yields in farmers' production chains.
According to Phu Puy, the purpose of the agreement is to encourage farmers to increase their income, reduce production costs and increase rice yields to meet market demand. At the same time, the green company will supply quality fertilizers and set up a laboratory to check the quality of rice seeds, with technicians to help farmers.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, highly appreciated and appreciated the green company for co-organizing this pure rice seed production agreement, and the Governor thanked the Rural Development Bank for its participation. Support this project as well.
