The Public Financial Management Reform Program, a long-term reform program with an ambitious and realistic vision, is to transform Cambodia's public financial system toward international excellence by building and strengthening the four core components: improving the system , Legal framework, institutional mechanisms and human resources. Public financial management reform is to be organized sequentially in the context of the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
