The NEC has posted the results of the council elections at the NEC Secretariat of the Capital and Provinces.
Eligible voters in the capital, provinces, municipalities, districts or Khans or representatives of political parties who have a list of candidates have the right to complain to the NEC about the provisional results of the election of each council. No later than 3 days after the posting of provisional results.
According to the law and the calendar of the third mandate council election, the deadline to appeal the provisional results is June 4, 2019. This is according to the NEC announcement.
