National Assembly High-Level Delegation Led by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Continues Visit to Laos
(Lao): On the afternoon of May 30, 2019, a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia led by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, arrived safely in the Lao People's Democratic Republic for an official visit. The three-day friendship in this country is from May 30 to June 1, 2019 at the invitation of Mrs. PANY YATHOTOU, President of the Lao National Assembly.
The high-level parliamentary delegation's visit to Laos comes after a three-day visit to Vietnam. At the Vientiane International Airport, the delegation was warmly welcomed by the Lao National Assembly.
According to the plan, on the morning of May 31, the President of the National Assembly will hold bilateral talks with Ms. PANY YATHOTUO, President of the Lao National Assembly, to further strengthen the friendship and solidarity between the two countries, especially the cooperation between the two parliaments. To all corners. Malaysian Prime Minister: The world is now more chaotic, so it is necessary to create a new system to solve the problem ...
TOKYO (Reuters) - Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad has said the world is in a state of disarray, which requires a new legal system that allows countries to resolve disputes through negotiations and arbitration. . This was released by Channel News Asia on the evening of Thursday, May 30, 2019.
Mahathir made the remarks at a press conference on Thursday on the sidelines of the 25th International Forum on the Future of Asia in Japan. "The current world order seems to be failing ... and this failure is because we like to take violent steps and threaten each other when differences cannot be resolved," the 93-year-old prime minister said. "We can agree."
According to Mahathir, the world now needs a new system based on the rule of law that allows countries to resolve disputes through fair negotiations and arbitration. But to get the new system, he also stressed that the world must all decide that all disputes must be reconciled at the negotiating table.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Urges Police Officers to Cooperate with Armed Forces and People to Solve and Facilitate Traffic on Roads
(Preah Sihanouk): Such encouragement was made during the meeting to review the work results for May on the morning of May 30, 2019. It should be noted that while Sihanoukville is developing rapidly, the living standard of the people has improved, the number of vehicles and the number of people coming to live, do business or work in this province have also increased today.
Traffic jams are also occurring almost daily and on all roads. This issue has also caused a great deal of controversy. To address this concern, Sihanoukville Governor Yon Min is meeting to find a way out.
In the future, urge traffic police officers to cooperate with the military police and the people to work together to solve and facilitate traffic on the road better so that this congestion does not continue to affect. To the feelings of the people and travelers.
At the same time, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration also presented a number of solutions, such as: to set up roadblocks on major roads, to be one-way roads, to widen roads or to repair roads between cities, urging police and local authorities to help with arrests. Disorderly parking on the streets, addressing the use of sidewalks as a place for shopping and other businesses, restricting the implementation of legal measures and fines for those who park illegally on the streets.
The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province plans to provide another crane to the Sihanoukville Municipality to facilitate the lifting of trucks parked on the road. All must work together responsibly.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor highlighted that the challenges include: traffic congestion, security, arrest, kidnapping of Chinese people, construction management, solid waste construction, water, electricity, damaged roads, land grabbing. The use of sidewalks as a place to shop, the settlement of land disputes, the issue of land anarchy and the lack of public services.
However, Yun Min encouraged the efforts of all officials in performing their duties, with remarkable results. At the same time, Mr. Yun Min also reminded that related to local challenges, local authorities are the closest.
He reminded that local officials must take measures to prevent and resolve immediately or report immediately, but if can not be resolved to report to higher levels to take measures to avoid colluding with them.
In addition, he reminded the Department of Land Management to prepare land titles for the people in the upper warehouse area as soon as possible after this area was cut off by the Royal Government.
In this case, the provincial governor confirmed that he had previously requested the Department of Land Management since Nuon Pok was the director of the department. In addition, the provincial governor also informed the representative of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Prosecutor's Office about the land case in the Kbal Chhay area after some individuals filed a claim for land management with an old title that had been revoked by the government. References.
He confirmed that the land in Kbal Chhay area has been revoked and confiscated by the government in the past, but part of it has been given to the Sihanoukville provincial administration to arrange for the exchange of people who actually live there. In this case, the governor asked the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court to know.
In the case of cardholders who have long been deported by the state to claim management rights, the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province believes that this is just a complaint, lest some can be returned, but this case is not possible.
