Minister Mam Bunheng: The Royal Government pays high attention to the development of human resources in the health sector to provide better medical services to the people
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has paid high attention to the development of human resources in the health sector with knowledge, professionalism, virtue and responsibility. Need to treat and save the people for the better.
Each year, the Royal Government provides about 600 to 700 scholarships, which is 10% of the students enrolled in the University of Health Sciences (CSU). In addition, the University of Health Sciences, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Katibandit Bun Rany Hun Sen have provided scholarships to specialized medical students, who are now 5 generations and a total of 154 people.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that the Ministry of Health also continues to make efforts to promote training focusing on skills, including soft skills, to strengthen the training with quality, virtue, good attitude and high professional ethics.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of presiding over the charity program of the University of Health Sciences 2019 under the theme "Youth, Sharing and Smiling" on May 30, 2019.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that in the past, the University of Health Sciences has provided opportunities for students to participate in social activities, provide free community health services and other humanitarian activities that are beneficial to our Cambodian society. .
At the same time, Professor Saphon Vattanak, Rector of the University of Health Sciences, said that the charity program organized by the university has helped 28 poor students pay tuition fees, support Kantha Bopha Hospital with some funds and help some poor children. In Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province, it is a study material.
