Mr. Naoto Si Okada's appreciation was made during his courtesy call and some work discussion with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on May 30, 2019.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, during the meeting, Mr. Naoto Si Okada praised the Prime Minister's strategy for economic reform in Cambodia to bring progress. He added that he had heard in many media outlets about Cambodia's progress in the economic, social and other fields.
The Prime Minister emphasized that there are two main factors that make Cambodia's economy grow and develop sustainably. The two factors include: First. Peace and political stability, and the second essential is macroeconomic stability.
Samdech Techo added that these two factors must be maintained and these two factors must be interdependent. Therefore, peace, political stability and macroeconomic status must be maintained. Then good governance is required to drive development. Samdech Techo emphasized that dirty governance can not bring success. Therefore, for Cambodia to continue to reform, especially to improve where necessary.
The Prime Minister also pointed out that Cambodia in 2001 did not have enough food by importing food from abroad, but later we became a country that exports food such as rice, we have 3 million tons left for export. So Cambodia has become a food importer to a food exporter.
The Prime Minister said that in order to promote the development of this country, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025. Samdech Techo stated that all these are efforts to promote the national budget to increase in order to enable Cambodia to address the needs as well as infrastructure construction.
Samdech Techo also pointed out that related to this progress, Cambodia also has an increase in the number of people who have a much better life. Despite Cambodia's progress, Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia still needs assistance from Japan to promote the country's development even better.
The Prime Minister also expressed hope that investors from Japan will invest more in Cambodia, despite the current increase in the number of investors from Japan, and Samdech still wants to see those who take from Japan goes further.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also invited Mr. Naoto Si Okada to visit Cambodia.
