The speech of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made at the 25th International Conference on "The Future of Asia" in Tokyo, Japan this morning, May 30, 2019.
At the international conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the theme of this year's forum is "The Search for a New World Order: Overcoming Chaos" which is very important and appropriate in the current context and for the future of our region. Faced with complex challenges and uncertain evolutionary trends due to various threats and the current turmoil of world order and globalization.
"In this sense, our regional leaders should consider and stand together on solutions to the major challenges that are threatening the world and our Asia in the current circumstances, especially the protectionist current, the trade war between them," he said. "Great powers and geopolitical crises."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen concluded that for the long term, the world must continue to face many other major structural changes, including: demographics of the elderly and young, connectivity. , Energy security, water and environmental issues, as well as technological advances, which require all of us to work together to increase closer cooperation to find appropriate solutions.
