He said that this is why Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, has always advised the local authorities as well as the authorities at all levels to pay attention to the situation of the people who have been in danger like this and Help each other, give you the opportunity to restore what was damaged, that is, help you solve every time you face this difficulty.
(Siem Reap): A Chinese man threw his suitcase at the Siem Reap International Airport because he was charged more than $ 80, which surprised the authorities and CMAC officials to check Suddenly, at first there was a suspicion of planting a bomb.
According to the inspections of the specialized police officers and CMAC officers, the results showed that only the clothes and coffee were in the suitcase, not the powder that caused the explosion.
On the afternoon of May 30, 2019, the National Police Commissioner General Neth Savoeun told Fresh News that the Chinese man was detained after throwing his suitcase at the airport. The suitcase contained clothes and coffee and was taken to the CMAC for further inspection.
In addition, a police officer at the Department of Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime also confirmed that the shock occurred at around 11 a.m., caused by a Chinese man preparing to fly back to Macau, but due to luggage. At the airport, he was required to pay another $ 80, so he left his suitcase.
The police officer added that after the Chinese dropped the suitcase, the police and CMAC officers went to check only the clothes and the coffee bag, not the bomb.
