Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department Holds a Meeting to Implement Cash Support Program for Pregnant Women and Children Under 2 Years of Equitable Cards
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Ke Ratha, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department, this morning, May 30, 2109, chaired a meeting to introduce the implementation of cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age with equity card. Or priority card. The event was attended by the Director of the District Health Office, the Director of the Hospital and the Director of the Health Center.
Mr. Ke Ratha stated that this cash support program will be implemented from June 1, 2019 onwards, in accordance with Inter-Ministerial Proclamation No. 524 MEF.PrK dated May 21, 2019 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Ministry of Health.
According to the director of the department, the identification of poor pregnant women to get a card must be carried out in accordance with the equity program for poor women, which allows the health center to evaluate and identify poor women and give priority cards.
By implementing assessment tools such as equity programs for poor women in referral hospitals. There are three members of the above identification committee: one district director and two staff members. Each card is valid for 2 years.
Mr. Ke Ratha said that the cash support program will be run by the data management program via mobile phone and computer system, after the woman and her 2-year-old child have already received health care services and will receive public services, officials will provide Wing Account Card for direct cash at WING Agent branches nationwide.
Please be informed that according to the inter-ministerial prakas on the implementation of the cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age, the family has an equity card or priority card for pregnant women to receive services at public health facilities in the following stages: 1: Provide 40,000 Riels for each visit to receive a pregnancy test, which provides a maximum of four times before childbirth.
The second stage provides a subsidy of 200,000 riels only once during childbirth and the third stage provides 40,000 riels at a time, a maximum of 10 times. Three times when receiving a postpartum check-up and seven times when a child is vaccinated until the child is 2 years old.
