Vietnamese PM asks Samdech Heng Samrin to boost Cambodia-Vietnam trade volume to reach 5 billion USD
The Prime Minister said this on the occasion of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia to pay a courtesy call at the Government House in Hanoi on May 29, 2019.
Nguyen Sun Phuc considers the visit of the National Assembly President to Vietnam as a good opportunity at a time when both countries' economies are growing at the same time. At the same time, the Prime Minister expressed his pleasure to see that the relationship between the two parliaments has been good, strong and constantly growing.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that the current visit of Samdech and his delegation to Vietnam is the first foreign visit of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature, a new legislature emerging from the general election in the middle of the year. 2018.
At the invitation of National Assembly President Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin, the visit was fruitful and contributed to further strengthening the traditional friendship, solidarity and comprehensive cooperation between the two countries. In particular, to strengthen the cooperation between the two legislatures to grow further.
Samdech informed the Prime Minister that during the visit, the two National Assembly signed a Memorandum of Understanding to further strengthen and enhance cooperation within the two countries' legislatures, especially the promotion of gender and youth parliaments. Technical level of both Secretariats. The two parliaments have always cooperated and supported each other in bilateral, multilateral, regional and international frameworks.
The National Assembly President and the Prime Minister of Vietnam praised the achievements of the two countries in demarcating the border between 84% to turn the border into a zone of peace, friendship, cooperation and development to be passed on to future generations. .
It should be noted that Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin has been leading a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia on a three-day official and friendly visit to Vietnam from May 28 to 30, 2019.
During the meeting, the two sides also discussed plans to hold the Cambodia-Vietnam-Laos Front Conference in Cambodia in 2020.
