Federation of Democratic Students of Cambodia: The Third Mandate Council Election is Fair, Transparent, Free and Fair
(Phnom Penh): The Student Federation of Democratic Scholars of Cambodia, which sent young volunteers to observe the 3rd Mandate Council Election, issued a statement saying that the 3rd Mandate Council Election last Sunday went smoothly. Accurate, transparent, free and acceptable justice.
On the basis of independence, democracy and neutrality, the National Observers of the Federation of Democratic Students of Cambodia observed:
* There are 7 political parties competing in the election of Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, District Council for the third mandate in 2019.
* The election process from the beginning to the end of the election is conducted smoothly in a good political environment.
* The vote counting process was conducted accurately and transparently, with the presence of agents of each political party, national and international observers and journalists monitoring and protesting in case of any irregularities.
Based on a practical overview of the election process, the Federation of Democratic Students of Cambodia, a group of national observers with the eyes of justice, highly appreciated the smooth, fair, transparent, and acceptable and fair election process. Declared support for the voting process organized by the NEC as an independent institution.
