The measures put forward by the Royal Government have two main parts: improving trade facilitation and reducing business costs and the legal framework for investment in Cambodia:
A: Improving trade facilitation and reducing business costs
1. Termination of the permanent role of the General Department of CamControl by keeping only the customs agents in the inspection of goods at the international gates, special economic zones and other export-import inspection points.
2: Abolition of the Cambodian Naval Agency, called Kamsap.
4: Reduction of the number of holidays and holidays from 28 days to 21 days, which will be implemented from 2020 onwards.
B: Legal framework on investment in Cambodia
