Camcontrol Officers Find Jelly-Injected Shrimp at Leu Market, Tumnup Rolok Market, Crab Market and Fresh Seafood Depot in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): Officials of CamControl Preah Sihanouk Branch on May 29, 2019, in cooperation with the officials of the Provincial Department of Commerce, the Market Commission and the local authority, continued to disseminate the quality of food safety, inspect food products and pre-packaged goods at Phsar Leu, Tumnup Rolok Market, Fresh Seafood Distribution Depot and Khmer Crab Market in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the Sihanoukville CamControl branch, the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and the presence of banned chemicals that could harm people's health.
During the inspection, officials took some food samples for preliminary testing, including fresh shrimp, squid, and oysters to find banned chemicals that could harm people's health. At the same time, professional officers inspected for non-compliance on the packaging of food products.
According to CamControl officials, as a result, the officers found 80 kilograms of shrimp with jelly-like substance in booth 826. After that, the officers made a record to confiscate and burn it according to the procedure and asked the traders to make a contract. Stop selling unhealthy foods.
On the same day, officials instructed other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid harm to health, people will be able to face the law.
