Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Participating in a Seminar on Investment in Cambodia in Tokyo, Japan
(Tokyo-Japan): On the morning of May 29, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over a seminar on investment in Cambodia held in Tokyo, Japan during an official visit to attend an international conference. The 25th edition of Asia's Future and more events from May 29 to 31, 2019.
A seminar on investing in Cambodia was organized by the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) and the Mizuho Bank of Japan, with the participation of many Japanese investors.
The purpose of this workshop is to enable Japanese investors to learn first-hand about socio-economic growth, investment opportunities and potential in Cambodia, as well as to be aware of the current implementation of new measures by the Royal Government of Cambodia. Improve the business and investment environment.
In fact, tomorrow, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and I will witness the signing of an exchange of letters on a grant of 339 million yen for human resource development scholarships and a container project in Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Special Economic Zone in the amount of 200 million yen.
Within the framework of formal cooperation financing, from 1992 to 2018, the Japanese friend provided a substantial official cooperation financing of more than 2.8 billion US dollars, equivalent to about 15% of the total financing of all development partners for development. Cambodian socio-economic.
Phnom Penh, the heart of the Kingdom of Cambodia, will also be a major hub along the economic corridor and will further push Cambodia to become a destination for Japanese companies, large and small, to invest and reap the benefits. Maximum from Thailand + 1 strategy and Vietnam + 1 strategy.
As for tourism, in the first quarter of 2019, Cambodia welcomed more than 60,000 Japanese tourists, an increase of about 2% compared to the same period in 2018. The number of Cambodians coming to Japan has also increased significantly, according to information we received from the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, compared to 2017 in 2018, the increase in visas to The population of Cambodia has increased by about 34%.
Of course, Cambodia is a country with the highest potential and highest economic growth in Southeast Asia, but Cambodia also faces a number of challenges that require action and the participation of all stakeholders.
In the goal of transforming Cambodia into an important part of the regional and global supply chain, as well as strengthening competitiveness and improving the business and investment environment in Cambodia, on March 29, 2019, I recently Led the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum, which provided an opportunity for the private sector to raise challenges and suggestions for the Royal Government to review and take appropriate measures to address.
The Royal Government-Private Sector Forum is considered a Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers and all decisions in this forum are considered as decisions of the Council of Ministers. As a result, the Royal Government has introduced a number of sharp new measures that contribute to reducing the total business costs of investors by about 400 million US dollars per year to contribute to improving the business and investment environment.
In addition to the above-mentioned joint mechanism, in order to solve the problem for investors in Cambodia, our two countries have signed an agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and Japan on the liberalization, promotion and protection of investment, which established a joint committee meeting mechanism. Cambodia-Japan, and so far 17 regular meetings have been held.
At the same time, Cambodia and Japan are in the process of negotiating an agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax. I hope that our two countries will be able to complete the negotiation of this agreement soon. These agreements and memoranda of understanding will make a significant contribution to strengthening and attracting investment as well as supporting Japanese investment activities in Cambodia.
It is noteworthy that the business activities and investments of Japanese companies in Cambodia are all quality investments, high value-added and provide a better working and living environment for the nieces and nephews of Cambodian workers, which is in line with the vision of the Royal Government. To provide decent employment opportunities, maintain economic growth and diversify Cambodia's industrial base.
On this occasion, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to welcome all the wise decisions of all foreign investors, especially Japanese investors who have selected and intend to select Cambodia as a potential investment destination to start or expand their business. Body.
I would like to appeal to Japanese businessmen and investors who have visited Cambodia and businessmen and investors who have not yet come to Cambodia to learn more about the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia and decide to invest to maximize the benefits of Bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Japan.
Once again, on behalf of the Royal Government, I would like to assure all investors of a conducive environment, especially peace, security and political stability, as well as macroeconomic stability, an effective legal and institutional framework, transparency, accountability and predictability. Yes. The Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to facilitate all administrative procedures and will accompany you at all stages of your investment operations in Cambodia.
