The Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense was established by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, through an announcement on April 30, 2019.
The chairman of the committee is General Chay Saing Yun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, accompanied by the two Vice-Chairmen, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Joint Chiefs of Staff, and General Chhum Socheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry. National Defense and consists of a total of 9 people.
According to General Chhum Socheat, the duties and responsibilities of the Anti-Drug Committee are as follows:
* To be the Secretary to the Minister of National Defense on anti-drug activities * To propose and request decision-making principles from the Minister of National Defense. * Assign education and dissemination of the Law on Drug Control and Use, Drug Trafficking and Combat in Units.
* Summarize the report to the Minister of National Defense on a monthly, quarterly and annual basis.
