Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Organizes the 12th National Road Safety Week for Traffic Accident Prevention
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration in cooperation with the leadership of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Sihanouk Province celebrated the 12th National Road Safety Week to educate and prevent traffic accidents.
The ceremony was held at the meeting hall of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Board of Governors, with the participation of government officials, the Armed Forces and students on May 28, 2019.
On that occasion, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that the celebration of the 12th National Road Safety Week aims to promote, prevent and reduce road traffic accidents to a low number.
He added that on behalf of the leadership of Sihanoukville and as the Provincial Road Safety Committee, we call on road users and road users to implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. "Today, tomorrow, do not have a traffic accident."
At this point, Mr. Yun Min asked the people to implement the following measures together:
1- Before driving, check the technical characteristics of the vehicle and promote high alertness.
2- All drivers must wear seat belts
3- Motorcyclists must wear helmets because helmets because "one helmet can save one life"
4- Reduce driving speed according to road conditions, traffic conditions, intersections, narrow roads or slippery roads.
5 - Before overtaking, be aware that the road ahead is free, safe, avoid overtaking at risk, causing accidents.
6- Drivers must respect the right of priority
9. There must be 10 points of driver ethics so that we can reduce traffic accidents in Sihanoukville, as well as throughout the country.
