Senior Communist Party of Vietnam official celebrates Cambodia's progress (Video inside) (Hanoi, Vietnam): Senior official of the Communist Party of Vietnam celebrates Cambodia's progress under the cold shadow of His Majesty the King. His Majesty Norodom Sihamoni and the leadership of the National Assembly of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and the Royal Government with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
Mr. Tran Quoc Vuong, Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam, praised Cambodia's progress during a meeting with National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin at the Communist Party of Vietnam in Hanoi.
Mr. Tran Quoc Vuong emphasized that the progress of Cambodia is the progress of Vietnam. The people of the Vietnamese State Party congratulate Cambodia on its progress. At the same time, he was pleased to see that the National Assembly of Cambodia and Vietnam have good relations and cooperation in bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
He emphasized that the good relations between the two parliaments were an important part of supporting the development of Cambodia and Vietnam.
On that occasion, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin shared his deepest condolences with the Party, State and people of Vietnam for the loss of one of its great leaders, Mr. Le Duc Anh, former President of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. .
Samdech emphasized that the loss of Mr. Le Duc Anh is the loss of a close friend of Cambodia, who made a great contribution to liberating the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, helping to rebuild and develop Cambodia.
Samdech mentioned that Samdech himself had a lot of memories with Mr. Le Duc Anh. The President of the National Assembly also prayed for the body of Mr. Le Duc Anh to be happy in the grave.
