(Koh Kong): The Department of Public Works and Transport of Koh Kong Province on May 28, 2019 organized the celebration of the "12th National Road Safety Week" in the presence of Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor. Mr. On Davuth, Director of the Provincial Public Works Department, as well as government officials of all institutions, teachers, students and the three armed forces.
Mr. On Davuth said that in order to implement the plan set by the National Road Safety Committee in 2018, May 28 is set every year to celebrate the 12th National Road Safety Week. "
In that, he showed many activities in the effort to promote the education of the road traffic law, such as:
* Organize a day to restrict the wearing of helmets * Disseminate information to the public about traffic safety * Inspect vehicles for technical defects, etc. * Distribute traffic law books and reflective masks and wear helmets * Explain He wears a helmet to protect his life * The driver must wear a seat belt regularly * Drive to respect traffic rules and understand each other * Do not drink alcohol.
The deputy governor said that before starting to drive a vehicle, drivers must automatically become accustomed to inspecting the technical characteristics of vehicles and constantly raising awareness of possible accidents on the road.
Mr. Sok Sothy said that all drivers and passengers should wear seat belts and all motorcyclists and passengers must wear helmets and drive to see the right road conditions. Understand each other, favor each other and respect the traffic law to reduce accidents.
