(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police has come out to reject the allegations that the department has released its subjects in exchange for thousands of dollars and that the officials who are inactive in these crimes must Remove the stand as ordered by General Mak Chito.
The director of the Anti-Drug Department, Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, told Fresh News on the afternoon of May 28, 2019 that allegations that the department released the perpetrators in exchange for thousands of dollars were likely to have been misrepresented. Because some scammers acted and ran for the release of drug addicts by using the name of the department to lie to the relatives of the perpetrators.
