Judge finally orders detention of mother-in-law and daughter-in-law stabbing son-in-law and husband in Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok
(Phnom Penh): Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Slina, on May 28, 2019, issued a temporary detention order for a mother-in-law and her daughter who stabbed their son-in-law to death. And her husband Kim Yot on May 24, 2019.
In connection with the murder, police said the mother and daughter killed their husband and son-in-law. Fear the victims hold their hands back. After the action was taken, they came to confess, so the two perpetrators (mother and daughter) were arrested by Sen Sok district police on May 25, 2019.
According to the police, the two murderers, Kong Thida, 49 years old (mother), living at 23J, Concrete Road, Group 76, Village 13, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Morn, and Ngoy Somary, 20 years old, were staying in a rented room at the scene. On the concrete road, Chong Thnal Khang Lech village, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok. The victim, Kim Yat, 29, an employee of a private company, died.
According to the confession of the two murderers in front of the authorities that this murder started from a dispute over money to the conspiracy to kill. According to the confession, the couple got married on January 26, 2019 and came to rent a house.
At that time, she shouted for her mother to come and help. Suddenly, the mother, Kim Thida, pulled out a machete and cut her son-in-law in the neck, causing him to fall. Fearing for his life, his wife, Ngoy Somary, tied his hands and feet with electric cords and scotch tape, and stabbed her to death with two knives.
