(Preah Vihear): In the morning of May 28, 2019, Preah Vihear Provincial Authority organized a lottery to distribute plots of land to 180 families to completely resolve the land dispute in Svay Chrum area in the Preah Vihear Temple Conservation Area.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear Constituency, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as leaders, civil servants, commanders and commanders of the three armed forces.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always taken care of the well-being and living of our people in order to improve the lives of our people. At the same time, Samdech addressed the land policy for people who lack land for real housing.
He said that today, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has provided residential land to the people to live better than those living on land in the restricted area, which affects the conservation area of the Temple of Preah Vihear.
At the same time, he also advised our people to have faith in the leadership at all levels of the authorities, not to believe in the incitement of some unscrupulous people.
Mr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear constituency, urged our brothers and sisters who received the land today to hurry up and cut down and build houses for everyone. He also urged the relevant authorities and experts to issue a proper title deed for him to use as needed.
Mr. Sous Yara also donated 30 million Riels to build a water station for the people in this area to use and also donated 5 tons of rice donated by the Cambodian Red Cross.
According to Mr. Sam Saroeun, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Preah Vihear Province, the land allotted to the people at this time is 25 meters by 50 meters. The procedure for handing over land to the people is to draw lots, respectively.
