(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yim Nol Sorn, Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council and Chairman of the Executive Committee on Legal Regulations on May 28, 2019, stated that the implementation of the assessment method on the impact of legal documents. (RIA approach) will make a significant contribution to the government's deepening reforms.
He added that the RIA method is a tool that in the preparation of legal documents will help to minimize the negative social and economic impact, reduce government spending on implementation and business operation costs, reduce Bureaucracy and scope overlap and can offer less costly options.
He added that the RIA approach will also increase transparency, accountability and trust from the public and businesses in the approved legal documents.
"In Cambodia, the implementation of the RIA will significantly contribute to the deepening reform of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to maintain strong economic growth and promote better socio-economic development," he said. "It is clearly stated in the Rectangular Strategy and the National Strategic Development Plan to achieve the goals of 2030 and 2050."
Please be informed that since 2011, the implementation of RIA pilot in Cambodia has achieved positive results step by step, therefore, on December 26, 2016, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issued Decision No. 132-Pillar to establish RIA working groups in all ministries and institutions to implement this RIA method in drafting legal documents.
