(Phnom Penh): Police forces from the 2nd Chao Chao Post of the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate raided an active trafficker along with 44 packs of ice cubes.
The above operation took place on May 28, 2019 at the point of concrete road, Thmor Koul 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, under the direct command of Mr. Yim Saran, Police Inspector of Por Senchey District.
Mr. San Pet, Chief of Choam Chao II Police Station, said that the suspect, Nhim Vannet, 23 years old, was born in Phneat Village, Sangkat Steung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, living in a rented room in Thmor Koul I Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Sanpet said that prior to the arrest of the suspect, while the suspect was actively trading under a mango tree, his forces immediately launched an operation to arrest the suspect. A search of the suspect's body turned up 44 packages of ice cubes.
Currently, the 2nd Chaom Chao Post Special Forces are interrogating and building a case to be forwarded to the Drug Division of the Por Sen Chey District Inspectorate for legal action.
