(Phnom Penh): Heng Sour, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that from 2050 onwards, Cambodia may face a challenge: the growth of the elderly population more than the younger workforce, but He added that despite these challenges, Cambodia must turn into opportunities for development.
In a national high-level dialogue on the future of employment for Cambodia held at the Raffles Royal Hotel on May 27, 2019, Mr. Heng Sour said that Cambodia today, despite being a country rich in young workers, There will be a slowdown in population growth, and from 2050 onwards there will be an increase in the elderly population, as in other developed countries.
He said that today, despite the large number of young workers, productivity is still limited and the birth rate is declining, so these are challenges that require the Cambodian workforce to work harder and be more productive. More can only increase the income to support life as they get older.
