The loan size in Cambodia is 23.03 trillion riels and will provide loans to 2.16 million people by the end of January 2019.
(Pursat): As of the end of January 2019, Cambodia had a loan size of 23.03 trillion riels (US $ 5.75 billion) and provided loans to 2.16 million customers nationwide. This is according to Mr. Kith Sovannarith, Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
This statement was made by the Deputy Director General of Supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia at a seminar on "Microfinance Sector in Cambodia" held in Bakan District, Pursat Province, with the participation of experts from the Inspection Department of the National Bank of Cambodia. Of Cambodia on May 27, 2019.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith said that along with the growth of loans, the size of deposits has also received interest and increase from the public sent to rural credit institutions and a network of about 275 operations across the country with branches up to That commune base.
"This progress reflects the past efforts and achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the direct supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia," he said. "
Mr. Kith Sovannarith added that today's workshop is to explain to the people in Bakan district, Pursat province to understand the use of loans to avoid cheating criminals and get out of debt.
He added that this is also to disseminate, share and explain to stakeholders such as authorities and citizens about the use of loans in Bakan district to better understand the procedures and some things to avoid.
He stressed that the main issues raised and discussed are: Legal issues and related regulations - services of licensed banking and financial institutions, challenges of the microfinance sector in Cambodia, etc. .
He added that in order to avoid debts on loans, authorities at all levels must promote and educate people to understand the rules of borrowing, the use of loans for the purpose and the obligation to repay. Extensive to the people.
