Labor Minister: Technological developments in the Fourth Industrial Revolution will create new types of jobs that young Cambodians must keep up with.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the technological development of the Fourth Industrial Revolution will create new types of jobs and will also cause the loss of youth jobs if they do not get them. Skills training and capacity building in line with market demand.
This statement was made by Mr. Ith Sam Heng at the opening ceremony of the National High-Level Dialogue on the Future of Jobs for Cambodia at the Raffles Royal Hotel on May 27, 2019.
The main purpose of organizing this dialogue is to provide a platform for initiating dialogue between policy makers, workers 'representatives, employers' representatives and development partners to better prepare Cambodia to respond to the emerging work world. Change.
The minister said that a 2016 ILO study on the future of jobs at risk of autonomy showed that 56% of the total jobs in five ASEAN countries would be at high risk of automation in two years. In the next decade, Cambodia will have 57%, Indonesia 56%, the Philippines 49%, Thailand 44% and Vietnam 70%.
According to the World Economic Forum report on job prospects for 2018, so far the advancement of this technology has not led to a general reduction in employment. While this change has had a negative impact on some sectors, it has also created many new jobs directly and indirectly in various sectors and occupations.
In fact, Cambodia is facing a mismatch of skills and an inadequate supply of skills due to the limited education and training system and the inability to respond to the rapidly changing workforce needs.
Moreover, technological advances during the Fourth Industrial Revolution will lead to job losses and the creation of new types of jobs. But those who lose their jobs at this stage of development will not be able to find a job if they do not receive skills training and skills development.
At this point, the Royal Government has specifically focused on the following priorities:
* Human resource development includes: strengthening the quality of education, science and technology, training of technical skills, promotion of public health and nutrition services, and strengthening of gender equality and social protection.
* Economic diversification includes: improving the logistics system, improving energy and digital transport connectivity, developing key and new sources of economic growth, preparing for the digital economy and responding to the Fourth Industrial Revolution, and boosting Financial and banking sector development.
* Private sector and employment development includes: labor market development, promotion of small and medium enterprises and entrepreneurship, organization and implementation of public-private partnerships, and strengthening competition. 3-Star General Run Rath Veasna Holds a Training Course on First Aid and Procedures for the Tourist Police Force
