The 75th Annual Meeting of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UN-ESCAP) will be held under the theme "Empowering People and Ensuring Environment and Equality". From 27 to 31 May 2019.
The annual conference is scheduled to be attended by Queen Sirindhorn, and will be attended by the President, Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Ministers and Senior Officials of officials from 53 member states and nine observer states. Asia-Pacific represents key UN agencies, international organizations, development partners, international financial institutions, NGOs, civil society and the private sector.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen was invited to deliver a keynote address at the opening ceremony of the conference, focusing on sharing Cambodia's experience in economic and social development, which has improved the living standards of the Cambodian people. The invitation for Samdech Techo Hun Sen to deliver a speech to share this experience is due to the fact that UN-ESCAP recognizes Cambodia's great achievements in the economic and social development of Cambodia.
Mr. Ly Thuch, Chairman of the ESCAP National Committee, a representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia, will also be chairing the meeting on the morning of May 28. A number of senior Cambodian officials will also be invited to address a number of sectoral discussions at this annual conference.
Cambodia has also benefited greatly from cooperation with UN-ESCAP. Those benefits include:
1. Access to macroeconomic policy formulation, poverty reduction and sectoral development.
2. Obtain technical numbers through various training workshops to determine data for environmental, economic and social situation analysis and capacity building of the National Statistics Office.
3. Facilitate trade and investment.
5. Receive support for integration, environmental sustainability and sustainable development.
6. Access to information technology policies that serve a range of areas, including: disaster reduction, support for the Industrial Revolution 4.0, women's and entrepreneurial development, and protection of the elderly and the sick.
7. Receive support for social development, such as gender mainstreaming in development, the suppression of human trafficking, HIV / AIDS, the promotion of the rights and welfare of people with disabilities, and the promotion of education for all.
