President of the Khmer One Party visits a crippled girl in Dang Tong district
8-year-old Sar Srey To is studying in the second grade at Trapeang Romeas Primary School in Damnak Sokrom commune, Dang Tong district. She has a father named Vorn Soth and a mother named Ian Ty with two siblings.
Srey To, the eldest daughter, has been crippled since birth. Although her parents sent her to several hospitals, including Kantha Bopha Hospital in Phnom Penh, her leg was still incurable.
She can walk on crutches. Recently, there was a post on Facebook calling for help for those who need materials for her studies.
During the visit, Srey To, Mr. Kem Rithisith, President of the Khmer Rouge Party, brought some materials including noodles, books, pens and some money to give to the disabled girl to encourage her to work hard. Keep learning.
Mr. Kem Rithisith also encouraged the disabled girl not to despair in life. Mr. Rithisith explained to the girl that even though we are crippled, our mind and brain are not crippled, so we must work hard to study hard to have a bright future in the future.
