The 2019 Third Mandate Council Election officially begins today, 7 am to 3 pm
(Phnom Penh): As planned, 203 polling stations across the country opened this morning, Sunday, May 26, 2019 to serve the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council elections. Council of the third mandate 2019. The voting process starts at 7:00 am and ends at 3:00 pm on the same day.
Mr. Nuth Sokhom, Vice Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC) and Representative of the Chairman of the NEC, inspected the election process at Polling Station 0013, Preah Yukunthor High School, Monivong Blvd., Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang II, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
According to the announcement from the NEC, at 4 pm on May 26, 2019, the NEC will summarize the general events of the 2019 Third Mandate Council Election at the Press Conference Hall. The first of the NEC office in Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Please note that the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council Election is a different election from the National Assembly Election and the Commune / Sangkat Council Election which is global in nature. Separately, council elections are held by secret ballot and by secret ballot. Council elections are held on Sundays every five years (the exact date is set by the Prime Minister at the request of the Minister of Interior).
The distribution of seats is proportional to the distribution of seats according to the highest average formula based on the number of seats and the results of the constituency elections. Council elections begin at 7:00 a.m. until 3:00 p.m.
Separately, those who have the right to vote are all Commune / Sangkat Councilors in office and whose names are on the voter list.
According to the NEC, the third mandate council election was also attended by 19 non-governmental organizations (NGOs) with up to 1,010 members.
