Lightning strikes, killing 3 people, parents and children at the cassava plantation in Sandan district, Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): In the geographical area of Kran Dek, a plantation area more than 2 kilometers away from the village, there were 3 deaths, parents and children due to a natural disaster by lightning. This incident happened on May 23, 2019 in Choam Phka village, Chheu Teal commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province.
According to the authorities, Ms. Bin Mai, the brother-in-law of Koylen's body, described that on May 23, 2019, at 7 o'clock, her brother-in-law, Koylen, his wife and children went to plant. Potatoes are finished at the Kran Dek plantation where the incident took place. When evening came, they did not return home.
According to Bin Mai, she assumed they were staying at the plantation. Until May 25, 2019, still not seeing them go home, Ms. Bin Mai went to look at the plantation.
She said that when she arrived at the plantation, she immediately saw the three of them lying dead under a mango tree in the field. She was so frightened that she returned home to tell her relatives about the news and reported it to the village authorities.
According to the authorities, in the case of death, the three bodies smelled rotten and concluded that it was caused by lightning. After the inspection, the authorities handed over the body to the family for the traditional ceremony.
