This morning, the King of Cambodia returns to Cambodia after celebrating the 25th anniversary of the ICC-Angkor International Committee in France.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 26, 2019, at 10:00 AM, His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, returned home after participating in the celebration. 25th Anniversary of the International Coordinating Committee for the Protection and Conservation of Angkor (ICC-Angkor) in France
It should be noted that the International Coordinating Committee (ICC-Angkor) was established on December 21-22, 1993 with the aim of preserving and developing Angkor after the temple, a valuable heritage of this Khmer ancestor, was included as UNESCO World Heritage Site at a meeting in Santa Fe, United States of America on December 14, 1992.
This committee was first formed only 10 years ago. But seeing the important role of this committee in the conservation and development of Angkor, it has been extended twice for another 10 years. One of the two renewals was made at a meeting in Paris on November 14-15, 2003, and another at an intergovernmental meeting in Cambodia on December 5, 2003. 2013.
ICC-Angkor is co-chaired by France and Japan, the Permanent Secretariat of Science is headed by the UNESCO Representative Office in the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Apsara Authority represents the Royal Government of Cambodia.
* Celebrate the success of the ICC Angkor mechanism, which is now a model of conservation and development for countries around the world.
* Show the national pride of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is a cultural power and has a long history, as well as the value of heritage
Express gratitude and appreciation to heroes, dignitaries and ancestors of all generations who have dedicated their bodies and minds to building, preserving, protecting and preserving cultural heritage.
* To cultivate the spirit of young people and the Cambodian people to love, participate in preserving, protecting and promoting Cambodia's rich cultural and traditional heritage.
* Presenting the achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of heritage under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia
* Promote cultural and tourism potential to the international arena.
