Cambodia is a country that has been completely destroyed in all areas due to more than three decades of war, especially in the genocide of Pol Pot. Since the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, under the leadership of the leaders and political figures from the Cambodian People's Party, Cambodia has been rescued from the devastation in the most difficult steps.
Cambodia has gone from being a poor and destitute country to a low middle income country in 2015 and is striving to achieve its ambition to become a high middle income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050. . The poverty rate in Cambodia continued to decline steadily from over 53 percent in 2004 to 13.5 percent in 2014 and is currently estimated at around 10 percent.
At the United Nations Conference on Economic and Social Development in the Asia-Pacific Region in Thailand, Samdech Techo Hun Sen is expected to share his experiences in ending the fires of war in Cambodia and maintaining Achieve peace to be the main capital for building and developing Cambodian society. Samdech Techo Hun Sen addresses the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly in September 2018.
