According to the inspector, prior to the incident, the suspect, Ngoy Somary, and the victim were married on January 26, 2019. The suspect, Ngoy Somary, talked to the victim and went to get married. He said that he waited for 2 years to register his marriage with jealousy of the victim and often had conflicts with each other.
On the evening of May 23, 2019, the suspect, Ngoy Somary, took his mother (suspect Kong Thida) from Tonle Bassac commune, Daun Penh district to stay with him to help look after the victim. Until May 24, 2019, the suspect named Ngoy Somary asked the victim for 10,000 Riel and the victim refused to have a dispute with each other.
The victim then strangled the suspect, Ngoy Somary, and the suspect, Ngoy Somary, shouted for his mother (suspect Kim Thida) to help, and the suspect, Kim Thida, used a machete to cut the victim's neck. To death, the suspect, Ngoy Somary, tied the victim's arms and legs with scotch tape and stabbed the victim with a sharp knife, causing his death on the spot.
