JICA and Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Agree to Sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Strategic Partnership
(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port have discussed a Memorandum of Understanding on Strategic Partnership to Strengthen and Expand Partnership for the Development of the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port. This is according to the announcement of JICA.
1: JICA will continue to support the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port in the development of the port and the capacity building of the Sihanoukville Port Special Economic Zone through the provision of grants, technical cooperation and financial loans.
2: Sihanoukville Autonomous Port will continue to strengthen the operation and management of ports and special economic zones.
3. JICA and Sihanoukville Autonomous Port will continue to exchange views and information related to port development and logistics development for the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
Sihanoukville Autonomous Port is the only international deep-sea port in Cambodia located in Sihanoukville, the southern economic corridor between Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville.
Coastal areas are gradually being developed and become industrial zones, which has brought many positive effects for the industrial and economic development of Cambodia. To boost this development, JICA provided official development funding for the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Emergency Rehabilitation Project in 1999 and the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Emergency Expansion Project in 2004, with the aim of improving the transit of goods through the port.
JICA also participated in the acquisition of shares of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, which went public in June 2017.
