Director General of Rural Development Bank urges safe vegetable buyers to implement agricultural contracts with farmers
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 24, 2019, the Rural Development Bank held a meeting with a company to buy safe vegetables and invited Japanese experts in the field of agriculture to present and share experiences on safe vegetable production lines in Japan. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank and was attended by representatives of more than 10 safe vegetable purchasing companies in Phnom Penh.
After listening to the presentation and sharing of experiences from Japanese agricultural experts, Mr. Kao Thach informed the meeting that as a bank implementing the policy of the Royal Government and on his own behalf, he wanted to see farmers or communities. Growing safe vegetables in Cambodia can supply safe, chemical-free vegetables to the market in a sustainable way, high quality vegetables by following the standards and high technology in cultivation.
Therefore, in the project to promote safe vegetable cultivation in Cambodia, which is one of the various projects of the Rural Development Bank (with the permission of the management) has prepared a team of experts in agricultural technology and credit budget at interest rates. Most favorable to provide farmers or farming communities growing safe vegetables in Cambodia. In addition, companies that purchase safe vegetables from farmers or farming communities can also borrow from the project.
