The National Anti-Drug Authority will continue to distribute 50,000 leaflets to all relevant authorities for distribution to local people.
(Phnom Penh): 50,000 leaflets obtained by the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs from LOLC will be distributed to the relevant ministries, institutions, units and relevant authorities to be distributed to the people in Basically.
The handing over of the leaflets took place on May 24, 2019 between Mr. Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legal Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Sok Voeun, Chief Executive Officer of LOLC.
These 50,000 leaflets highlight the slogan "Let's solve the drug problem together", which is a slogan to educate people to join the fight against drugs. Drug use adversely affects the physical and mental health and causes serious problems for the family and society.
Mr. Sok Voeun said that the provision of information leaflets on drug issues now is to participate in social work with the Royal Government and the National Authority for Combating Drugs. He added that he encouraged all stakeholders and the people to work together to help solve the drug problem and eliminate the drug problem in Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Lim Tong Huot said that in relation to these 50,000 leaflets, the General Secretariat will continue to distribute to ministries, institutions, units that are members of the authorities and the Capital-Provincial Drug Control Commission to be used for dissemination. At public forums in order to make people and participants aware of the drug problem.
For the distribution of leaflets on drug issues, the authorities will continue to distribute more at the request of all relevant ministries, institutions and units to be disseminated for the common good of the nation. At the same time, he added that the fight against drugs is complex, which requires multi-sectoral cooperation with the National Authority for Combating Drugs, as the LOLC has been working with.
Mr. Lim Tong Huot thanked the management of LOLC Microfinance Institution for always assisting the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs in the fight against drug education.
Please note that this is the fifth time that LOLC has handed over to the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs a leaflet on drug issues, which reflects the LOLC's commitment to continue to participate in the elimination of drugs. Addiction in Cambodia. The LOLC fully supports existing national and sub-national mechanisms to contribute to the fight against drugs.
