Brigadier General Tith Bonna, a professional officer of the Ministry of Interior, who testified in court, stated that during the investigation at the scene, the point of the inverted tie was hanging and the size of the steel rod and two screws could not support the weight of the person when dropped. It can come down. There were no scars on the windowsill to be hung, while on the surface of the body there were small blood clots indicating suffocation, indicating that he had died of suffocation.
