Health officials call on people to keep the environment clean and eliminate tiger mosquito breeding grounds to prevent dengue fever
(Koh Kong): To reduce the rate of increase in the number of dengue patients at the local level, which caused some patients to die on May 24, 2019, Dr. Mak Kimly, Vice President. Koh Kong Provincial Health Department calls on all citizens and stakeholders to take care of the environment, including the elimination of tiger mosquito breeding grounds to prevent dengue fever at the local level more effectively.
Dr. Mak Kimly told Fresh News that the rate of dengue fever in Koh Kong province has risen steadily, which is also worrying local people throughout the province. Most cases of dengue fever occur in children due to mosquito bites that cause dengue fever, which is caused by people not paying attention to children and lacking environmental hygiene.
For the dissemination of the above education, the provincial health department has educated and sprayed tiger mosquito repellent in many villages, and the health department continues to implement in accordance with the Ministry of Health's certification to get rid of tiger mosquitoes at the local level.
