(Phnom Penh): Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon has requested the Ambassador of the Republic of Belarus to Cambodia to encourage Belarusian machinery companies to consider the possibility of considering machinery for cassava harvesting. Reduce labor shortages in the harvest.
During the meeting, Minister Veng Sakhon stated that the cooperation between the two countries (Cambodia-Belarus) is mostly focused on agricultural machinery, in the future he hopes that this cooperation will be further strengthened and expanded. Especially on investing in processing, packaging and exporting Cambodian agricultural products to the EU market.
As the Republic of Belarus specializes in agricultural machinery, through the Ambassador, the Minister requested the machinery manufacturers to review and consider the production of machinery for cassava harvesting to help reduce labor shortages. . Most cassava production uses human labor, wasting time, higher labor costs, and especially in line with the Ministry of Agriculture's agricultural modernization policy.
In response, the Ambassador agreed with the Minister's request, stating that cooperation between the two countries would be strengthened and expanded soon through a meeting between the private sector and the state. This coming July in Siem Reap.
