Dr. Kun Nhim emphasized the purpose of the meeting was to push for more in-depth discussions, both policy and technical, to ensure that the revision of the list of prohibited and restricted items can be carried out effectively. And can reduce the number of items on the list as well as eliminate the overlap of institutions in accordance with the policy of deep reform of the Royal Government.
After the presentation on the method of inspecting and updating the items that are prohibited or restricted on exports and imports, the representatives of each ministry and institution presented the relevant legal documents, work progress and the results of the inspection and revision as Introduce the items under their respective responsibilities and highlight the shortcomings and challenges that need to be addressed in order to complete the inventory.
Based on the results of the discussions in order to be able to complete the work on time by the Royal Government, the meeting agreed to set out the work in the following steps:
