(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, on May 24, 2019, held a meeting to disseminate the Inter-Ministerial Proclamation and Instruction on the Implementation of the Cash Support Program for Pregnant Women and Children Under 2 Years of Age. The family has an equity card or priority card.
Minister Mam Bunheng stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to provide cash to poor women, pregnant women and children under 2 years old. Separately, poor women come for prenatal check-ups 4 times, get 40,000 riels, at the time of delivery receive 200,000 riels, postpartum check-ups and care for children 10 times, for 1,000 days.
