Along with posting this picture, the United Nations also wrote a short article thanking and admiring the dedication of Cambodia's Blue Hat forces to participate in peacekeeping missions around the world.
The United Nations writes: "Courageous women and men from Cambodia are willing to leave their families to pursue peacekeeping missions with the United Nations around the world. We really thank them for their work and dedication. ”
Please note that the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to send troops to participate in world peacekeeping missions under the UN flag in 2006.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who decided on this work, once stated that the decision to send troops to join the peacekeeping mission with the United Nations is the most difficult decision because it faces high responsibility. Most with the nation and the families of the forces, if these forces are in danger or life-threatening.
The report shows that since 2006, Cambodia has sent 6,053 Blue Hat troops to 285 countries, including 285 women, to conduct peacekeeping missions in various countries. Countries where Cambodian forces have participated in the mission include the Republic of South Sudan, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria, Chad, Mali and Central Africa. Currently, 797 Cambodian troops, 54 of them women, are deployed in these countries.
Cambodia has become the largest contributor to ASEAN, with peacekeepers on missions in other countries. Cambodia has also been ranked 29th by the United Nations in the 17th category of men and women out of 122 countries that have deployed troops to UN peacekeeping missions.
Cambodian forces also suffered casualties from disease and attacks during the mission. However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always announced the strong and unyielding position of the Royal Government of Cambodia in participating in missions with the United Nations to maintain peace in war-torn countries.
As a leader in a country plagued by the crisis of war and with the help of the United Nations, Samdech Techo Hun Sen not only expressed his commitment to strengthen his position in this mission, but also announced his commitment to participate in the mission. This makes it more active and energetic.
