He informed that the company is preparing to cultivate this type of rice on 300 hectares in Kampong Thom province and hopes to get more than 6.5 tons per hectare. Meanwhile, the company has signed a contract with farmers to try to grow and collect at a price of 1,000 riel per kilogram of rice sold to Vietnam.
Mr. Veng Sakhon praised the achievements of the company because it has made farmers' rice market more open and maintain the price.
He added that in terms of experimentation and seed production, in order to ensure quantity, supply, quality and meet market demand, especially in line with the rice production development strategy, the private sector should be used as a production partner with the state.
