After receiving the current confession, the suspect and the exhibits were sent to the Takeo Provincial Police Commission by the Tram Kak District Police Inspectorate to be sent to the court for legal proceedings. Discover another strange phenomenon that could cause Mars to run out of water!
The presence of water vapor at high altitudes above Mars is surprising because Mars has a central layer of its atmosphere that should prevent this water cycle from occurring. Scientists say that the middle layer of Mars' atmosphere has extremely cold temperatures, which is not conducive to water vapor. So why can water pass through the middle layer?
When this happens, every two years on Earth, a gate will open in the middle layer of Mars' atmosphere at an altitude of between 60 and 90 kilometers, allowing water vapor to pass through. The upper layer of the atmosphere.
In addition, Mars is different from Earth in that it suffers from frequent dust storms. The storms prevented the sun from penetrating the surface of Mars, instead allowing light to reach its atmosphere and warming the atmosphere, creating favorable conditions for water vapor to pass through the middle layer. Of the Mars atmosphere.
Researchers have confirmed that when the water vapor passes through the middle layer of the atmosphere, two things will happen. The first is that some of the water vapor will drift to the north and south poles of Mars, but the sun's ultraviolet (UV) rays in the upper atmosphere can also separate oxygen and hydrogen in the molecules of both water vapor. That, too, causes hydrogen to drift into space, leaving only oxygen.
