(Phnom Penh): Life as a female singer really has to go through a bitter life full of scandals and jealousy from some hungry men. In fact, 19-year-old Prak Phanny, due to poverty, started a career as a singer in concerts in the provinces and cities, just to earn a little money to support her elderly parents and two siblings living in The burden is learned.
But her life was followed by her boss for more than a year, but she refused because she already knew that he already had a wife and two children, making the boss jealous and even violent. Also.
Unable to withstand the violence, Ms. Panny decided to file a complaint to the Dangkor District Military Command to help resolve the matter and deal with her boss, who was the perpetrator.
19-year-old Prak Phanny, also known as Amara, a concert singer and sports TV presenter, said she could not accept the 38-year-old Hong Zhen. In Borey Lay Kong, Moo Village, Sangkat-Khan Dangkor, the boss set up a concert music stage, which harassed her for not living comfortably and not for her to work as a singer just to earn money to support her family.
After the violence, she filed a complaint with the local authorities for help, but then Hong Zhen's wife raised her hand and begged her to withdraw the complaint, because if her husband was in prison, no one would help raise the child. No, and because she was soft-hearted and passionate about Hong Zhen's wife, she agreed to withdraw the complaint without receiving a penny in compensation.
Until the night of May 16, 2019, recently, the boss was still not tired of harassing her again while she was performing in an art show in Phum Prakar, Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, while she was singing and walking down. Coming backstage, suddenly the boss chased her and surprised her, making her feel embarrassed in front of the crowd.
At that time, if no one intervened yet, it is clear that she was seriously injured or may have lost her life. This is the fourth time that Hong Zen has used violence against her, and this time she no longer has any favors, so she decided to file a complaint with the Dangkor District Gendarmerie Command to seek justice on May 17, 2019. So far, she demanded $ 30,000 in compensation for her mental illness.
This harassment made her very scared of Mr. Hong Zen, even though she was hired to perform at a concert at the Plaza Kien Svay Entertainment Center from May 20-26, 2019, she did not dare to go out to perform. .
Regarding Ms. Prak Phanny's statement above, Fresh News Agency could not ask for an explanation from Mr. Hong Xen without a phone number. Separately, Sar Sophoan, Commander of the Dangkor District Gendarmerie, told reporters that he had indeed received a complaint from Ms. Prak Phanny, but could not find a solution between the two parties, so he sent the case to Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command to deal with already.
