(Kampong Speu): A fire broke out at a black oil processing handicraft factory in Damnak Trach village, Dambok Rong commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province on the afternoon of May 21, 2019 due to a power outage.
Kampong Speu Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sam Samoun said this morning, May 22, that the black oil processing handicraft is owned by Thorn Sengly, a 30-year-old male resident of Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
According to the General Commissioner, the accident destroyed one fuel truck, seven refineries, six fuel tanks, 24 plastic tanks and 67,000 liters of refined diesel. For the rescue operation, the police used 4 fire trucks, 1 inspection vehicle, 2 vehicles of Kampong Speu Provincial Police, 1 vehicle of Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship School, 05 vehicles using water and 25 people.
However, this social disaster did not spread to people's homes or cause any harm to anyone.
According to the General Commissioner of the diesel refinery, in the past, the authorities have already closed the business due to unauthorized operation, but it is likely that the fire was started quietly.
Koh Peam Reang, Peam Chor District, Becomes an Important Area for Supply of Organic Vegetables to the Market, Gaining Knowledge from a Professional Unit
(Prey Veng): Koh Peam Reang, Koh Chek commune, Peam Chor district, Prey Veng province, is not well known, but recently the provincial authorities of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries have targeted this area to become an organic vegetable export area. The period of training on how to grow successfully has greatly improved the livelihood of the people in this area.
The farmer said that before worrying about the hot weather, the crop was not successful through the technology, if the heat had to cover the irrigation water to turn the water like rain, using natural fertilizers with the help of the Provincial Department of Agriculture. Making water bags, automatic pumping water up and down to irrigate the crops, it shows that the nearest authorities and officials are helping, and the market is close, that is the main motivation for growing these vegetables.
Farmers continue to say that before they got the technique, it was almost impossible to eat, but now it is different from before, and this vegetable is guaranteed to be pure, non-toxic, organic, as this vegetable has a higher market price than vegetables using chemical fertilizers. Poisons imported from neighboring countries.
Farmers said that Koh Peam Reang now has 1 to 2 tons of vegetables exported to the market every day, there are more than 10 kinds, and in the next year may be more than double, apart from the provincial Department of Agriculture to provide water bags, there are many NGOs Down to the project to help more water bags to expand the area for growing vegetables, vegetables, cabbage sold 1 kg 2,000 Riel and 1 kg 1,300 Riel or more.
Regarding the cultivation of vegetables, Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Prey Veng Province, said that this is the first time in the whole country that the state budget has been requested to irrigate vegetables for farmers and with farmers and technicians. Help teach them to promote the island as an important area for exporting vegetables to the market.
He said that if this becomes a vegetable export area, an ecotourism area, vegetables, fish, meat, guests come to taste grilled chicken, grilled fish, enjoy fresh vegetables, see the nature of the river here, with success on vegetable crops. .
