(Phnom Penh): The Board of Study, Marketing and Promotion of Tourism in Cambodia (CPPCC) has agreed to submit a number of solutions related to tourism to the Royal Government to determine strategies to attract more tourists to Cambodia, especially tourism destinations. Important of Cambodia.
The agreement was reached after a half-day discussion meeting at the Ministry of Tourism on May 21, 2019, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Tourism Marketing and Promotion Committee. Cambodia.
In the above meeting, the meeting of the Board of Study, Marketing and Tourism Promotion of Cambodia mentioned the quarterly report and the draft internal regulations, the statute, the structure of the council and the structure of the secretariat of the CPPCC.
At the same time, the President and members of the CPPCC raised some practical issues that occur in the current tourism sector in Cambodia, including:
* Visa of International Tourists: Minister Thong Khon expressed his desire for a visa waiver for international tourists.
* Promoting Cambodia's tourism sector to foreign tourism markets, especially to prepare for the ASEAN Tourism Forum in 2021 and other major tourism events such as CTM 2019 to receive 2,000 Chinese tourists in the future.
* Connecting flights to transport tourists from cruise ships in Sihanoukville to Siem Reap-Angkor, as no company is currently organizing this tour. He also pushed for flights for this type of tourist.
Expansion of flights from India to attract more Indian tourists and third-party tourists in India.
* Creating a lot of new tourism products in Siem Reap to meet the entertainment needs of tourists in addition to Angkor Wat and other important temples, in particular, he also expressed his desire to organize the Tonle Sap Lake and the Koulong mountain range to the product. New tourism for Cambodia as well.
* The problem of selling souvenirs and goods to tourists, while fraudulent sales of counterfeit goods and substandard goods to customers still exist.
* Infrastructure problems in Siem Reap and in some tourist areas have not been prepared for Sam Suon and cause inconvenience to tourists who want to visit Cambodia.
