The Royal Plowing Ceremony under the Presidency of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, was held on Wednesday morning, May 22, 2019. This is in the stadium of Daun Keo city, Takeo province. According to the royal tradition according to the Hindu religion, the royal ceremony is held continuously according to the reading.
According to the Royal Tradition, before the beginning of the Royal Ceremony, the Acharya prayed to the deities to take care of Cambodia and the sacred objects in the world to bless the Buddha, the Great Blessing to the King of Cambodia and the Queen Mother. The Khmer people and the Khmer people, as well as ask for abundant rainfall on a regular basis from time to time and may the cultivation be good.
After the Acharya had finished praying, Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, whom the King had authorized to be the King of Heaven, began to plow the fields and sow rice by Mrs. Bonna Davy, wife of Mr. Ouch. Phea is elected as a leader for 3 rounds.
After plowing and sowing rice for three rounds, the Brahmin priest performed a blessing ceremony to heal the water on the oxen and remove the oxen to eat seven grains, including: rice, corn, beans, sesame, grass Wine and water already prepared.
Please note that the Royal Plowing Ceremony is an important royal civilization, considered as one of the great culture of the people of Cambodia, which all kings have always led since ancient times as a proclamation to the people of Cambodia. That the planting season has arrived.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Defense also warned the person who created the Facebook page to stop using the image of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and called on the authorities to investigate the Facebook user Gro Angel to take legal action.
