(Switzerland): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, addressed the Plenary Session of the 72nd General Assembly of the World Health Organization in Geneva, Switzerland on May 21, 2019. Mention the progress of the health sector in Cambodia as follows:
* The Kingdom of Cambodia has made remarkable progress in the fields of education, socio-economics, social stability, economic growth and poverty reduction under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Director. Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. All these developments have made a significant contribution to the well-being of the Cambodian people, especially in the last three decades.
* Development and growth of the public health system, especially the achievement of key health indicators such as improving and expanding public health coverage, improving the quality of health services, strengthening medical professional ethics, and expanding health care mechanisms. Society to avoid financial risks when accessing health care services among workers, both formal and informal, public officials, the disabled, the poor and vulnerable.
* The Royal Government of Cambodia cooperates with development partners to implement the Equity Fund project, which has been providing quality, effective and safe health care services to approximately 3 million disadvantaged people.
* Reaffirm the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to achieving universal health coverage by improving the quality coverage of health care services and eliminating financial barriers to accessing health care services.
On the occasion of attending the conference, Mr. Ny Sam Ol, Ambassador of Cambodia to the United Nations in Geneva, also joined the Minister of Health. He also met with key figures such as the Minister of Health of Laos, who has been appointed chair of the 72nd National Assembly, and the Minister of Health of Singapore, Director of the World Health Organization for the Western Pacific.
