At the same time, Dr. Kim Heang also presented some factors that make him a successful entrepreneur in the field of land and famous as today.
Dr. Kim Heang said that becoming a successful entrepreneur in the land sector like now is not easy, that is, have to persevere through all obstacles to be successful like now. He added that with this success, he always reminds himself of a slogan, "What I am not afraid of, what I fear is poverty."
"I used to go through a lot of pain because as a child I was rich, but when I was a teenager my family started to fall into poverty, then I know who we are, when we were rich, we had friends," he said. You are the only one who knows yourself when you are poor. ”
Dr. continued, "There is an encouraging proverb that says, 'Be rich, do not be poor, but for me, I am determined not to be poor, both in heart and in money.' "When I grew up and got involved in society, I noticed that society and people have these castes, which made me realize that I could not be poor."
He added, "In this life, what I fear most is fear, because I used to be poor, when I was poor, I know a lot of poor people, no one is happy to be born poor." Samdech Norodom Serey Vuth Receives an Medal from the Government of Japan for Contributing to the Improvement of Cambodia-Japan Relations
According to a press release from the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, the Council of Ministers of the Government of Japan has decided to present the medal to Samdech Norodom Serey Vuth on May 21, 2019.
The Embassy of Japan also stated that since 1993, when Samdech Norodom Sirivuth was appointed Deputy Prime Minister, he has contributed to the promotion of bilateral relations not only as Deputy Prime Minister but also as Supreme Personal Adviser to the King. The monarch is also the founder of the Khmer Institute for Cooperation and Peace.
It should be noted that every year, the Japanese government always gives this award to political figures or Cambodian people who have worked and contributed to improve the relationship between Cambodia and Japan. Dangkor District Governor Inspects Concrete Road Project in Choeung Ek Sangkat to Facilitate People's Travel
