(Battambang): A man, angry with his wife's family, wanted to separate his wife from him and was jealous, so he decided to use a knife to cut his wife to death immediately in the morning on May 21, 2019 at Group 1, Chamkar O village, Kantea 2 commune, Banan district, Battambang province.
Brigadier General Chet Vanny, Deputy Commissioner for Justice Planning, told Fresh News that after the incident, the police arrested the suspect's husband and immediately brought him to the Banan District Inspector for questioning and then sent him to the Provincial Police Commissioner's Office. To take legal action.
Brigadier General Chet Vanny confirmed that the assailants arrested by the police were 33-year-old Yoeut Roeut and the victim's wife, 37-year-old Man Sophea.
After questioning, the suspect confessed that in the past, his wife's family always tried to separate his wife and take her back to his wife's family home, and because he was jealous, he was afraid of losing his wife, so he could not control himself.
Currently, the authorities have sent the suspects to the specialized office of the provincial police commissioner for further questioning and to build a case to be sent to the provincial court for legal action.
(Kratie): Kratie City Police launched a drug busting operation by detaining 3 suspects and 23 packages of drugs on the night of May 20 and 21, 2019 in Sangkat Kratie, Kratie City.
According to a report from Kratie City Police, on the night of May 20, Kratie City Police patrolled and found and intercepted a suspect named Hul Seng. Aun, a 51-year-old male mechanic living in Krakor village, Krakor commune, was detained at a rice barn in Trapeang Pring village, Kratie commune, Kratie city, and a motorcycle and a package of drugs were confiscated.
According to the report, after questioning the suspects on May 21, Kratie City Police continued to detain two more suspects at the suspect's house in Trapeang Pring Village, Kratie Sangkat. Kratie. The first suspect: Wu Bunnarith, alias Touch, male, 26 years old, engaged in handicrafts, and the second suspect: Horn Srey Len, female, 21 years old, both husband and wife, living in the same commune.
Police confiscated 22 packages of white gram powder, 1 drug scale, 2 drug sharing tubes, drug sharing bags, some drug paraphernalia, 2 mobile phones, and 1 motorcycle. $ 220 in jewelry, 2,950,000 riel and some jewelry.
Currently, the three suspects and the object were detained and temporarily kept at the Kratie City Police Inspectorate to build a case according to the procedure.
