The secret journey of Samdech Techo and his colleagues to Thailand on September 19, 1989, due to the accident because the road was a minefield and there was a tripartite army to attack at all times.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen described his intention to go to Thailand at that time as the introduction of a policy of "decentralization of the armed forces and the Thai administration" aimed at preventing and reducing Thai aid to the Khmer Rouge and the tripartite. .
Not many people know this, even I just found a photo that a former Belgian journalist gave me this Sunday.
On September 19, 1989, the delegation and I traveled secretly to Thailand, crossing the railway bridge at Poipet, where both Cambodian and Thai roads were then mined. Moreover, on both sides of the road, about 1 km, there is a tripartite army waiting to attack the Cambodian state army standing on National Road 5.
What is such a secret mission? I set out a policy of "the liberalization of the armed forces and the Thai administration" aimed at preventing and reducing Thai aid to the Khmer Rouge and the tripartite, so that there was a secret meeting between me and His Excellency Chao Walit Yongchaiyuth. An influential Thai army chief on October 27, 1988 in Vientiane, Laos. It was through this meeting that my visit opened in Bangkok, January 1989.
I secretly traveled to Bangkok on September 19, 1989, when the connection between the war and the peace in Cambodia, which can be considered as part of the search for peace for Cambodia.
At around 2 pm, the delegation and I crossed the border to Aranyaprathet for lunch with the Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Thai Armed Forces and then by helicopter to Bangkok for secret talks with Thai Prime Minister Chatchai Chunhawan and Thai Army Chief Chao Walit Yong. Chhay Yuth on the evening of October 19, 1989. "My relationship with the Thai leader has improved, which has led to the success of my win-win politics in the future."
(Pursat): In the near future, Pursat province will have two other large irrigation systems, including Wat Chre irrigation system in Boeung Khnar commune, Bakan district, and Damnak Ampil irrigation system in Lolok Sor commune, Pursat city, which can irrigate the area. Thousands of hectares of land will be used for other purposes.
While the team is building, Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, on May 20, 2019, led the working group led by the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to inspect the construction site of Wat Chre Irrigation System and continued to visit. To check the modernization of the open-close water system of Damnak Ampil and the concrete canal of Damnak Ampil irrigation system.
Please be informed that the construction of Wat Chre Irrigation System under the loan of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) of $ 4.61 million will take 5 years (2016-2020) and so far the work has been completed. 69 percent. When completed, the project will be able to irrigate 1,979 hectares in the rainy season and 1,949 hectares in the dry season.
Separately, the project to modernize the open-close water system of Damnak Ampil and concrete canals of Damnak Ampil irrigation system was implemented under a Japanese concession loan of approximately $ 1.50 million for a period of 2 years (2018-2019) and Currently, 90% of the work has been completed.
